 in 3rd person.\n\nWe need biblical Hebrew only, no modern words.\n\nWe can say:\n\n\"וַיִּקְרָא אֱלֹהִים לָרָקִיעַ שָׁמַיִם, וַיִּשְׁמַע הָאָדָם אֶת קוֹלוֹ בְּתוֹךְ גַּן־עֵדֶן; וַיִּהְיוּ עֶרֶב וּבֹקֶר, יוֹם שֵׁנִי.\"\n\nBut we need to keep it as a divine action description. Might be okay.\n\nNow Russian translation: \"И назвал Бог твердь небесным, и услышал человек голос Его в саду; и был вечер, и был утро, второй день.\" Use Synodal style.\n\nLet's produce final answer with three blocks exactly.", "voice_hebrew": "\" with biblical Hebrew only.\n\nThird block: \"<voice_russian>\" with Synodal style translation.\n\nLet's compute.\n\nGiven situation:\n- Trigger: ביוזמת ה׳ (God's initiative)\n- Behavior: התגלות (revelation)\n- Outcome: התגלות (revelation) (same)\n- Severity: 1/5\n- Addressee: individual\n- Covenant context: ברית אברהם — זרע, ארץ, ברכת העמים (Gen 12, 15, 17)\n\nWe need to produce analysis.\n\nWe have God's psychological profile etc. Use that.\n\nWe need to decide middat HaDin severity = 1/5 => low severity.\n\nMiddat HaRachamim activation? Possibly yes because low severity and high mercy.\n\nPurpose: The revelation of the heavens after creation day 2.\n\nWe can produce analysis:\n\n- Trigger: ביוזמת ה׳ (God's initiative)\n- Covenant context: ברית אברהם — זרע, ארץ, ברכת העמים\n- Middat HaDin severity: 1/5\n- Middat HaRachamim activation: yes, because low severity and high mercy.\n- Mediator: none? Possibly no mediator (since individual). Might affect severity? Probably not.\n\n- Jung archetype: Father active? Yes.\n\n- Bowlby attachment: Anxious-Ambivalent reaction: God expects obedience but shows gentle mercy.\n\n- Decision: balance leads to outcome: revelation of heavens, naming the firmament \"Shamayim\". This is a merciful act.\n\nNow produce Hebrew voice block. Since addressee = individual (not prophet), we use divine action narrative in 3rd person.\n\nWe need biblical Hebrew only, no modern words.\n\nWe can say:\n\n\"וַיִּקְרָא אֱלֹהִים לָרָקִיעַ