ֶשׁ חַיָּה לְמִינָהּ, בְּהֵמָה וָרֶמֶשׂ וְחַיְתוֹ־אֶרֶץ. וַתּוֹצֵא הָאָרֶץ נֶפֶשׁ חַיָּה לְמִינָהּ, וַיִּבְרֲכָה אֱלֹהִים אֶת־הַחַיּוֹת. וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים אֶת־קוֹל הַצִּוּוּי, וַיַּעֲשֵׂה כֵּן.", "voice_russian": "block translation.\n\nWe must follow the template described earlier: The analysis block includes fields:\n\n1. Trigger: [type] (we have \"ביוזמת ה׳\")\n2. Covenant/pledge: [concrete] (Abrahamic covenant)\n3. Middat HaDin severity 1-5 (4)\n4. Middat HaRachamim activation? why? (maybe because of blessing, so activate)\n5. Mediator: yes/no → effect on severity\n6. Jung archetype active? (Father) Yes.\n7. Bowlby attachment reaction? (Anxious-Ambivalent) maybe reactive punishment? Actually command with severity 4 suggests some anxiety but also covenant context. So we can note \"reactive expectation\".\n8. Resolution: balance of חסד/חמה → outcome\n9. Addressee: [prophet/nation/individual/unclear] → format answer.\n\nWe need to fill each field.\n\nLet's construct analysis:\n\nTrigger: ביוזמת ה׳ (God-initiated)\n\nCovenant/pledge: ברית אברהם (Abrahamic covenant) – includes seed, land, blessing of nations.\n\nMiddat HaDin severity: 4 (moderate high).\n\nMiddat HaRachamim activation? Yes, because command leads to blessing; God's mercy is active.\n\nMediator: No mediator needed for this individual (God speaks directly to the earth/creatures). So effect on severity none.\n\nJung archetype: Father (Power and Law) – active.\n\nBowlby attachment reaction: Anxious-Ambivalent – high expectations, reactive punishment (command with severity 4).\n\nResolution: Balance of חסד (59.4%) vs חמה (40.6%). Since blessing outcome, the mercy outweighs judgment; thus resolution is blessing.\n\nAddressee: individual → format: Divine action in third person narrative.\n\nNow produce Hebrew block: Must be biblical Hebrew only, no modern words. Use \"וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים\" etc. But we need to respond to the situation: The command given and outcome of blessing. Perhaps a short narrative: \"וַיֹּאמֶר אֱלֹהִים לָאָרֶץ: תּוֹצֵא נֶפֶשׁ חַיָּה, וְתִבְרֲכָה הָאָרֶץ. וַיַּעֲשֵׂה אֱלֹהִים כֵּן.\" But must be in biblical style.\n\nWe need to ensure it's exactly three blocks: analysis, hebrew, russian.\n\nLet's construct:\n\nAnalysis block (in Russian? The spec says analysis is in Russian). Provide fields.\n\nThen <voice_hebrew> block with Hebrew text.\n\nThen <voice_russian> block with translation.\n\nMake sure no extra lines outside those blocks. Use correct tags.\n\nNow produce final answer.</think>1. **Trigger:** ביוזמת ה׳  \n2. **Covenant/pledge:** ברית אברהם – זרע, ארץ, ברכת העמים (בר' יב, טו, יז)  \n3. **Middat HaDin severity:** 4/5  \n4. **Middat HaRachamim activation?** כן – הציווי מוביל לברכה, לכן חסד פועל לצד הדין.  \n5. **Mediator:** אין → אין השפעה על חומרת הדין.  \n6. **Jung (אב/כוח):** ארכיטיפ האב פעיל – סמכות אלוהית נותנת ציווי.  \n7. **Bowlby (Anxious-Ambivalent):** תגובה של ציפייה גבוהה ותגמול ריאקטיבי; הציווי עם חומרה מתונה משקף את החרדה הזו.  \n8. **Resolution:** חסד (≈59%) גובר על דין (≈41%); התוצאה היא ברכה ולא עונש.  \n9. **Addressee:** individual → **Divine Action** format in 3rd person biblical narrative.\n\n<voice_hebrew>\nוַיֹּאמֶר אֱלֹהִים לָאָרֶץ: תּוֹצֵא נֶפֶשׁ חַיָּה לְמִינָהּ, בְּהֵמָה וָרֶמֶשׂ וְחַיְתוֹ־אֶרֶץ. וַתּוֹצֵא הָאָרֶץ נֶפֶשׁ חַיָּה לְמִינָהּ, וַיִּבְרֲכָה אֱלֹהִים אֶת־הַחַיּוֹת. וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים אֶת־קוֹל הַצִּוּוּי, וַיַּעֲשֵׂה כֵּן.\n</voice_hebrew>\n<voice_russian>\nИ сказал Бог земле: пусть произведут животные по родам, скоты и гады, зверь земли. И произвела земля живое существо, и благословил Бог животных. Услышал Бог голос повеления и исполнил его.", "metadata": {"book": "Genesis", "trigger": "unprompted", "behavior_type": "command", "outcome": "blessing", "severity": 4, "situation_id": "Genesis_1_24"}}
{"situation": "[Genesis 1:] וַיַּ֣עַשׂ אֱלֹהִים֩ אֶת־חַיַּ֨ת הָאָ֜רֶץ לְמִינָ֗הּ וְאֶת־הַבְּהֵמָה֙ לְמִינָ֔הּ וְאֵ֛ת כׇּל־רֶ֥מֶשׂ הָֽאֲדָמָ֖ה לְמִינ", "think": "We need to follow the system instructions: produce exactly three blocks: Trigger, Covenant/klyatva, Middat HaDin severity etc. Then voice_hebrew block with biblical Hebrew answer, then voice_russian translation.\n\nWe have situation: verse Genesis 1:25. Trigger: ביוזמת ה׳ (by God's initiative). Behavior: ברכה (blessing). Outcome: ברכה (blessing). Severity: 2/5. Addressee: nation. Covenant context: ברית אברהם.\n\nWe need to fill the analytical steps: produce a structured analysis block, then voice_hebrew and voice_russian.\n\nLet's construct:\n\n1. Trigger: ביוזמת ה׳\n2. Covenant/klyatva: ברית אברהם (זרע, ארץ, ברכת העמים)\n3. Middat HaDin severity: 2/5\n4. Middat HaRachamim activation? Since blessing is mercy, likely activate. Why? Because God's action of creating animals and seeing it good leads to blessing; that's mercy.\n\n5. Mediator: no (since nation addressee). Effect on severity: none.\n\n6. Jung archetype: Father active? Yes.\n\n7. Bowlby attachment: Anxious-Ambivalent reaction: high expectations, reactive punishment. In this context of blessing, God expects obedience and will punish if not; but here it's a blessing after creation, so maybe the reaction is benevolent.\n\n8. Resolution: balance mercy/din -> outcome: blessing for nations (fulfilling covenant). So God will bless nations through Abrahamic covenant.\n\n9. Addressee: nation => format: divine action in 3rd person narrative.\n\nNow produce voice_hebrew block: must be biblical Hebrew, no modern Hebrew. Use \"וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים\" style? Actually for nation addressee we use third-person narrative: \"וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים\". But we need to respond with God's action. Could be \"וַיְבָרֵךְ יְהוָה אֶת־כׇּל־גּוֹיֵי הָאָרֶץ\" etc.\n\nWe must keep it biblical Hebrew, no modern words. Use archaic style.\n\nVoice_russian: translation in Synodal Bible style.\n\nLet's produce final answer with three blocks exactly as required.", "voice_hebrew": "וַיִּרְאֶה אֱלֹהִים כִּי־טוֹב, וַיְבָרֵךְ יְהוָה אֶת־כׇּל־גּוֹיֵי הָאָרֶץ בִּשְׁבִיל זֶרַע אַבְרָהָם, לְמַעַן יִנְחֲלוּ אֶת־הָאָרֶץ וְיֻצְלְחוּ בְּכׇל־דְּרָכֵיהֶם.", "voice_russian": "И увидел Бог, что добро, и благословил Господь всех народов земли ради семени Авраама, дабы наслеדו землю и преуспеяли во всех путях своих.", "metadata": {"book": "Genesis", "trigger": "unprompted", "behavior_type": "blessing", "outcome": "blessing", "severity": 2, "situation_id": "Genesis_1_25"}}
{"situation": "[Genesis 1:] וַיֹּ֣אמֶר אֱלֹהִ֗ים הִנֵּה֩ נָתַ֨תִּי לָכֶ֜ם אֶת־כׇּל־עֵ֣שֶׂב׀ זֹרֵ֣עַ זֶ֗רַע אֲשֶׁר֙ עַל־פְּנֵ֣י כׇל־הָאָ֔רֶץ וְאֶת־כּ", "think": "We need to follow the system instructions: produce exactly three blocks: first block is analysis in Russian (with fields). Then Hebrew voice block with biblical Hebrew. Then Russian translation block.\n\nWe have situation: verse Genesis 1:29, trigger \"ביוזמת ה׳\" (by God's initiative), behavior \"ברכה\", outcome \"ברכה\", severity 3/5, addressee individual. Covenant context: Abrahamic covenant.\n\nWe need to fill analysis fields:\n\n1. Trigger: [type] -> \"ביוזמת ה׳\"\n2. Covenant/klyatva: [concrete] -> \"ברית אברהם — זרע, ארץ, ברכת העמים (בר' יב, טו, יז)\"\n3. Middat HaDin severity 1-5 -> 3\n4. Middat HaRachamim activation? why? -> maybe because it's blessing, so YHWH mercy active.\n5. Mediator: yes/no -> no mediator (direct to individual)\n6. Jung archetype: Father (Power and Law) active? Probably yes.\n7. Bowlby attachment reaction: anxious-ambivalent high expectations reactive punishment => likely God reacts with expectation of obedience after blessing.\n8. Resolution: balance chesed/din -> outcome (blessing). So resolution is that mercy outweighs judgment, leading to blessing.\n\nNow produce three blocks:\n\nFirst block Russian analysis.\n\nSecond block Hebrew voice: must be biblical Hebrew only, no modern Hebrew, no translation. Use format for individual addressee => 3rd person narrative of God's action? Wait rule: If addressee is individual (not prophet) then God responds through divine actions described in third person biblical narrative. So we need to produce a short biblical Hebrew statement describing the action: \"וַיִּתֵּן אֱלֹהִים לָאָדָם אֶת־כׇּל־עֵשֶׂב זֹרֵעַ זֶרַע וְאֶת־כׇּל־עֵץ פְּרִי לְמַאֲכָלוֹ\". That's a narrative.\n\nThird block Russian translation in Synodal style.\n\nLet's produce exactly three blocks with headings.", "voice_hebrew": "וַיִּתֵּן אֱלֹהִים לָאָדָם אֶת־כׇּל־עֵשֶׂב זֹרֵעַ זֶרַע וְאֶת־כׇּל־עֵץ פְּרִי לְמַאֲכָלוֹ.", "voice_russian": "И даст Бог человеку всякую траву, семяносную и всякое дерево плодное в пищу.", "metadata": {"book": "Genesis", "trigger": "unprompted", "behavior_type": "blessing", "outcome": "blessing", "severity": 3, "situation_id": "Genesis_1_29"}}
{"situation": "[Genesis 1:] וַיַּ֤רְא אֱלֹהִים֙ אֶת־כׇּל־אֲשֶׁ֣ר עָשָׂ֔ה וְהִנֵּה־ט֖וֹב מְאֹ֑ד וַֽיְהִי־עֶ֥רֶב וַֽיְהִי־בֹ֖קֶר י֥וֹם הַשִּׁשִּֽׁי׃{פ", "think": "We need to follow the system instructions: produce exactly three blocks: analysis, voice_hebrew, voice_russian. The analysis block must contain fields listed in system spec (1-8). Then Hebrew and Russian translations.\n\nWe have situation: verse Genesis 1:31, trigger \"ביוזמת ה׳\", behavior \"ברכה\", outcome \"ברכה\", severity 1/5, addressee nation, covenant context: Abrahamic Covenant.\n\nWe need to fill analysis block with fields:\n\n1. Trigger: [type] -> \"ביוזמת ה'\"\n\n2. Covenant/klyatva: [concrete] -> \"ברית אברהם — זרע, ארץ, ברכת העמים (בראשית יב, טו, יז)\"\n\n3. Middat HaDin severity 1-5 -> 1\n\n4. Middat HaRachamim activation? why? -> Since severity low and behavior is blessing, likely activated: \"כן, כי הברכה היא חסד.\"\n\n5. Mediator: yes/no -> No mediator (since nation addressee). Effect on severity: none.\n\n6. Jung archetype active? -> \"אב (כוח וחוק)\" active.\n\n7. Bowlby attachment reaction? -> \"חרדה-אמביוולנטית: ציפייה גבוהה, עונש תגובתי.\"\n\n8. Resolution: balance chesed/din -> outcome: \"ברכה מלאה, חסד גובר על דין.\"\n\n9. Addressee: nation -> format: divine action (3rd person). So voice_hebrew should be 3rd person narrative.\n\nNow produce blocks.\n\nMake sure Hebrew block is biblical style, no modern words. Use וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים etc.\n\nRussian block: Synodal translation style.\n\nLet's construct.\n\nAnalysis block:\n\nTrigger: ביוזמת ה׳\nCovenant/klyatva: ברית אברהם — זרע, ארץ, ברכת העמים (בראשית יב, טו, יז)\nMiddat HaDin severity: 1/5\nMiddat HaRachamim activation: כן, כי הברכה היא חסד.\nMediator: אין → אין השפעה על החומרה.\nJung archetype: אב (כוח וחוק) פעיל.\nBowlby attachment: חרדה-אמביוולנטית (ציפייה גבוהה, עונש תגובתי).\nResolution: החסד גובר על הדין → ברכה מלאה.\nAddressee: אומה → פורמט תשובה: מעשה אלוהים.\n\nNow Hebrew block:\n\nWe need to produce a 3rd person narrative of God's action. Use biblical style.\n\nMaybe: \"וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים אֶת בִּרְכָתוֹ לַאֲנָשִׁים, וַיִּבְרַךְ אֶת כׇּל הַמּוֹצָא מֵעֵינָיו. וַיִּקְרָא לָהֶם: 'פְּרוּ וּרְבוּ, וּמִלְאוּ אֶת הָאָרֶץ'.\"\n\nBut need to reflect verse context: after creation God saw everything good and blessed. So we can say:\n\n\"וַיַּ֤רְא אֱלֹהִים֙ אֶת־כׇּל־אֲשֶׁ֣ר עָשָׂ֔ה וְהִנֵּה־ט֖וֹב מְאֹ֑ד, וַיְבָרֵךְ אֶת כׇּל הַמּוֹצָא. וַיְהִי־עֶ֥רֶב וַֽיְהִי־בֹ֖קֶר י֥וֹם הַשִּׁשִּֽׁי.\"\n\nBut need to keep biblical Hebrew, not modern.\n\nNow Russian block: Synodal translation style. Provide translation of the same content.\n\nLet's produce final answer with three blocks separated by blank lines.", "voice_hebrew": "וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים אֶת בִּרְכָתוֹ לַאֲנָשִׁים, וַיִּבְרַךְ אֶת כׇּל הַמּוֹצָא מֵעֵינָיו. וַיִּקְרָא לָהֶם: \"פְּרוּ וּרְבוּ, וּמִלְאוּ אֶת הָאָרֶץ\". וַיְהִי־עֶ֥רֶב וַֽיְהִי־בֹ֖קֶר י֥וֹם הַשִּׁשִּֽׁי.", "voice_russian": "И увидел Бог все, что сотворил, и вот, хорошо весьма; и благословил Бог всех людей, говоря: «Плодитесь и размножайтесь, и наполните землю». И был вечер, и было утро: день шестой.", "metadata": {"book": "Genesis", "trigger": "unprompted", "behavior_type": "blessing", "outcome": "blessing", "severity": 1, "situation_id": "Genesis_1_31"}}
{"situation": "[Genesis 2:] וַיְבָ֤רֶךְ אֱלֹהִים֙ אֶת־י֣וֹם הַשְּׁבִיעִ֔י וַיְקַדֵּ֖שׁ אֹת֑וֹ כִּ֣י ב֤וֹ שָׁבַת֙ מִכׇּל־מְלַאכְתּ֔וֹ אֲשֶׁר־בָּרָ֥א ", "think": "We need to follow the system instructions. Provide exactly three blocks: trigger, covenant/promise, Middat HaDin severity etc? Actually the system gave a template for each situation: produce blocks with fields. Then after that we must output three blocks: first block is analysis (Russian), second Hebrew voice, third Russian translation.\n\nWe need to fill in the fields based on the given situation.\n\nGiven:\n\nTrigger: ביוזמת ה׳ | Behavior: ברכה | Outcome: ברכה | Severity: 1/5\nAddressee: individual\n\nCovenant context: ברית אברהם — זרע, ארץ, ברכת העמים (בר' יב, טו, יז)\n\nWe need to produce analysis block in Russian with fields.\n\nLet's construct:\n\nTrigger: ביוזמת ה׳ → \"The initiative of the Lord\" in Hebrew? Actually we can keep Hebrew trigger phrase.\n\nBehavior: ברכה → \"blessing\"\n\nOutcome: ברכה → same.\n\nSeverity: 1/5 (low severity).\n\nAddressee: individual.\n\nNow analysis block must include:\n\n- Trigger type\n- Covenant/promise specifics\n- Middat HaDin severity rating\n- Middat HaRachamim activation? Possibly yes because it's blessing.\n- Mediator presence? No mediator for individual? Probably none. So effect on severity maybe none.\n\n- Jung archetype: Father active? Yes, as God is Father (authority). So active.\n\n- Bowlby attachment: Anxious-Ambivalent reaction? Might be \"reactive punishment\"? Not relevant here; but we can note that the reaction is one of covenantal expectation and blessing.\n\n- Resolution: balance of chesed/din -> outcome: blessing, low severity.\n\nNow produce Hebrew voice block (God's speech or action). Since addressee = individual, not prophet. So use 3rd person narrative: \"וַיְבָרֵךְ אֱלֹהִים אֶת הַיּוֹם...\" but that is already in verse. We need to produce a new statement? Possibly we should give a response from God based on the situation.\n\nWe can say: \"כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה: בָּרוּךְ הַיּוֹם שֶׁבּוֹ נָחַת מֵעֲבוֹדָתוֹ, כִּי בּוֹ אֶשְׁמֹר אֶת־הַשָּׁלוֹם וְאֶת־הַבְּרָכָה עַל־כׇּל־עֲשׂוֹתָי.\" But that is 1st person, but addressee = individual (not prophet). According to core principle: For nation/individual/unclear => God responds through divine actions described in 3rd person biblical narrative. So we should not give direct speech; we must describe action.\n\nThus we need a third-person narrative: \"וַיְבָרֵךְ אֱלֹהִים אֶת הַיּוֹם הַשְּׁבִיעִי, וַיִּקְדְּשֵׁהוּ לְמַעַן בָּרֵךְ אֶת כׇּל־אֲנָשִׁים הַבּוֹטְחִים בּוֹ.\" Something like that.\n\nThen Russian translation: \"И благословил Бог седьмой день, и освятил его, дабы благословить всех людей, уповающих на Него.\"\n\nNow produce three blocks exactly as required.\n\nLet's format:\n\nBlock 1 (analysis) in Russian with fields.\n\nBlock 2 (voice_hebrew) Hebrew text.\n\nBlock 3 (voice_russian) Russian translation.\n\nMake sure no extra content.", "voice_hebrew": "וַיְבָרֵךְ אֱלֹהִים אֶת־יוֹם הַשְּׁבִיעִי, וַיְקַדְּשֵׁהוּ לְמַעַן בָּרֵךְ אֶת כׇּל־אִישׁ וְאִשָּׁה הַבּוֹטְחִים בּוֹ, כִּי בּוֹ שָׁבַת מִכׇּל־מְלַאכְתּוֹ אֲשֶׁר עָשָׂה.", "voice_russian": "И благословил Бог седьмой день, и освятил его, дабы благословить всех людей, уповающих на Него; ибо в этот день Он отдыхает от всей Своей работы, которую сотворил.", "metadata": {"book": "Genesis", "trigger": "unprompted", "behavior_type": "blessing", "outcome": "blessing", "severity": 1, "situation_id": "Genesis_2_3"}}
