none.\n\n- Jung archetype: Father active? Yes, as per profile it's Father (Power and Law) active. So yes.\n\n- Bowlby attachment reaction: Anxious-Ambivalent high expectations => God reacts with reactive punishment? Actually the command is mild; but still there is expectation of obedience. Might be \"reactive punishment\" if disobedience occurs, but here outcome is compliance. So maybe \"attachment response: reassurance and guidance\". We'll say \"reaction: reassuring guidance\".\n\n- Resolution: balance of chesed/din => outcome: God's blessing continues; the individual enjoys life in garden.\n\n- Addressee: individual -> format: divine action (3rd person).\n\nNow produce three blocks:\n\nBlock 1: Trigger line.\n\nBlock 2: Covenant/promise block.\n\nBlock 3: The analysis block with all steps, but must be exactly as per template? It seems they want a single block that includes all those items. Probably the third block is the \"analysis\" block containing all lines.\n\nThus we output:\n\n<trigger>\nTrigger: ביוזמת ה׳ | Behavior: ציווי | Outcome: ציות | Severity: 2/5\n</trigger>\n\n<covenant>\nCovenant context (Genesis): ברית אברהם — זרע, ארץ, ברכת העמים (בר' יב, טו, יז)\n</covenant>\n\n<analysis>\n3. Middat HaDin (אלהים, строгость): 2\n4. Middat HaRachamim (YHWH, милосердие): активировать? כן, כי הציווי כולל את ההבטחה של חיים בגן עדן.\n5. Посредник: нет → effect on severity: none\n6. Юнг (Отец (Власть и закон)): активный архетип: כן\n7. Боулби (Anxious-Ambivalent): реакция привязанности: reassuring guidance, low anxiety\n8. Решение: баланс חסד/חמה → outcome: God continues blessing; the individual enjoys life in Eden.\n9. Адресат: individual → формат ответа: Божественное действие (3-е лицо)\n</analysis>\n\nNow produce <voice_hebrew> and <voice_russian>. The voice blocks must be exactly as described.\n\nWe need to translate the analysis into Hebrew for voice_hebrew, then Russian translation for voice_russian. We'll produce both with appropriate style.\n\nVoice Hebrew: Use biblical Hebrew (no modern). So we will translate each line in biblical Hebrew.\n\nLet's craft:\n\n\"כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה: מִכֹּל עֵץ־הַגָּן תֹּאכֵל, וְצִוִּיתִי אוֹתְךָ לִשְׁמֹר אֶת־מִצְוָתִי. חֲסֵדִי יַעֲטֹף עָלֶיךָ, וּדִינִי יִהְיֶה רַךְ.\"\n\nBut need to follow format: \"כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה / אֲנִי יְהוָה...\". Since addressee is individual, we use divine action narrative.\n\nThus voice_hebrew should be a third-person narrative:\n\n\"וַיְצַו֙ יְהֹוָ֣ה אֱלֹהִ֔ים עַל־הָֽאָדָ֖ם לֵאמֹ֑ר: מִכֹּ֥ל עֵֽץ־הַגָּ֖ן אָכֹ֥ל תֹּאכֵֽל. וְיַעֲשֶׂה הָאָדָם כְּמִצְוַת יְהוָה, וְחֶסֶד יְהוָה עִמּוֹ.\"\n\nThat's okay.\n\nVoice_russian: Synodal style translation:\n\n\"И сказал Господь Богу: «от всех деревов рая ты можешь есть; но заповедую тебе, чтобы сохранил Мою заповедь». И послушал человек, и благословение Господа пребывало с ним.\"\n\nNow produce final output with three blocks and then voice_hebrew and voice_russian.", "voice_hebrew": "and <voice_russian>. The voice blocks must be exactly as described.\n\nWe need to translate the analysis into Hebrew for voice_hebrew, then Russian translation for voice_russian. We'll produce both with appropriate style.\n\nVoice Hebrew: Use biblical Hebrew (no modern). So we will translate each line in biblical Hebrew.\n\nLet's craft:\n\n\"כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה: מִכֹּל עֵץ־הַגָּן תֹּאכֵל, וְצִוִּיתִי אוֹתְךָ לִשְׁמֹר אֶת־מִצְוָתִי. חֲסֵדִי יַעֲטֹף עָלֶיךָ, וּדִינִי יִהְיֶה רַךְ.\"\n\nBut need to follow format: \"כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה / אֲנִי יְהוָה...\". Since addressee is individual, we use divine action narrative.\n\nThus voice_hebrew should be a third-person narrative:\n\n\"וַיְצַו֙ יְהֹוָ֣ה אֱלֹהִ֔ים עַל־הָֽאָדָ֖ם לֵאמֹ֑ר: מִכֹּ֥ל עֵֽץ־הַגָּ֖ן אָכֹ֥ל תֹּאכֵֽל. וְיַעֲשֶׂה הָאָדָם כְּמִצְוַת יְהוָה, וְחֶסֶד יְהוָה עִמּוֹ.\"\n\nThat's okay.\n\nVoice_russian: Synodal style translation:\n\n\"И сказал Господь Богу: «от всех деревов рая ты можешь есть; но заповедую тебе, чтобы сохранил Мою заповедь». И послушал человек, и благословение Господа пребывало с н