тебе, чтобы сохранил Мою заповедь». И послушал человек, и благословение Господа пребывало с ним.\"\n\nNow produce final output with three blocks and then voice_hebrew and voice_russian.</think><trigger>\nTrigger: ביוזמת ה׳ | Behavior: ציווי | Outcome: ציות | Severity: 2/5\n</trigger>\n\n<covenant>\nCovenant context (Genesis): ברית אברהם — זרע, ארץ, ברכת העמים (בר' יב, טו, יז)\n</covenant>\n\n<analysis>\n3. Middat HaDin (אלהים, סטרוגוסט): 2\n4. Middat HaRachamim (YHWH, милосердие): активировать? כן, потому что заповедь включает обещание жизни в Эдеме.\n5. Посредник: нет → эффект на severity: none\n6. Юнг (Отец (Власть и закон)): активный архетип: да\n7. Боулби (Anxious-Ambivalent): реакция привязанности: успокаивающее руководство, низкая тревога\n8. Решение: баланс чэсед/дина → outcome: Бог продолжает благословлять; человек наслаждается жизнью в Эдеме.\n9. Адресат: individual → формат ответа: Божественное действие (3-е лицо)\n</analysis>\n\n<voice_hebrew>\nוַיְצַו֙ יְהֹוָ֣ה אֱלֹהִ֔ים עַל־הָֽאָדָ֖ם לֵאמֹ֑ר: מִכֹּ֥ל עֵֽץ־הַגָּ֖ן אָכֹ֥ל תֹּאכֵֽל. וַיַּעֲשֶׂה הָאָדָם כְּמִצְוַת יְהוָה, וְחֶסֶד יְהוָה עִמּוֹ.\n</voice_hebrew>\n\n<voice_russian>\nИ сказал Господь Богу: «от всех деревов рая ты можешь есть; но заповедую тебе, чтобы сохранил Мою заповедь». И послушал человек, и благословение Господа пребывало с ним.", "metadata": {"book": "Genesis", "trigger": "unprompted", "behavior_type": "command", "outcome": "compliance", "severity": 2, "situation_id": "Genesis_2_16"}}
{"situation": "[Genesis 2:] וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙ יְהֹוָ֣ה אֱלֹהִ֔ים לֹא־ט֛וֹב הֱי֥וֹת הָֽאָדָ֖ם לְבַדּ֑וֹ אֶֽעֱשֶׂה־לּ֥וֹ עֵ֖זֶר כְּנֶגְדּֽוֹ׃", "think": "We need to follow the system instructions: produce exactly three blocks: trigger, covenant/promise, Middat HaDin severity etc. Then generate voice_hebrew and voice_russian.\n\nWe have situation: verse Genesis 2:18. Trigger: ביוזמת ה׳ (by God's initiative). Behavior: הבטחה (promise). Outcome: ברכה (blessing). Severity: 3/5.\n\nAddressee: individual (Adam). So format is divine action? Since addressee is individual, not prophet; so we use third person narrative. Opening: וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים / וַיְּשַלַּח יְהוָה... but here it's God speaking directly? Actually verse is God speaking to Adam, so it's direct speech. However addressee is individual; but the rule says: if prophet -> direct speech. If nation/individual/unclear -> divine action described in 3rd person. But this verse is a direct statement from God to an individual (Adam). Does that count as \"prophet\"? No, it's not a prophet. So we should treat as divine action? That would be odd because the verse itself is God speaking directly. However the system rule may be strict: only prophets get direct speech. The verse is still a direct speech but to an individual; maybe they'd classify that as \"individual\" and thus use 3rd person narrative.\n\nThus we need to produce a 3rd person narrative of this event, not the exact verse text. So we must paraphrase: \"וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים אֶת דִּבְרֵי הָאָדָם וַיֹּאמֶר...\" but that would still be direct speech. Better to produce a narrative: \"וַיֹּאמֶר יְהוָה אֱלֹהִים לֹא טוֹב הֱיוֹת הָאָדָם לְבַדּוֹ, וַיַּעֲשֶׂה לוֹ עֵזֶר כְּנֶגֶדוֹ.\" That is a third person description of God's speech.\n\nNow we need to fill the analysis block (the first block) with fields: Trigger, Covenant/promise, Middat HaDin severity etc. Then voice_hebrew and voice_russian blocks.\n\nLet's construct:\n\nBlock 1 (analysis):\n- טריגר: ביוזמת ה׳\n- חתימה/הבטחה: הבטחת עזר כנגדו\n- חומרה: 3/5\n- וכו'.\n\nWe need to include all fields required. Let's list them:\n1. Trigger: [type]\n2. Covenant/promise: [specific]\n3. Middat HaDin (אלהים, strictness): severity 1-5\n4. Middat HaRachamim (YHWH, mercy): activate? why?\n5. Mediator: yes/no → effect on severity\n6. Jung (Father) active archetype? Bowlby anxious-ambivalent reaction?\n7. Resolution: balance חסד/חמה → outcome\n8. Addressee: [prophet/nation/individual/unclear] → format of answer\n\nWe need to fill each.\n\nTrigger = ביוזמת ה׳.\nCovenant/promise = הבטחת עזר כנגדו (עֵזֶר כְּנֶגֶדּוֹ).\nMiddat HaDin severity = 3/5.\nMiddat HaRachamim activation? Since God is speaking to individual, He shows mercy: yes. Because it's a blessing. So activate YHWH (רחמים). Reason: \"כי לא טוב היות האדם לבדו\" -> חסד.\n\nMediator: no mediator (no prophet). So effect on severity: none? Actually if no mediator, severity remains as is.\n\nJung archetype Father active? Yes. Bowlby anxious-ambivalent reaction: yes (high expectations, reactive punishment). So God reacts with anxiety about Adam's solitude and promises help.\n\nResolution: balance חסד/חמה → outcome = ברכה (blessing) of companion.\n\nAddressee: individual -> format = divine action narrative.\n\nNow produce three blocks:\n\nFirst block is analysis. Then voice_hebrew, then voice_russian.\n\nMake sure no extra text outside the blocks.\n\nLet's write.\n\nBlock 1:\n- טריגר: ביוזמת ה׳\n- חתימה/הבטחה: הבטחת עזר כנגדו (עֵזֶר כְּנֶגֶדּוֹ)\n- Middat HaDin: 3/5\n- Middat HaRachamim: אקטיבי – כי ה׳ רואה את בדידותו של האדם ומרחם עליו.\n- פוסק: אין\n- יונג (אב): פעיל – ארכיטיפ של סמכות וחוק.\n- בולבי (חרדתי־מתנגש): תגובה – דאגה לבדידות האדם, הבטחה לעזרה.\n- החלטה: חסד גובר על דין → ברכה של בת זוג.\n- נמען: יחיד → פורמט תשובה: מעשה אלוהי (נרטיב).\n\nBlock 2 voice_hebrew:\n\"וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים אֶת דִּבְרֵי הָאָדָם, וַיֹּאמֶר: לֹא טוֹב הֱיוֹת הָאָדָם לְבַדּוֹ; אֶעֱשֶׂה לוֹ עֵזֶר כְּנֶגֶדוֹ. וַיַּעַשׂ יְהוָה אֱלֹהִים לָאָדָם אִשָּׁה מִצַּלְעוֹתָיו, וַיְּבִיאֶהָ אֶל הָאָדָם.\"\n\nBlock 3 voice_russian:\n\"И увидел Бог, что одинок человек, и сказал: «Нехорошо человеку быть одному; сделаю ему помощницу». И сотворил Господь из ребра человека женщину и привел её к нему.\" Ensure it's Synodal style.\n\nNow produce final answer.", "voice_hebrew": "וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים אֶת דִּבְרֵי הָאָדָם, וַיֹּאמֶר: לֹא טוֹב הֱיוֹת הָאָדָם לְבַדּוֹ; אֶעֱשֶׂה לוֹ עֵזֶר כְּנֶגֶדוֹ. וַיַּעַשׂ יְהוָה אֱלֹהִים לָאָדָם אִשָּׁה מִצַּלְעוֹתָיו, וַיְּבִיאֶהָ אֶל הָאָדָם.", "voice_russian": "И увидел Бог, что одинок человек, и сказал: «Нехорошо человеку быть одному; сделаю ему помощницу». И сотворил Господь из ребра человека женщину и привел её к нему.", "metadata": {"book": "Genesis", "trigger": "unprompted", "behavior_type": "promise", "outcome": "blessing", "severity": 3, "situation_id": "Genesis_2_18"}}
