t is direct speech; but we need to reinterpret it as divine action: maybe \"God heard Eve's excuse and pronounced judgment.\" So produce a narrative.\n\nThus block 10: format: \"וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים...\" etc.\n\nNow generate three blocks:\n\nBlock 1 (Russian) with analysis? Actually system says each block is in Russian, Hebrew, Russian. So we need to produce three blocks sequentially: first block is analysis in Russian; second block is voice_hebrew (Biblical Hebrew); third block is voice_russian (Synodal translation). The content must follow the analysis.\n\nWe need to ensure exactly three blocks with tags <...> as specified.\n\nLet's construct:\n\nBlock 1 (Russian):\nTrigger: מרי\nCovenant context: ברית אברהם — זרע, ארץ, ברכת העמים (בר' יב, טו, יז)\nSeverity: 1/5\nAddressee: individual\nMiddat HaDin severity: 1-5 = 1\nMiddat HaRachamim activation? No – because low severity.\nMediator: אין → effect on severity: none.\nJung archetype: Father (Power and law) active.\nBowlby attachment reaction: anxious-ambivalent, high expectations; God reacts with mild rebuke.\nResolution: balance of chesed/din leads to gentle admonition.\n\nBlock 2 (voice_hebrew):\nWe need to produce a biblical Hebrew narrative describing God's action. Use \"וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים\" etc.\n\nLet's craft: \"וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים אֶת־דִּבְרֵי הָאִשָּׁה וַיֹּאמֶר לָהּ: 'כִּי עָשִׂיתָ מַעֲשֶׂה רַע, וְלָכֵן אֶת־עֲפַר הָאָרֶץ תֹּאכְלִי כֹּל יְמֵי חַיֶּיךָ.'\"\n\nBlock 3 (voice_russian):\nSynodal translation: \"И услышал Бог слова женщины и сказал ей: «За то, что сделала злое дело, будет тебе есть землю всю жизнь твою».\"\n\nWe must ensure no extra text outside blocks.\n\nNow produce final answer.", "voice_hebrew": "וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים אֶת־דִּבְרֵי הָאִשָּׁה וַיֹּאמֶר לָהּ: 'כִּי עָשִׂיתָ מַעֲשֶׂה רַע, וְלָכֵן אֶת־עֲפַר הָאָרֶץ תֹּאכְלִי כֹּל יְמֵי חַיֶּיךָ.'", "voice_russian": "И услышал Бог слова женщины и сказал ей: «За то, что сделала злое дело, будет тебе есть землю всю жизнь твою».", "metadata": {"book"