{"situation": "[Genesis 3:] וַיֹּ֩אמֶר֩ יְהֹוָ֨ה אֱלֹהִ֥ים׀אֶֽל־הַנָּחָשׁ֮ כִּ֣י עָשִׂ֣יתָ זֹּאת֒ אָר֤וּר אַתָּה֙ מִכׇּל־הַבְּהֵמָ֔ה וּמִכֹּ֖ל חַיַּ", "think": "We need to follow the system instructions: produce three blocks: analysis block in Russian, then voice_hebrew block with biblical Hebrew, then voice_russian translation. The analysis block must contain fields as listed: Trigger, Covenant/klyatva, Middat HaDin severity, Middat HaRachamim activation (why?), Mediator effect on severity, Jung archetype active?, Bowlby attachment reaction, Resolution balance outcome, Addressee and format.\n\nWe have situation: verse Genesis 3:14. Trigger: מרי (rebellion). Behavior: עונש (punishment). Outcome: עונש. Severity: 4/5.\n\nAddressee: individual (the serpent). So God's response is divine action described in third person narrative, not direct speech? The rule says: If addressee = individual (not prophet), then format = \"וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים / וַיְּשַלַּח יְהוָה...\". So we should produce a third-person narrative.\n\nWe need to fill analysis block: Trigger: מרי (rebellion). Covenant context: ברית אברהם — זרע, ארץ, ברכת העמים (Gen 12,15,17). Middat HaDin severity = 4/5. Middat HaRachamim activation? Possibly not activated because it's a punishment; but we can note that there is no explicit mercy, so \"לא\". Why? Because the curse is severe.\n\nMediator: none (no prophet). So effect on severity: none.\n\nJung archetype: Father (Power and Law) active. Bowlby attachment: Anxious-Ambivalent reaction: high expectations, reactive punishment.\n\nResolution: balance of חסד/חמה → outcome: the serpent is cursed, but also given a role in God's plan? Not sure; but we can say \"עונש שולט, אך זרע האישה מבטיח תקווה\" maybe. But for this situation it's just punishment.\n\nAddressee: individual => format: divine action (3rd person). So voice_hebrew block will be a biblical Hebrew narrative of God's curse on the serpent.\n\nWe need to produce exactly three blocks, with headings: first analysis block in Russian, then <voice_hebrew>, then <voice_russian>. Ensure no extra text outside these blocks.\n\nLet's construct.\n\nAnalysis block:\n\n- Триггер: מרי\n- Завет/клятва: ברית אברהם (זרע, ארץ, ברכת העמים)\n- Middat HaDin severity: 4/5\n- Middat HaRachamim activation: לא (почему? – наказание без милосердия)\n- Pосредник: нет → effect on severity: none\n- Юнг (Отец): активный архетип\n- Боулби (Anxious-Ambivalent): реакция привязанности – тревожно-амбивалентная, высокая требовательность, реактивное наказание.\n- Решение: баланс חסד/חמה → outcome: серпент проклят; нет явного милосердия, но наказание служит целесообразным судом.\n- Адресат: individual → формат ответа: Божественное действие (3-е лицо).\n\nNow voice_hebrew block: need biblical Hebrew narrative. Use verse but maybe rephrase? The system says \"Voice format: וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים / וַיְּשַלַּח יְהוָה...\". So we can write:\n\nוַיֹּאמֶר יְהוָה אֱלֹהִים אֶל־הַנָּחָשׁ כִּי עָשִׂיתָ זֹּאת, אָרוּר אַתָּה מִכׇּל הַבְּהֵמָה וּמִכֹּל חַיַּת הַשָּׂדֶה; עַל־גְּחֹנְךָ תֵלֵךְ, וְעָפָר תֹּאכַל כׇּל יְמֵי חַיֶּיךָ.\n\nBut that's direct speech. The rule says for individual addressee we use divine action description in third person: \"וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים...\". So maybe we need to describe the event: \"וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים אֶת־דִּבְרֵי הַנָּחָשׁ וַיַּעֲנֵהוּ בְּקֶלֶס, לֵאמֹר: 'אָרוּר אַתָּה...'\". That still includes direct speech but within narrative.\n\nBetter to follow the format exactly: \"וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים אֶת־דִּבְרֵי הַנָּחָשׁ וַיֹּאמֶר: '...'\". That includes divine action and direct speech.\n\nWe'll produce that.\n\nNow voice_russian block: translation in Synodal style.\n\nLet's construct final output.", "voice_hebrew": ", then <voice_russian>. Ensure no extra text outside these blocks.\n\nLet's construct.\n\nAnalysis block:\n\n- Триггер: מרי\n- Завет/клятва: ברית אברהם (זרע, ארץ, ברכת העמים)\n- Middat HaDin severity: 4/5\n- Middat HaRachamim activation: לא (почему? – наказание без милосердия)\n- Pосре