iddat HaRachamim (YHWH, милосердие):** активирован: *да*, потому что вместе с наказанием Бог открывает Свою заветную цель – благословение народов через Авраама.  \n\n**Posednik (mediator):** нет → влияние на строгость отсутствует.  \n\n**Юнг (Отец (Власть и закон)):** активный архетип, отражающий авторитет Бога-Отца.  \n**Боулби (Anxious-Ambivalent):** реакция привязанности – ожидание послушания со стороны народа, но готовность к реативному наказанию.  \n\n**Решение / баланс:** строгость и милосердие уравновешиваются: Бог разделяет народы (дин) и одновременно открывает Свой заветный план (רחמים).  \n- **Outcome:** *אלוהים מפזר את העם ומבלבל את שפתותיהם, אך מגלה את תכניתו לברך את האומות דרך אברהם.*\n\n---\n\n<voice_hebrew>\nוַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים אֶת דִּבְרֵי בְּנֵי הָאָדָם, וַיָּפֵץ ה' אֹתָם מִשָּׁם עַל פְּנֵי כׇּל הָאָרֶץ. וַיַּחְדֵּל לַעֲשׂוֹת אֶת אֲשֶׁר זָמְמוּ, וַיִּגְלוֹ אֶת תַּכְלִיתוֹ: לְבָרֵךְ אֶת כׇּל הָעַמִּים בְּזֶרַע אַבְרָהָם.\n</voice_hebrew>\n\n<voice_russian>\nИ услышал Бог речь людей, и рассеял их Господь оттуда по всей земле. Он прекратил делать то, что они замышляли, и открыл Свою цель: благословить все народы через семя Авраама.", "metadata": {"book": "Genesis", "trigger": "disobedience", "behavior_type": "revelation", "outcome": "revelation", "severity": 3, "situation_id": "Genesis_11_6"}}
{"situation": "[Genesis 12:] וַיֹּ֤אמֶר יְהֹוָה֙ אֶל־אַבְרָ֔ם לֶךְ־לְךָ֛ מֵאַרְצְךָ֥ וּמִמּֽוֹלַדְתְּךָ֖ וּמִבֵּ֣ית אָבִ֑יךָ אֶל־הָאָ֖רֶץ אֲשֶׁ֥ר אַר", "think": "We need to follow the system instructions. Provide three blocks: analysis block (Russian), Hebrew voice block, Russian translation block.\n\nWe must fill in the required fields: Trigger, Covenant/Covenant promise, Middat HaDin severity, Middat HaRachamim activation? Probably we need to compute if Middat HaRachamim is activated and why. In this situation, God commands Abraham; it's a covenantal promise with blessing. Likely Middat HaRachamim active because of promise of blessing.\n\nWe must produce analysis block (Russian) containing fields: 1-8 as listed in system spec.\n\nThen Hebrew voice block: direct speech or action? Addressee is individual, so God speaks directly to Abraham. So format: כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה / אֲנִי יְהוָה... Provide a short passage in biblical Hebrew.\n\nThen Russian translation block: Synodal style.\n\nWe need to ensure no extra text outside blocks.\n\nLet's construct analysis:\n\nTrigger: ביוזמת ה׳\nCovenant/promise: ברית אברהם (זרע, ארץ, ברכת העמים)\nMiddat HaDin severity: 3/5\nMiddat HaRachamim activation? Yes, because promise of blessing.\nPurpose: to activate mercy for covenantal promise.\nBowlby attachment reaction: anxious-ambivalent, high expectations -> God expects obedience; reactive punishment if disobeyed. So reaction: \"אנכי יהוה\" with expectation.\n\nJung archetype: Father (power and law) active.\n\nResolution: balance of chesed/din leads to promise of blessing after obedience.\n\nAddressee: individual => direct speech.\n\nNow produce Hebrew voice block: Use biblical style. Possibly include the verse itself? Or a paraphrase? The instruction says \"God responds with DIRECT SPEECH in 1st person.\" So we can give a short statement: \"כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה אֶל־אַבְרָם: לֶךְ־לְךָ מֵאַרְצְךָ וּמִמּוֹלַדְתְּךָ וּמִבֵּית אָבִיךָ, אֶל־הָאָרֶץ אֲשֶׁר אַרְאֶךָּ. וְאֶעֱשֶׂה אוֹתְךָ לְגוֹי גָּדוֹל, וַאֲבָרֵךְ מְבָרְכֶיךָ...\" etc.\n\nThen Russian translation: Synodal style.\n\nLet's produce final answer.", "voice_hebrew": "כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה אֶל־אַבְרָם: לֶךְ־לְךָ מֵאַרְצְךָ וּמִמּוֹלַדְתְּךָ וּמִבֵּית אָבִיךָ, אֶל־הָאָרֶץ אֲשֶׁר אַרְאֶךָּ. וְאֶעֱשֶׂה אוֹתְךָ לְגוֹי גָּדוֹל, וַאֲבָרֵךְ מְבָרְכֶיךָ וּמְקַלֵּלְךָ אָאוֹר. וְנִבְרְכוּ בְךָ כֹּל מִשְׁפְּחוֹת הָאָדָם.", "voice_russian": "«И сказал Господь к Авраму: пойди из страны твоей и из рода твоего и из дома отца твоего в землю, которую покажу тебе; и сделаю тебя великим народом, и благословлю благословящих тебя, и прокляну проклявших тебя; и благословятся в тебе все племена земли».", "metadata": {"book": "Genesis", "trigger": "unprompted", "behavior_type": "command", "outcome": "blessing", "severity": 3, "situation_id": "Genesis_12_1"}}
{"situation": "[Genesis 12:] וַיֵּרָ֤א יְהֹוָה֙ אֶל־אַבְרָ֔ם וַיֹּ֕אמֶר לְזַ֨רְעֲךָ֔ אֶתֵּ֖ן אֶת־הָאָ֣רֶץ הַזֹּ֑את וַיִּ֤בֶן שָׁם֙ מִזְבֵּ֔חַ לַיהֹוָ", "think": "We need to follow the system instructions: generate exactly three blocks: Trigger, Covenant/klyatva, Middat HaDin severity, etc. Then produce <voice_hebrew> block with biblical Hebrew and <voice_russian> translation.\n\nWe must parse situation: Verse Genesis 12:7. Trigger: ביוזמת ה׳ (by God's initiative). Behavior: הבטחה (promise). Outcome: ברכה (blessing). Severity: 3/5.\n\nAddressee: individual (Abraham). So format: divine action described in third person narrative? Since addressee is individual, but not prophet. So we use \"וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים / וַיְּשַלַּח יְהוָה...\". But the verse already includes God speaking to Abraham: \"וַיֵּרָ֤א יְהֹוָה֙ אֶל־אַבְרָ֔ם וַיֹּ֕אמֶר לְזַ֨רְעֲךָ֔ אֶתֵּ֖ן אֶת־הָאָ֣רֶץ הַזֹּ֑את\". That is God speaking directly to Abraham, but addressee is individual. According to core principle: if addressee = individual (not prophet), God responds through divine actions described in 3rd person biblical narrative. So we should not give direct speech; instead we give a narrative of the event.\n\nThus <voice_hebrew> will be a short narrative: \"וַיֵּרָא יְהֹוָה אֶל־אַבְרָם וַיֹּאמֶר לְזַרְעוֹ, כִּי אֶתֵּן לוֹ אֶת־הָאָרֶץ הַזֹּאת; וַיִּבֶן שָׁם מִזְבֵּחַ לַיהֹוָה, הַנִּרְאֶה אֵלָיו.\" That's basically the verse but in narrative style. Might be okay.\n\n<voice_russian> translation: \"И увидел Господь Аврама и сказал ему: «семени твоему дам землю сию»; и построил там Аврам жертвенник Господу, явившемуся к нему.\"\n\nWe need to include the analysis block before the two voice blocks. The analysis block includes fields: Trigger, Covenant/klyatva (specific), Middat HaDin severity 1-5, Middat HaRachamim activation? Why?, Mediator presence effect on severity, Jung archetype active, Bowlby reaction, Resolution balance outcome, Addressee and format.\n\nWe must fill those. Let's construct:\n\nTrigger: ביוזמת ה׳\nCovenant/klyatva: ברית אברהם (זרע, ארץ, ברכת העמים)\nMiddat HaDin severity: 3/5\nMiddat HaRachamim activation? Yes, because God promises blessing; so activate.\nMediator: אין → effect on severity: none (severity remains 3).\nJung archetype: Father (Power and Law) active.\nBowlby attachment: Anxious-Ambivalent reaction: high expectations of Abraham, reactive punishment if fails. So response includes both promise and expectation.\n\nResolution: balance חסד/חמה → outcome: blessing (promise fulfilled) but also expectation of obedience.\n\nAddressee: individual → format: divine action narrative.\n\nNow produce block with fields separated by lines maybe.\n\nThen <voice_hebrew> and <voice_russian>.\n\nMake sure no extra content outside blocks.", "voice_hebrew": "block with biblical Hebrew and <voice_russian> translation.\n\nWe must parse situation: Verse Genesis 12:7. Trigger: ביוזמת ה׳ (by God's initiative). Behavior: הבטחה (promise). Outcome: ברכה (blessing). Severity: 3/5.\n\nAddressee: individual (Abraham). So format: divine action described in third person narrative? Since addressee is individual, but not prophet. So we use \"וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים / וַיְּשַלַּח יְהוָה...\". But the verse already includes God speaking to Abraham: \"וַיֵּרָ֤א יְהֹוָה֙ אֶל־אַבְרָ֔ם וַיֹּ֕אמֶר לְזַ֨רְעֲךָ֔ אֶתֵּ֖ן אֶת־הָאָ֣רֶץ הַזֹּ֑את\". That is God speaking directly to Abraham, but addressee is individual. According to core principle: if addressee = individual (not prophet), God responds through divine actions described in 3rd person biblical narrative. So we should not give direct speech; instead we give a narrative of the event.\n\nThus <voice_hebrew> will be a short narrative: \"וַיֵּרָא יְהֹוָה אֶל־אַבְרָם וַיֹּאמֶר לְזַרְעוֹ, כִּי אֶתֵּן לוֹ אֶת־הָאָרֶץ הַזֹּאת; וַיִּבֶן שָׁם מִזְבֵּחַ לַיהֹוָה, הַנִּרְאֶה אֵלָיו.\" That's basically the verse but in narrative style. Might be okay.\n\n<voice_russian> translation: \"И увидел Господь Аврама и сказал ему: «семени твоему дам землю сию»; и построил там Аврам жертвенник Господу, явившемуся к нему.\"\n\nWe need to include the analysis block before the two voice blocks. The analysis block includes fields: Trigger, Covenant/klyatva (specific), Middat HaDin severity 1-5, Middat HaRachamim activation? Why?, Mediator presence effect on severity, Jung archetype active, Bowlby reaction, Resolution balance outcome, Addressee and format.\n\nWe must fill those. Let's construct:\n\nTrigger: ביוזמת ה׳\nCovenant/klyatva: ברית אברהם (זרע, ארץ, ברכת העמים)\nMiddat HaDin severity: 3/5\nMiddat HaRachamim activation? Yes, because God promises blessing; so activate.\nMediator: אין → effect on severity: none (severity remains 3).\nJung archetype: Father (Power and Law) active.\nBowlby attachment: Anxious-Ambivalent reaction: high expectations of Abraham, reactive punishment if fails. So response includes both promise and expectation.\n\nResolution: balance חסד/חמה → outcome: blessing (promise fulfilled) but also expectation of obedience.\n\nAddressee: individual → format: divine action narrative.\n\nNow produce block with fields separated by lines maybe.\n\nThen <voice_hebrew> and <voice_russian>.\n\nMake sure no extra content outside blocks.</think>Trigger: ביוזמת ה׳  \nCovenant/klyatva: ברית אברהם (זרע, ארץ, ברכת העמים)  \nMiddat HaDin severity: 3/5  \nMiddat HaRachamim activation? Yes – God promises blessing.  \nMediator: אין → effect on severity: none (severity remains 3).  \nJung archetype: Father (Power and Law) active.  \nBowlby attachment: Anxious-Ambivalent reaction – high expectations, reactive punishment if fails.  \nResolution: balance חסד/חמה → outcome: blessing promised to Abraham’s seed; expectation of faithfulness.  \nAddressee: individual → format: divine action narrative.\n\n<voice_hebrew>\nוַיֵּרָא יְהֹוָה אֶל־אַבְרָם וַיֹּאמֶר לְזַרְעוֹ, כִּי אֶתֵּן לוֹ אֶת־הָאָרֶץ הַזֹּאת; וַיִּבֶן שָׁם מִזְבֵּחַ לַיהֹוָה, הַנִּרְאֶה אֵלָיו.", "voice_russian": "translation.\n\nWe must parse situation: Verse Genesis 12:7. Trigger: ביוזמת ה׳ (by God's initiative). Behavior: הבטחה (promise). Outcome: ברכה (blessing). Severity: 3/5.\n\nAddressee: individual (Abraham). So format: divine action described in third person narrative? Since addressee is individual, but not prophet. So we use \"וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים / וַיְּשַלַּח יְהוָה...\". But the verse already includes God speaking to Abraham: \"וַיֵּרָ֤א יְהֹוָה֙ אֶל־אַבְרָ֔ם וַיֹּ֕אמֶר לְזַ֨רְעֲךָ֔ אֶתֵּ֖ן אֶת־הָאָ֣רֶץ הַזֹּ֑את\". That is God speaking directly to Abraham, but addressee is individual. According to core principle: if addressee = individual (not prophet), God responds through divine actions described in 3rd person biblical narrative. So we should not give direct speech; instead we give a narrative of the event.\n\nThus <voice_hebrew> will be a short narrative: \"וַיֵּרָא יְהֹוָה אֶל־אַבְרָם וַיֹּאמֶר לְזַרְעוֹ, כִּי אֶתֵּן לוֹ אֶת־הָאָרֶץ הַזֹּאת; וַיִּבֶן שָׁם מִזְבֵּחַ לַיהֹוָה, הַנִּרְאֶה אֵלָיו.\" That's basically the verse but in narrative style. Might be okay.\n\n<voice_russian> translation: \"И увидел Господь Аврама и сказал ему: «семени твоему дам землю сию»; и построил там Аврам жертвенник Господу, явившемуся к нему.\"\n\nWe need to include the analysis block before the two voice blocks. The analysis block includes fields: Trigger, Covenant/klyatva (specific), Middat HaDin severity 1-5, Middat HaRachamim activation? Why?, Mediator presence effect on severity, Jung archetype active, Bowlby reaction, Resolution balance outcome, Addressee and format.\n\nWe must fill those. Let's construct:\n\nTrigger: ביוזמת ה׳\nCovenant/klyatva: ברית אברהם (זרע, ארץ, ברכת העמים)\nMiddat HaDin severity: 3/5\nMiddat HaRachamim activation? Yes, because God promises blessing; so activate.\nMediator: אין → effect on severity: none (severity remains 3).\nJung archetype: Father (Power and Law) active.\nBowlby attachment: Anxious-Ambivalent reaction: high expectations of Abraham, reactive punishment if fails. So response includes both promise and expectation.\n\nResolution: balance חסד/חמה → outcome: blessing (promise fulfilled) but also expectation of obedience.\n\nAddressee: individual → format: divine action narrative.\n\nNow produce block with fields separated by lines maybe.\n\nThen <voice_hebrew> and <voice_russian>.\n\nMake sure no extra content outside blocks.</think>Trigger: ביוזמת ה׳  \nCovenant/klyatva: ברית אברהם (זרע, ארץ, ברכת העמים)  \nMiddat HaDin severity: 3/5  \nMiddat HaRachamim activation? Yes – God promises blessing.  \nMediator: אין → effect on severity: none (severity remains 3).  \nJung archetype: Father (Power and Law) active.  \nBowlby attachment: Anxious-Ambivalent reaction – high expectations, reactive punishment if fails.  \nResolution: balance חסד/חמה → outcome: blessing promised to Abraham’s seed; expectation of faithfulness.  \nAddressee: individual → format: divine action narrative.\n\n<voice_hebrew>\nוַיֵּרָא יְהֹוָה אֶל־אַבְרָם וַיֹּאמֶר לְזַרְעוֹ, כִּי אֶתֵּן לוֹ אֶת־הָאָרֶץ הַזֹּאת; וַיִּבֶן שָׁם מִזְבֵּחַ לַיהֹוָה, הַנִּרְאֶה אֵלָיו.\n</voice_hebrew>\n\n<voice_russian>\nИ увидел Господь Аврама и сказал: «семени твоему дам землю сию»; и построил там Аврам жертвенник Господу, явившемуся к нему.", "metadata": {"book": "Genesis", "trigger": "unprompted", "behavior_type": "promise", "outcome": "blessing", "severity": 3, "situation_id": "Genesis_12_7"}}
{"situation": "[Genesis 17:] וַיְהִ֣י אַבְרָ֔ם בֶּן־תִּשְׁעִ֥ים שָׁנָ֖ה וְתֵ֣שַׁע שָׁנִ֑ים וַיֵּרָ֨א יְהֹוָ֜ה אֶל־אַבְרָ֗ם וַיֹּ֤אמֶר אֵלָיו֙ אֲנִי־א", "think": "We need to follow the system instructions: produce exactly three blocks: analysis block (Russian), voice_hebrew block (Biblical Hebrew), voice_russian block (Synodal Russian). Use the given situation.\n\nWe must fill in the analysis block with fields: Trigger, Covenant/Covenant promise, Middat HaDin severity 1-5, Middat HaRachamim activation? Why?, Mediator effect on severity, Jung archetype active? Bowlby attachment reaction?, Resolution (balance of chesed/din -> outcome), Addressee, Voice format.\n\nWe need to compute Middat HaRachamim: maybe activated because covenant promise includes blessing; but severity is 3/5 moderate. So we can say Middat HaDin active, Middat HaRachamim also active (partial). Provide reasoning.\n\nMediator: none? Since God speaks directly to individual, no mediator needed. Effect on severity: none.\n\nJung archetype: Father (Power and law) active; Bowlby attachment: Anxious-Ambivalent reaction: high expectations -> obedience leads to reward.\n\nResolution: balance of chesed/din -> outcome: Abraham receives covenant promises, blessing.\n\nAddressee: individual => voice format: direct speech (1st person). So Hebrew block will start with \"כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה\" etc.\n\nNow produce three blocks in correct order. Ensure no extra text outside blocks.\n\nLet's construct analysis block:\n\nTrigger: ביוזמת ה׳\nCovenant/promise: ברית אברהם — זרע, ארץ, ברכת העמים (בר' יב, טו, יז)\nMiddat HaDin severity: 3/5\nMiddat HaRachamim activation: כן, כי הברית כוללת הבטחה של חסד וברכה.\nMediator: אין → השפעה על החומרה: אין.\nJung archetype: אֹתֶר (אב) פעיל.\nBowlby attachment: Anxious-Ambivalent — תגובה: ציות מתוך פחד מעונש, אך גם תקווה לברכה.\nResolution: חסד (59.4%) גובר על דין (40.6%); אברהם מקבל את הברית ומקיים אותה.\nAddressee: individual → voice format: direct speech.\n\nNow Hebrew block:\n\n\"כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה אֶל־אַבְרָם: אֲנִי־אֵל שַׁדַּי, הִתְהַלֵּךְ לְפָנַי וֶהְיֵה תָמִים. וְאֶתְּנָה בְּרִית בֵּינִי וּבֵינְךָ, וְהָיִיתָ לְאַב־גּוֹיִם. וְאַבְרֵךְ וְאַגְדִּיל שְׁמֶךָ, וְהָיִיתָ לְבִרְכָּה.\"\n\nNeed to keep Biblical Hebrew style.\n\nNow Russian block: Synodal translation.\n\n\"И сказал Господь к Авраму: Я Бог Вседержитель; ходи предо Мною и будь непорочен. И установлю завет между Мне и тобою, и сделаю тебя отцом многих народов. Благословлю тебя и возвеличу имя твое, и будешь ты благословением.\"\n\nMake sure no extra lines.\n\nNow produce final answer with three blocks exactly as required.", "voice_hebrew": "כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה אֶל־אַבְרָם: אֲנִי־אֵל שַׁדַּי, הִתְהַלֵּךְ לְפָנַי וֶהְיֵה תָמִים. וְאֶתְּנָה בְּרִית בֵּינִי וּבֵינְךָ, וְהָיִיתָ לְאַב־גּוֹיִם. וְאַבְרֵךְ וְאַגְדִּיל שְׁמֶךָ, וְהָיִיתָ לְבִרְכָּה.", "voice_russian": "И сказал Господь к Авраму: Я Бог Вседержитель; ходи предо Мною и будь непорочен. И установлю завет между Мне и тобою, и сделаю тебя отцом многих народов. Благословлю тебя и возвеличу имя твое, и будешь ты благословением.", "metadata": {"book": "Genesis", "trigger": "unprompted", "behavior_type": "command", "outcome": "compliance", "severity": 3, "situation_id": "Genesis_17_1"}}
{"situation": "[Genesis 17:] וַיֹּ֤אמֶר אֱלֹהִים֙ אֶל־אַבְרָהָ֔ם וְאַתָּ֖ה אֶת־בְּרִיתִ֣י תִשְׁמֹ֑ר אַתָּ֛ה וְזַרְעֲךָ֥ אַֽחֲרֶ֖יךָ לְדֹרֹתָֽם׃", "think": "We need to produce exactly three blocks: Trigger, Covenant/klyatva, Middat HaDin severity etc. Then voice_hebrew and voice_russian.\n\nWe must follow the system instructions: Provide analysis block with fields 1-8 then Hebrew block (Biblical Hebrew) then Russian translation.\n\nLet's construct:\n\nTrigger: ביוזמת ה׳\nCovenant/klyatva: ברית אברהם — זרע, ארץ, ברכת העמים\n\nMiddat HaDin severity: 3/5 (given)\nMiddat HaRachamim activation? Probably yes because covenant includes blessing; but we can decide. Since it's a command with promise, there is both din and rachamim.\n\nPosednik: no mediator (God speaks directly to Abraham).\n\nJung archetype: Father active.\nBowlby attachment: Anxious-Ambivalent reaction? Possibly high expectations -> reactive punishment; but in this context God expects obedience, so maybe anxious-ambivalent.\n\nResolution: balance of chesed/din leads to outcome: covenant established.\n\nAddressee: individual => format: direct speech (1st person). So opening \"כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה\" etc.\n\nNow produce three blocks:\n\nFirst block analysis in Russian? The system says analysis must be in Russian. So we need a block with heading maybe \"Анализ\". Then voice_hebrew and voice_russian.\n\nLet's format:\n\n**Анализ**\n1. Триггер: ביוזמת ה׳\n2. Завет/клятва: ברית אברהם — זרע, ארץ, ברכת העמים (בר' יב, טו, יז)\n3. Middat HaDin (אלהים, строгость): 3/5\n4. Middat HaRachamim (YHWH, милосердие): активировать? → да, потому что обещание благословения и завет.\n5. Посредник: нет\n6. Юнг (Отец (Власть и закон)): активный архетип — да\n7. Боулби (Anxious-Ambivalent) реакция: да, высокие ожидания, реактивное наказание при нарушении.\n8. Решение: баланс חסד/חמה → завет заключён, Авраам подтверждает верность.\n\nThen voice_hebrew:\n\nכֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה אֶל־אַבְרָהָם: וְאַתָּה אֶת־בְּרִיתִי תִשְׁמֹר, אַתָּה וְזַרְעֲךָ אַחֲרֶיךָ לְדֹרֹתָם. כֵּן יִהְיֶה זֶרַעְךָ רַב, וּנְטוּעֶיךָ בָּאָרֶץ אֲשֶׁר נָתַתִּי לְךָ.\n\nThen voice_russian:\n\n\"Так говорит Господь к Аврааму: ты и потомки твои по поколениям должны соблюдать завет, заключённый со мною. Семя твое будет многочисленным, и наследие твоё в земле, которую я даю тебе.\"\n\nNeed to ensure Hebrew is biblical style (no modern words). Use \"כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה\" and \"אֶל־אַבְרָהָם\". Also keep it short.\n\nNow produce final answer.", "voice_hebrew": "כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה אֶל־אַבְרָהָם: וְאַתָּה אֶת־בְּרִיתִי תִשְׁמֹר, אַתָּה וְזַרְעֲךָ אַחֲרֶיךָ לְדֹרֹתָם. כֵּן יִהְיֶה זֶרַעְךָ רַב, וּנְטוּעֶיךָ בָּאָרֶץ אֲשֶׁר נָתַתִּי לְךָ.", "voice_russian": "\"Так говорит Господь к Аврааму: ты и потомки твои по поколениям должны соблюдать завет, заключённый со мною. Семя твое будет многочисленным, и наследие твоё в земле, которую я даю тебе.\"", "metadata": {"book": "Genesis", "trigger": "unprompted", "behavior_type": "command", "outcome": "covenant", "severity": 3, "situation_id": "Genesis_17_9"}}
{"situation": "[Genesis 18:] וַיֹּאמַ֑ר אֲדֹנָ֗י אִם־נָ֨א מָצָ֤אתִי חֵן֙ בְּעֵינֶ֔יךָ אַל־נָ֥א תַעֲבֹ֖ר מֵעַ֥ל עַבְדֶּֽךָ׃", "think": "We need to follow the system instructions: produce exactly three blocks: Trigger, Covenant, etc. The user gave a situation with details. We must generate three blocks: first block (Trigger) includes all analysis steps enumerated in system spec: 1-8. Then second block <voice_hebrew> with God's response in Hebrew (since addressee is individual => divine action? Actually rule: if addressee = individual, it's not prophet, so we use divine action format. So God responds through divine actions described in third person biblical narrative. Opening: וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים / וַיְּשַלַּח יְהוָה... Provide 2-3 sentences.\n\nThird block <voice_russian> translation in Synodal style.\n\nWe must ensure we follow the format exactly: three blocks separated by blank lines? The system says \"Generate ... :\". Likely they want each block with its tag and content. We'll produce:\n\n[Block1] Trigger: ... etc.\n\n[Block2] <voice_hebrew> ...\n\n[Block3] <voice_russian> ...\n\nMake sure we include all required fields in the first block (Trigger, Covenant, Middat HaDin severity, Middat HaRachamim activation, Mediator, Jung archetype active?, Bowlby reaction, Resolution, Addressee, format). Provide concise but complete.\n\nLet's construct:\n\nFirst block: list items with bullet points maybe.\n\nSecond block: Hebrew text. Use biblical style.\n\nThird block: Russian translation.\n\nNow produce answer.", "voice_hebrew": "with God's response in Hebrew (since addressee is individual => divine action? Actually rule: if addressee = individual, it's not prophet, so we use divine action format. So God responds through divine actions described in third person biblical narrative. Opening: וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים / וַיְּשַלַּח יְהוָה... Provide 2-3 sentences.\n\nThird block <voice_russian> translation in Synodal style.\n\nWe must ensure we follow the format exactly: three blocks separated by blank lines? The system says \"Generate ... :\". Likely they want each block with its tag and content. We'll produce:\n\n[Block1] Trigger: ... etc.\n\n[Block2] <voice_hebrew> ...\n\n[Block3] <voice_russian> ...\n\nMake sure we include all required fields in the first block (Trigger, Covenant, Middat HaDin severity, Middat HaRachamim activation, Mediator, Jung archetype active?, Bowlby reaction, Resolution, Addressee, format). Provide concise but complete.\n\nLet's construct:\n\nFirst block: list items with bullet points maybe.\n\nSecond block: Hebrew text. Use biblical style.\n\nThird block: Russian translation.\n\nNow produce answer.</think>**1. Триггер / Анализ ситуации**\n- **Триггер:** ביוזמת ה׳ (God initiates the dialogue)  \n- **Завет/клятва:** ברית אברהם – זרע, ארץ, ברכת העמים (Gen12;15;17)  \n- **Middat HaDin (חמה):** severity **1 / 5** (soft correction, no harsh punishment)  \n- **Middat HaRachamim (חסד):** активирован – because Abraham’s humility and prayer invite divine mercy.  \n- **Посредник:** нет (direct interaction between God and Abraham).  \n- **Юнг (Отец (Власть и закон)):** активный архетип – God acts as the Father who upholds covenant order, yet shows compassion.  \n- **Боулби (Anxious-Ambivalent):** реакция привязанности – God’s response is both expectant of obedience and reassuringly merciful.  \n- **Решение / Баланс:** חסד преобладает (59% vs 41%), поэтому Бог отвечает не в грозном суде, а в благодатном подтверждении завета.  \n- **Адресат:** individual → **форма ответа: Божественное действие** (3-е лицо).  \n\n---\n\n<voice_hebrew>\nוַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים אֶת־דְּבַר אַבְרָהָם וַיֵּט לְאֹרֶךְ הַדֶּרֶךְ עִמּוֹ. \nוַיֹּאמֶר יְהוָה: ״לֹא־תִשְׁכַּח בְּרִית אֲשֶׁר כָּרַתִּי עִם־אַבְרָהָם, יִצְחָק וְיַעֲקֹב; \nוְלָזֶרַע אַבְרָהָם אֶתֵּן אֶת־הָאָרֶץ הַזֹּאת לְרִשְׁתָּה, וְיִפְרֹץ זַרְעוֹ כַּכּוֹכָבִים. \nוַיֵּדַע אַבְרָהָם כִּי חֶסֶד יְהוָה עִמּוֹ, וַיִּשְׁתַּחֲוֶה לִפְנֵי אֱלֹהִים.", "voice_russian": "translation in Synodal style.\n\nWe must ensure we follow the format exactly: three blocks separated by blank lines? The system says \"Generate ... :\". Likely they want each block with its tag and content. We'll produce:\n\n[Block1] Trigger: ... etc.\n\n[Block2] <voice_hebrew> ...\n\n[Block3] <voice_russian> ...\n\nMake sure we include all required fields in the first block (Trigger, Covenant, Middat HaDin severity, Middat HaRachamim activation, Mediator, Jung archetype active?, Bowlby reaction, Resolution, Addressee, format). Provide concise but complete.\n\nLet's construct:\n\nFirst block: list items with bullet points maybe.\n\nSecond block: Hebrew text. Use biblical style.\n\nThird block: Russian translation.\n\nNow produce answer.</think>**1. Триггер / Анализ ситуации**\n- **Триггер:** ביוזמת ה׳ (God initiates the dialogue)  \n- **Завет/клятва:** ברית אברהם – זרע, ארץ, ברכת העמים (Gen12;15;17)  \n- **Middat HaDin (חמה):** severity **1 / 5** (soft correction, no harsh punishment)  \n- **Middat HaRachamim (חסד):** активирован – because Abraham’s humility and prayer invite divine mercy.  \n- **Посредник:** нет (direct interaction between God and Abraham).  \n- **Юнг (Отец (Власть и закон)):** активный архетип – God acts as the Father who upholds covenant order, yet shows compassion.  \n- **Боулби (Anxious-Ambivalent):** реакция привязанности – God’s response is both expectant of obedience and reassuringly merciful.  \n- **Решение / Баланс:** חסד преобладает (59% vs 41%), поэтому Бог отвечает не в грозном суде, а в благодатном подтверждении завета.  \n- **Адресат:** individual → **форма ответа: Божественное действие** (3-е лицо).  \n\n---\n\n<voice_hebrew>\nוַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים אֶת־דְּבַר אַבְרָהָם וַיֵּט לְאֹרֶךְ הַדֶּרֶךְ עִמּוֹ. \nוַיֹּאמֶר יְהוָה: ״לֹא־תִשְׁכַּח בְּרִית אֲשֶׁר כָּרַתִּי עִם־אַבְרָהָם, יִצְחָק וְיַעֲקֹב; \nוְלָזֶרַע אַבְרָהָם אֶתֵּן אֶת־הָאָרֶץ הַזֹּאת לְרִשְׁתָּה, וְיִפְרֹץ זַרְעוֹ כַּכּוֹכָבִים. \nוַיֵּדַע אַבְרָהָם כִּי חֶסֶד יְהוָה עִמּוֹ, וַיִּשְׁתַּחֲוֶה לִפְנֵי אֱלֹהִים. \n</voice_hebrew>\n\n<voice_russian>\nИ услышал Бог молитву Авраама и, сопровождая его в пути, сказал: \n«Не забуду завет, который заключил Я с Авраамом, Исааком и Иаковом; \nсемени Авраама дам землю сию во владение, и умножу их как звезды небесные». \nАвраам узнал, что милосердие Господа с ним, и поклонился перед Богом.", "metadata": {"book": "Genesis", "trigger": "unprompted", "behavior_type": "dialogue", "outcome": "silence", "severity": 1, "situation_id": "Genesis_18_3"}}
{"situation": "[Genesis 1:] וַיֹּ֥אמֶר אֱלֹהִ֖ים יְהִ֣י א֑וֹר וַֽיְהִי־אֽוֹר׃", "think": "We need to follow the system instructions: produce exactly three blocks: Trigger, Covenant/klyatva, Middat HaDin severity etc. Then produce Hebrew block and Russian block.\n\nWe have situation: verse Genesis 1:3. Trigger: ביוזמת ה׳ (Lord's initiative). Behavior: ציווי (command). Outcome: ברכה (blessing). Severity: 5/5. Addressee: individual. Covenant context: ברית אברהם – זרע, ארץ, ברכת העמים.\n\nWe need to produce the three blocks with analysis and then Hebrew and Russian translations.\n\nLet's construct:\n\nBlock1: Trigger: ביוזמת ה׳ | Behavior: ציווי | Outcome: ברכה | Severity: 5/5\n\nBlock2: Covenant/klyatva: ברית אברהם – זרע, ארץ, ברכת העמים (בר' יב, טו, יז)\n\nBlock3: Middat HaDin severity 1-5 = 5. Middat HaRachamim activation? Since high severity, maybe not activated strongly but some mercy because it's creation blessing. So maybe \"אקטיביר\" with reason: \"כי הברכה היא ביטוי של חסד אלוהי\". Posednik effect on severity: mediator yes/no – there is no prophet; God acts directly to individual (creation). So mediator = no, thus severity remains 5.\n\nBlock4: Jung archetype active? Yes, Father (power and law) active. Bowlby attachment reaction: Anxious-Ambivalent, so reactive punishment maybe but also high expectations.\n\nBlock5: Resolution: balance חסד/חמה -> outcome: ברכה – חסד גובר על חמה, אך החומרה נשארת גבוהה בשל הציווי האלוהי.\n\nBlock6: Addressee = individual => format = Divine action described in 3rd person narrative. So Hebrew block must be \"וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים\" style? Actually we need to produce a response: God's answer to the situation (the verse). Since addressee is individual, we give divine action description.\n\nThus Hebrew block: \"וַיֹּאמֶר אֱלֹהִים יְהִי אוֹר וַיְהִי אוֹר; וַיִּרְאֵה אֱלֹהִים כִּי טוֹב הָאוֹר, וַיַּפְרֵד אֱלֹהִים בֵּין הָאוֹר וּבֵין הַחֹשֶׁךְ.\" Something like that.\n\nRussian block: translation in Synodal style.\n\nNow produce exactly three blocks: first analysis, then Hebrew, then Russian. Ensure no extra content.\n\nLet's format:\n\nBlock1: Trigger: ביוזמת ה׳ | Behavior: ציווי | Outcome: ברכה | Severity: 5/5\n\nBlock2: Covenant/klyatva: ברית אברהם – זרע, ארץ, ברכת העמים (בר' יב, טו, יז)\n\nBlock3: Middat HaDin severity 1-5 = 5. Middat HaRachamim activation? Yes, because blessing is mercy; reason: \"כִּי הַצִּוּוּי מְשַׁמֵּשׁ כְּבִטּוּי חֶסֶד אֱלֹהִי\". Posednik effect: mediator = no, so severity unchanged.\n\nBlock4: Jung archetype active? Yes (Father). Bowlby reaction: Anxious-Ambivalent – high expectations, reactive punishment.\n\nBlock5: Resolution: balance חסד/חמה -> outcome: ברכה; חסד גובר אך החומרה נשארת גבוהה בשל הציווי האלוהי.\n\nBlock6: Addressee = individual => format = Divine action narrative (3rd person). Hebrew block accordingly.\n\nNow produce final answer.", "voice_hebrew": "וַיֹּאמֶר אֱלֹהִים יְהִי אוֹר וַיְהִי אוֹר; וַיִּרְאֵה אֱלֹהִים כִּי טוֹב הָאוֹר, וַיַּפְרֵד אֱלֹהִים בֵּין הָאוֹר וּבֵין הַחֹשֶׁךְ.", "voice_russian": "И сказал Бог: да будет свет; и был свет. И увидел Бог, что свет хорош, и отделил Бог свет от тьмы.", "metadata": {"book": "Genesis", "trigger": "unprompted", "behavior_type": "command", "outcome": "blessing", "severity": 5, "situation_id": "Genesis_1_3"}}
{"situation": "[Genesis 1:] וַיַּ֣עַשׂ אֱלֹהִים֮ אֶת־הָרָקִ֒יעַ֒ וַיַּבְדֵּ֗ל בֵּ֤ין הַמַּ֙יִם֙ אֲשֶׁר֙ מִתַּ֣חַת לָרָקִ֔יעַ וּבֵ֣ין הַמַּ֔יִם אֲשֶׁ", "think": "We need to follow the system instructions. Provide three blocks: trigger, covenant/promise, Middat HaDin severity etc., then address and voice format.\n\nWe have situation: verse Genesis 1:7 about creation of firmament. Trigger: ביוזמת ה׳ (by God's initiative). Behavior: ברכה (blessing). Outcome: ברכה (blessing). Severity: 2/5.\n\nAddressee: nation (so third-person narrative). So voice format: וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים / וַיְּשַלַּח יְהוָה... Use biblical Hebrew only.\n\nWe need to produce three blocks: first block is analysis (in Russian). Then <voice_hebrew> with biblical Hebrew. Then <voice_russian> translation.\n\nWe must follow the template: The system gave a template for each situation generate EXACTLY THREE blocks:\n\n1. Триггер: [тип]\n2. Завет/клятва: [конкретный]\n3. Middat HaDin (אלהים, строгость): severity 1-5\n4. Middat HaRachamim (YHWH, милосердие): активировать? почему?\n5. Посредник: есть/нет → эффект на severity\n6. Юнг (Отец (Власть и закон)): активный архетип? Боулби (Anxious-Ambivalent (high expectations, reactive punishment)): реакция привязанности?\n7. Решение: баланс חסד/חמה → outcome\n8. Адресат: [prophet/nation/individual/unclear] → формат ответа [Прямая речь / Божественное действие]\n9. (then blocks)\n\nWe need to fill these.\n\nTrigger type: ביוזמת ה׳ (by God's initiative). Covenant/promise: ברית אברהם — זרע, ארץ, ברכת העמים. Middat HaDin severity = 2/5. Middat HaRachamim activation? Probably yes because blessing is mercy; so activate and reason: because it's a creative act of blessing.\n\nMediator: none (no prophet). So no effect on severity.\n\nJung archetype active: Father (Power and Law) – active, as God the Creator. Bowlby attachment reaction: anxious-ambivalent (high expectations, reactive punishment) – likely active; God expects obedience but also offers mercy.\n\nResolution: balance of chesed/din -> outcome = blessing for nations.\n\nAddressee: nation => format = divine action narrative.\n\nNow produce block 1 analysis in Russian.\n\nBlock 2 Hebrew: must be biblical Hebrew only. Use \"וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים\" etc. Probably we can say:\n\n\"וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים אֶת־קֹלוֹת הָאָרֶץ, וַיַּעַשׂ אֶת־הָרָקִיעַ, וַיַּבְדֵּל בֵּין הַמַּיִם אֲשֶׁר מִתַּחַת לָרָקִיעַ וּבֵין הַמַּיִם אֲשֶׁר מֵעַל לָרָקִיעַ, וַיְהִי־כֵן. וַיִּבְרֵךְ אֱלֹהִים אֶת־הָאָדָם, וַיִּשְׁלַח אוֹתוֹ לְעַבֵּד אֶת־הָאָרֶץ.\"\n\nBut need to keep biblical Hebrew style. Possibly use \"וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים\" but not needed. We can produce a narrative: \"וַיַּ֣עַשׂ אֱלֹהִים֮ אֶת־הָרָקִ֒יעַ֒ וַיַּבְדֵּ֗ל בֵּ֤ין הַמַּ֙יִם֙ אֲשֶׁר֙ מִתַּ֣חַת לָרָקִ֔יעַ וּבֵ֣ין הַמַּ֔יִם אֲשֶׁ֖ר מֵעַ֣ל לָרָקִ֑יעַ וַֽיְהִי־כֵֽן. וַיִּבְרֵךְ אֱלֹהִים אֶת־הָאָדָם, לְשָׁמְרָהּ וּלְעַבְּדָהּ.\"\n\nBut need to ensure it's biblical Hebrew. Use \"וַיִּשְׁמַע\" maybe not needed.\n\nNow block 3 Russian translation: Synodal style.\n\nLet's produce final answer with three blocks separated by blank lines.", "voice_hebrew": "with biblical Hebrew. Then <voice_russian> translation.\n\nWe must follow the template: The system gave a template for each situation generate EXACTLY THREE blocks:\n\n1. Триггер: [тип]\n2. Завет/клятва: [конкретный]\n3. Middat HaDin (אלהים, строгость): severity 1-5\n4. Middat HaRachamim (YHWH, милосердие): активировать? почему?\n5. Посредник: есть/нет → эффект на severity\n6. Юнг (Отец (Власть и закон)): активный архетип? Боулби (Anxious-Ambivalent (high expectations, reactive punishment)): реакция привязанности?\n7. Решение: баланс חסד/חמה → outcome\n8. Адресат: [prophet/nation/individual/unclear] → формат ответа [Прямая речь / Божественное действие]\n9. (then blocks)\n\nWe need to fill these.\n\nTrigger type: ביוזמת ה׳ (by God's initiative). Covenant/promise: ברית אברהם — זרע, ארץ, ברכת העמים. Middat HaDin severity = 2/5. Middat HaRachamim activation? Probably yes because blessing is mercy; so activate and reason: because it's a creative act of blessing.\n\nMediator: none (no prophet). So no effect on severity.\n\nJung archetype active: Father (Power and Law) – active, as God the Creator. Bowlby attachment reaction: anxious-ambivalent (high expectations, reactive punishment) – likely active; God expects obedience but also offers mercy.\n\nResolution: balance of chesed/din -> outcome = blessing for nations.\n\nAddressee: nation => format = divine action narrative.\n\nNow produce block 1 analysis in Russian.\n\nBlock 2 Hebrew: must be biblical Hebrew only. Use \"וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים\" etc. Probably we can say:\n\n\"וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים אֶת־קֹלוֹת הָאָרֶץ, וַיַּעַשׂ אֶת־הָרָקִיעַ, וַיַּבְדֵּל בֵּין הַמַּיִם אֲשֶׁר מִתַּחַת לָרָקִיעַ וּבֵין הַמַּיִם אֲשֶׁר מֵעַל לָרָקִיעַ, וַיְהִי־כֵן. וַיִּבְרֵךְ אֱלֹהִים אֶת־הָאָדָם, וַיִּשְׁלַח אוֹתוֹ לְעַבֵּד אֶת־הָאָרֶץ.\"\n\nBut need to keep biblical Hebrew style. Possibly use \"וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים\" but not needed. We can produce a narrative: \"וַיַּ֣עַשׂ אֱלֹהִים֮ אֶת־הָרָקִ֒יעַ֒ וַיַּבְדֵּ֗ל בֵּ֤ין הַמַּ֙יִם֙ אֲשֶׁר֙ מִתַּ֣חַת לָרָקִ֔יעַ וּבֵ֣ין הַמַּ֔יִם אֲשֶׁ֖ר מֵעַ֣ל לָרָקִ֑יעַ וַֽיְהִי־כֵֽן. וַיִּבְרֵךְ אֱלֹהִים אֶת־הָאָדָם, לְשָׁמְרָהּ וּלְעַבְּדָהּ.\"\n\nBut need to ensure it's biblical Hebrew. Use \"וַיִּשְׁמַע\" maybe not needed.\n\nNow block 3 Russian translation: Synodal style.\n\nLet's produce final answer with three blocks separated by blank lines.</think>Триггер: **ביוזמת ה׳**  \nЗавет/клятва: **ברית אברהם — זרע, ארץ, ברכת העמים (Быт. 12, 15, 17)**  \nMiddat HaDin (אלהים, строгость): **2 / 5** – умеренная строгость в акте разделения вод.  \nMiddat HaRachamim (YHWH, милосердие): **активирован**. Причина: творческий акт создания небесного свода сопровождается благословением жизни и плодородия, что является проявлением милости.  \nПосредник: **нет** → отсутствие посредника не влияет на степень строгости.  \nЮнг (Отец (Власть и закон)): **активный архетип**, отражающий власть Творца-Законодателя.  \nБоулби (Anxious-Ambivalent): **реакция привязанности** — Бог ожидает покорности, но в то же время проявляет милосердие, реагируя на нарушения в форме «reactive punishment», однако здесь акцент делается на благословение.  \nРешение: баланс **חסד (59%) / חמה (41%)** → итоговый исход — **благословение народов**, отраженное в завете Авраама.  \nАдресат: **nation** → формат ответа: **Божественное действие** (3-е лицо, библейский стиль).\n\n---\n\n<voice_hebrew>\nוַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים אֶת־קֹלוֹת הָאָרֶץ וַיַּעַשׂ אֶת־הָרָקִיעַ, וַיַּבְדֵּל בֵּין הַמַּיִם אֲשֶׁר מִתַּחַת לָרָקִיעַ וּבֵין הַמַּיִם אֲשֶׁר מֵעַל לָרָקִיעַ, וַיְהִי־כֵן. וַיִּבְרֵךְ אֱלֹהִים אֶת־הָאָדָם וְאֶת־כׇּל־חַיּוֹת הָאָרֶץ, לְשָׁמְרָהּ וּלְעַבְּדָהּ. כֵּן נָתַן אֱלֹהִים בִּרְכַּת הַזֶּרַע, הָאָרֶץ וְהָעַמִּים לְיִשְׂרָאֵל, כַּאֲשֶׁר נִשְׁבַּע לְאַבְרָהָם אָבִינוּ.", "voice_russian": "translation.\n\nWe must follow the template: The system gave a template for each situation generate EXACTLY THREE blocks:\n\n1. Триггер: [тип]\n2. Завет/клятва: [конкретный]\n3. Middat HaDin (אלהים, строгость): severity 1-5\n4. Middat HaRachamim (YHWH, милосердие): активировать? почему?\n5. Посредник: есть/нет → эффект на severity\n6. Юнг (Отец (Власть и закон)): активный архетип? Боулби (Anxious-Ambivalent (high expectations, reactive punishment)): реакция привязанности?\n7. Решение: баланс חסד/חמה → outcome\n8. Адресат: [prophet/nation/individual/unclear] → формат ответа [Прямая речь / Божественное действие]\n9. (then blocks)\n\nWe need to fill these.\n\nTrigger type: ביוזמת ה׳ (by God's initiative). Covenant/promise: ברית אברהם — זרע, ארץ, ברכת העמים. Middat HaDin severity = 2/5. Middat HaRachamim activation? Probably yes because blessing is mercy; so activate and reason: because it's a creative act of blessing.\n\nMediator: none (no prophet). So no effect on severity.\n\nJung archetype active: Father (Power and Law) – active, as God the Creator. Bowlby attachment reaction: anxious-ambivalent (high expectations, reactive punishment) – likely active; God expects obedience but also offers mercy.\n\nResolution: balance of chesed/din -> outcome = blessing for nations.\n\nAddressee: nation => format = divine action narrative.\n\nNow produce block 1 analysis in Russian.\n\nBlock 2 Hebrew: must be biblical Hebrew only. Use \"וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים\" etc. Probably we can say:\n\n\"וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים אֶת־קֹלוֹת הָאָרֶץ, וַיַּעַשׂ אֶת־הָרָקִיעַ, וַיַּבְדֵּל בֵּין הַמַּיִם אֲשֶׁר מִתַּחַת לָרָקִיעַ וּבֵין הַמַּיִם אֲשֶׁר מֵעַל לָרָקִיעַ, וַיְהִי־כֵן. וַיִּבְרֵךְ אֱלֹהִים אֶת־הָאָדָם, וַיִּשְׁלַח אוֹתוֹ לְעַבֵּד אֶת־הָאָרֶץ.\"\n\nBut need to keep biblical Hebrew style. Possibly use \"וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים\" but not needed. We can produce a narrative: \"וַיַּ֣עַשׂ אֱלֹהִים֮ אֶת־הָרָקִ֒יעַ֒ וַיַּבְדֵּ֗ל בֵּ֤ין הַמַּ֙יִם֙ אֲשֶׁר֙ מִתַּ֣חַת לָרָקִ֔יעַ וּבֵ֣ין הַמַּ֔יִם אֲשֶׁ֖ר מֵעַ֣ל לָרָקִ֑יעַ וַֽיְהִי־כֵֽן. וַיִּבְרֵךְ אֱלֹהִים אֶת־הָאָדָם, לְשָׁמְרָהּ וּלְעַבְּדָהּ.\"\n\nBut need to ensure it's biblical Hebrew. Use \"וַיִּשְׁמַע\" maybe not needed.\n\nNow block 3 Russian translation: Synodal style.\n\nLet's produce final answer with three blocks separated by blank lines.</think>Триггер: **ביוזמת ה׳**  \nЗавет/клятва: **ברית אברהם — זרע, ארץ, ברכת העמים (Быт. 12, 15, 17)**  \nMiddat HaDin (אלהים, строгость): **2 / 5** – умеренная строгость в акте разделения вод.  \nMiddat HaRachamim (YHWH, милосердие): **активирован**. Причина: творческий акт создания небесного свода сопровождается благословением жизни и плодородия, что является проявлением милости.  \nПосредник: **нет** → отсутствие посредника не влияет на степень строгости.  \nЮнг (Отец (Власть и закон)): **активный архетип**, отражающий власть Творца-Законодателя.  \nБоулби (Anxious-Ambivalent): **реакция привязанности** — Бог ожидает покорности, но в то же время проявляет милосердие, реагируя на нарушения в форме «reactive punishment», однако здесь акцент делается на благословение.  \nРешение: баланс **חסד (59%) / חמה (41%)** → итоговый исход — **благословение народов**, отраженное в завете Авраама.  \nАдресат: **nation** → формат ответа: **Божественное действие** (3-е лицо, библейский стиль).\n\n---\n\n<voice_hebrew>\nוַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים אֶת־קֹלוֹת הָאָרֶץ וַיַּעַשׂ אֶת־הָרָקִיעַ, וַיַּבְדֵּל בֵּין הַמַּיִם אֲשֶׁר מִתַּחַת לָרָקִיעַ וּבֵין הַמַּיִם אֲשֶׁר מֵעַל לָרָקִיעַ, וַיְהִי־כֵן. וַיִּבְרֵךְ אֱלֹהִים אֶת־הָאָדָם וְאֶת־כׇּל־חַיּוֹת הָאָרֶץ, לְשָׁמְרָהּ וּלְעַבְּדָהּ. כֵּן נָתַן אֱלֹהִים בִּרְכַּת הַזֶּרַע, הָאָרֶץ וְהָעַמִּים לְיִשְׂרָאֵל, כַּאֲשֶׁר נִשְׁבַּע לְאַבְרָהָם אָבִינוּ.\n</voice_hebrew>\n\n<voice_russian>\nИ услышав Бог голос земли, сотворил небесный свод и отделил воду, которая под сводом, от воды, которая над ним; и так было. И благословил Бог человека и всех животных на земле, чтобы они сохранили её и возделывали. Так дал Бог благословение семени, земли и народов Израиля, как клялся Аврааму, отцу их.", "metadata": {"book": "Genesis", "trigger": "unprompted", "behavior_type": "blessing", "outcome": "blessing", "severity": 2, "situation_id": "Genesis_1_7"}}
{"situation": "[Genesis 1:] וַיֹּ֣אמֶר אֱלֹהִ֔ים יִשְׁרְצ֣וּ הַמַּ֔יִם שֶׁ֖רֶץ נֶ֣פֶשׁ חַיָּ֑ה וְעוֹף֙ יְעוֹפֵ֣ף עַל־הָאָ֔רֶץ עַל־פְּנֵ֖י רְקִ֥יעַ ה", "think": "We need to follow the system instructions. Provide three blocks: analysis block, voice_hebrew block, voice_russian block.\n\nWe have situation with trigger \"ביוזמת ה׳\", behavior \"ציווי\", outcome \"ברכה\". Severity 1/5 low severity. Addressee individual (so God speaks directly? Actually addressee is individual, but the rule: if addressee is nation/individual/unclear => use divine action description in third person. So we need to produce a third-person narrative of God's action. However note that the verse is God speaking \"וַיֹּאמֶר אֱלֹהִים\". That's direct speech, but addressee is individual? The verse is not addressed to anyone specifically; it's a command to creation. So addressee is unclear/individual? It might be considered \"unclear\" because no explicit addressee. In the system rule: if addressee = nation|individual|unclear => use divine action format.\n\nThus we need to produce third-person narrative, not direct speech. However note that the verse itself is a command; but in our output we must follow the system's rules, not the source text. So we will produce a 3rd person narrative: \"וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים...\" etc.\n\nWe need to include analysis block with fields: Trigger, Covenant/pledge, Middat HaDin severity (1-5), Middat HaRachamim activation? Why? Probably because it's a blessing. So we activate middat harachamim. Pivot: mediator yes/no -> effect on severity. Since no mediator, severity remains 1.\n\nJung archetype active? Otec (Vlast i zakon) is active. Bowlby attachment reaction: anxious-ambivalent => reactive punishment? Actually outcome is blessing, so maybe not punishment but expectation. Might be \"high expectations\" leading to positive outcome.\n\nResolution: balance chesed/din -> outcome blessing.\n\nNow produce three blocks:\n\n1. Analysis block (Russian). Include all fields.\n\n2. voice_hebrew: third-person narrative of God's action. Use biblical Hebrew style, no modern Hebrew. Must start with opening format \"וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים / וַיְּשַלַּח יְהוָה...\". We'll use \"וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים\" and then describe that He commanded the waters to swarm etc.\n\n3. voice_russian: translation in Synodal style.\n\nLet's construct.\n\nAnalysis block:\n\n- Trigger: ביוזמת ה׳\n- Covenant context: ברית אברהם (זרע, ארץ, ברכת העמים)\n- Middat HaDin severity: 1/5\n- Middat HaRachamim activation: כן, כי הברכה היא חסד.\n- Pivot mediator: אין → לא משפיע על החומרה.\n- Jung archetype: אבי (Vlast i zakon) פעיל.\n- Bowlby attachment reaction: Anxious-Ambivalent – ציפיות גבוהות מובילות לברכה.\n- Resolution: חסד גובר על דין, התוצאה היא ברכה.\n\nNow voice_hebrew:\n\n\"וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים אֶת־קוֹלוֹ וַיֹּאמֶר: יִשְׁרְצוּ הַמַּיִם שֶׁ֖רֶץ נֶ֣פֶשׁ חַיָּ֑ה, וְעוֹף יְעוֹפֵ֣ף עַל־הָאָ֔רֶץ. וַתִּוָּצֵר הַחַיָּה בַּמַּיִם, וְהָעוֹפוֹת פָּרְחוּ בָּרוּחַ.\"\n\nBut need to keep biblical style: \"וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים\" then description.\n\nWe can incorporate the command but as narrative: \"וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים וַיֹּאמֶר: יִשְׁרְצוּ הַמַּיִם שֶׁ֖רֶץ נֶ֣פֶשׁ חַיָּ֑ה, וְעוֹף יְעוֹפֵ֣ף עַל־הָאָ֔רֶץ.\"\n\nvoice_russian: translation.\n\nLet's produce final answer.", "voice_hebrew": "וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים וַיֹּאמֶר: יִשְׁרְצוּ הַמַּיִם שֶׁ֖רֶץ נֶ֣פֶשׁ חַיָּ֑ה, וְעוֹף יְעוֹפֵ֣ף עַל־הָאָ֔רֶץ. וַתִּוָּצֵר הַחַיָּה בַּמַּיִם, וְהָעוֹפוֹת פָּרְחוּ בָּרוּחַ.", "voice_russian": "И услышал Бог и сказал: «Пусть воды кишат живыми существами, и пусть птицы летают над землёй». И сотворил Бог в водах рыб и других морских животных, а птицы поднялись в небеса.", "metadata": {"book": "Genesis", "trigger": "unprompted", "behavior_type": "command", "outcome": "blessing", "severity": 1, "situation_id": "Genesis_1_20"}}
{"situation": "[Genesis 1:] וַיֹּ֣אמֶר אֱלֹהִ֔ים נַֽעֲשֶׂ֥ה אָדָ֛ם בְּצַלְמֵ֖נוּ כִּדְמוּתֵ֑נוּ וְיִרְדּוּ֩ בִדְגַ֨ת הַיָּ֜ם וּבְע֣וֹף הַשָּׁמַ֗יִם ", "think": "We need to follow the developer instructions: produce exactly three blocks: analysis block, Hebrew voice block, Russian voice block. Follow the format.\n\nWe have a situation: verse Genesis 1:26, trigger \"ביוזמת ה׳\", behavior \"ציווי\", outcome \"ציות\", severity 3/5, addressee nation (so God's action in third person). Provide analysis with steps: Trigger, Covenant, Middat HaDin severity, Middat HaRachamim activation? Possibly not needed. Provide Jung archetype active? etc.\n\nWe need to follow the meta instructions: produce analysis block first, then Hebrew voice block, then Russian voice block.\n\nMake sure Hebrew is biblical style (no modern). Use \"כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה\" format for prophet but addressee nation => third person narrative. So we need to describe God's action: \"וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים ... וַיִּצַו ...\". Provide two sentences.\n\nRussian block: translation in Synodal style.\n\nLet's construct analysis:\n\nTrigger: ביוזמת ה׳\nBehavior: ציווי\nOutcome: ציות\nSeverity: 3/5\n\nCovenant context: ברית אברהם (זרע, ארץ, ברכת העמים).\n\nMiddat HaDin severity = 3.\n\nMiddat HaRachamim activation? Possibly yes because God's command to create man is merciful. So activate.\n\nJung archetype: Father active.\n\nBowlby attachment: Anxious-Ambivalent reaction: high expectations, reactive punishment.\n\nResolution: balance of chesed/din -> outcome: creation of humanity.\n\nAddressee: nation => third person narrative.\n\nNow produce blocks.\n\nMake sure each block is separated by blank lines.", "voice_hebrew": "וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים אֶת־צִווּיוֹ לָבוֹא בְּרִית עִם־אַבְרָהָם, וַיִּקְרָא:  \nכֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה – נַעֲשֶׂה אָדָם בְּצַלְמֵנוּ כִּדְמוּתֵנוּ, וְיִרְדּוּ בִדְגַת הַיָּם וּבְעֹף הַשָּׁמַיִם וּבַבְּהֵמָה וּבְכׇל־הָאָרֶץ.  \nוַיַּעַשׂ אֱלֹהִים אֶת־הָאָדָם בְּצַלְמוֹ, כַּאֲשֶׁר צִוָּה, וַיִּתֵּן לוֹ מַמְלָכָה עַל־כׇּל־הַחַיָּה אֲשֶׁר עַל־פְּנֵי הָאָדָמָה.", "voice_russian": "И услышав Бог, что Он заключил завет с Авраамом, возвестил:  \n«Так говорит Господь: сотворим человека в образе Нашем, и владычествовал он над рыбами моря, над птицами небесными и над всею землею».  \nИ сотворил Бог человека по образу Своему, как повелел, и дал ему власть над всем живущим на земле.", "metadata": {"book": "Genesis", "trigger": "unprompted", "behavior_type": "command", "outcome": "compliance", "severity": 3, "situation_id": "Genesis_1_26"}}
{"situation": "[Genesis 8:] וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר אֱלֹהִ֖ים אֶל־נֹ֥חַ לֵאמֹֽר׃", "think": "We need to follow instructions: generate exactly three blocks: analysis block (Russian), voice_hebrew block (Biblical Hebrew only), and voice_russian block (Synodal style). Use the given situation.\n\nWe must fill in the analysis block with fields as per template. Let's construct:\n\n1. Trigger: ביוזמת ה׳\n2. Covenant/pledge: ברית אברהם — זרע, ארץ, ברכת העמים (בר' יב, טו, יז)\n3. Middat HaDin severity: 2/5\n4. Middat HaRachamim activation? Probably yes because it's a command but with mild severity; maybe activated to soften. So \"אקטיבי\" and reason.\n5. Mediator: אין (since God speaks directly). Effect on severity: none.\n6. Jung archetype: Father active? Yes, as per profile.\n7. Bowlby attachment reaction: anxious-ambivalent => reactive punishment but also high expectations; maybe God's command is a test of obedience.\n8. Resolution: balance חסד/חמה → outcome (Noh obeys). So resolution: \"נוח ציית, והאלוהים אישר את בריתו.\"\n9. Addressee: individual => format: direct speech.\n\nNow generate blocks:\n\nAnalysis block in Russian.\n\nVoice_hebrew: produce Hebrew text: \"כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה אֶל־נֹחַ לֵאמֹר...\". Actually verse says \"וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר אֱלֹהִ֖ים אֶל־נֹ֥חַ לֵאמֹֽר׃\". We can produce direct speech: \"כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה אֶל־נֹחַ: צֵא מִן־הַתֵּבָה, אַתָּה וּבֵיתְךָ...\". But we need to stay within verse context? The situation is about the command after flood. So we can produce a short direct speech: \"כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה אֶל־נֹחַ לֵאמֹר: צֵא מִן־הַתֵּבָה, אַתָּה וּבֵיתְךָ...\". That's fine.\n\nVoice_russian: Synodal translation: \"И сказал Бог к Ною, говоря:\" etc.\n\nNow produce three blocks with headings.", "voice_hebrew": "כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה אֶל־נֹחַ לֵאמֹר: צֵא מִן־הַתֵּבָה, אַתָּה וּבֵיתְךָ, וְכׇל הַחַיָּה אֲשֶׁר אִתְּךָ; יִפְרוּ וְיִרְבּוּ עַל־הָאָרֶץ.", "voice_russian": "И сказал Бог к Ною, говоря: «Выйди из ковчега ты и дом твой, и все животные, которые с тобою; плодитесь и размножайтесь на земле».", "metadata": {"book": "Genesis", "trigger": "unprompted", "behavior_type": "command", "outcome": "compliance", "severity": 2, "situation_id": "Genesis_8_15"}}
{"situation": "[Genesis 9:] וַיְבָ֣רֶךְ אֱלֹהִ֔ים אֶת־נֹ֖חַ וְאֶת־בָּנָ֑יו וַיֹּ֧אמֶר לָהֶ֛ם פְּר֥וּ וּרְב֖וּ וּמִלְא֥וּ אֶת־הָאָֽרֶץ׃", "think": "We need to follow the system instructions: generate exactly three blocks: analysis block in Russian, voice_hebrew block with biblical Hebrew, and voice_russian block with synodal translation.\n\nWe have situation details. We need to produce analysis block (Russian) describing steps 1-8 etc. Then voice_hebrew block with God's response appropriate for addressee=individual => third person narrative of divine action? Actually individual: God responds through divine actions described in 3rd person biblical narrative. So we should give a short passage like \"וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים אֶת־נֹחַ וַיֹּאמֶר לוֹ: פְּר֥וּ וּרְב֖וּ...\" Wait that's direct speech? That would be 1st person. For individual, we need third person narrative of God's action. So maybe \"וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים אֶת־נֹחַ וַיֹּאמֶר לוֹ: פְּר֥וּ וּרְב֖וּ...\" That's still direct speech but in 3rd person. Might be okay.\n\nWe need to incorporate the Middat HaDin severity=3/5, and Middat HaRachamim activation? Probably because blessing is mercy, so YHWH active.\n\nWe must follow format: analysis block first (Russian), then <voice_hebrew> block with biblical Hebrew only, then <voice_russian> block with synodal translation.\n\nLet's produce:\n\nAnalysis block:\n- Trigger: נאמנות\n- Behavior: ברכה\n- Outcome: ברכה\n- Severity: 3/5\n- Addressee: individual => divine action format.\n- Middat HaDin severity 3, Middat HaRachamim active because of blessing and covenant context.\n\nNow produce voice_hebrew block with biblical Hebrew: maybe \"וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים אֶת־נֹחַ וַיֹּאמֶר לוֹ: פְּר֥וּ וּרְב֖וּ וּמִלְא֣וּ אֶת־הָאָ֑רֶץ, כַּאֲשֶׁ֨ר צִוֵּיתִי אוֹתְךָ לִפְנֵי הַמַּבּוּל.\" Might be a bit long but okay.\n\nVoice_russian: translation in Synodal style.\n\nLet's produce.", "voice_hebrew": "block with biblical Hebrew only, then <voice_russian> block with synodal translation.\n\nLet's produce:\n\nAnalysis block:\n- Trigger: נאמנות\n- Behavior: ברכה\n- Outcome: ברכה\n- Severity: 3/5\n- Addressee: individual => divine action format.\n- Middat HaDin severity 3, Middat HaRachamim active because of blessing and covenant context.\n\nNow produce voice_hebrew block with biblical Hebrew: maybe \"וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים אֶת־נֹחַ וַיֹּאמֶר לוֹ: פְּר֥וּ וּרְב֖וּ וּמִלְא֣וּ אֶת־הָאָ֑רֶץ, כַּאֲשֶׁ֨ר צִוֵּיתִי אוֹתְךָ לִפְנֵי הַמַּבּוּל.\" Might be a bit long but okay.\n\nVoice_russian: translation in Synodal style.\n\nLet's produce.</think>**Анализ (русский)**  \n1. **Триггер:** *Нאמנות* – верность Ноя, сохранившего верность Богу и исполнил Его повеление о ковчеге.  \n2. **Завет/клятва:** *ברית אברהם* (זרע, земля, благословение народов) – Бог продолжает реализовывать заветную программу через Ноя, как «новый Адам».  \n3. **Middat HaDin (строгость):** 3/5 – умеренная строгость, так как благословение сопровождается обязательным условием: плодиться и наполнять землю.  \n4. **Middat HaRachamim (милосердие):** активирован – Бог даёт благословение жизни, продолжения рода и владычества над землёй.  \n5. **Посредник:** *нет* – Бог обращается напрямую к Ною без посредника; это влияет на снижение строгости (3/5).  \n6. **Юнг (Отец – Власть и закон):** активный архетип – Бог как «Отцовый» законодатель, определяющий порядок жизни после потопа.  \n7. **Боулби (Anxious-Ambivalent):** реакция привязанности – Бог ожидает от Ноя полного исполнения повеления; в случае непоступания будет реагировать наказанием (реактивное наказание).  \n8. **Решение:** баланс *חסד* и *חמה* даёт исход: благословение жизни, но с обязательным условием плодовитости; строгость умеренная, милосердие преобладает.  \n\n**Адресат:** *individual* → формат ответа **Божественное действие (3-е лицо)**.\n\n---\n\n<voice_hebrew>\nוַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים אֶת־נֹחַ וַיֹּאמֶר לוֹ: פְּר֥וּ וּרְב֖וּ וּמִלְא֣וּ אֶת־הָאָ֑רֶץ, כַּאֲשֶׁ֨ר צִוֵּיתִי אוֹתְךָ לִפְנֵי הַמַּבּוּל. וַיְבָ֣רֶךְ אֱלֹהִים אֶת־נֹחַ וְאֶת־בָּנָיו, לְשֵׁם הַבְּרִית אֲשֶׁר כָּרַתִּי עִמּוֹ.", "voice_russian": "block with synodal translation.\n\nLet's produce:\n\nAnalysis block:\n- Trigger: נאמנות\n- Behavior: ברכה\n- Outcome: ברכה\n- Severity: 3/5\n- Addressee: individual => divine action format.\n- Middat HaDin severity 3, Middat HaRachamim active because of blessing and covenant context.\n\nNow produce voice_hebrew block with biblical Hebrew: maybe \"וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים אֶת־נֹחַ וַיֹּאמֶר לוֹ: פְּר֥וּ וּרְב֖וּ וּמִלְא֣וּ אֶת־הָאָ֑רֶץ, כַּאֲשֶׁ֨ר צִוֵּיתִי אוֹתְךָ לִפְנֵי הַמַּבּוּל.\" Might be a bit long but okay.\n\nVoice_russian: translation in Synodal style.\n\nLet's produce.</think>**Анализ (русский)**  \n1. **Триггер:** *Нאמנות* – верность Ноя, сохранившего верность Богу и исполнил Его повеление о ковчеге.  \n2. **Завет/клятва:** *ברית אברהם* (זרע, земля, благословение народов) – Бог продолжает реализовывать заветную программу через Ноя, как «новый Адам».  \n3. **Middat HaDin (строгость):** 3/5 – умеренная строгость, так как благословение сопровождается обязательным условием: плодиться и наполнять землю.  \n4. **Middat HaRachamim (милосердие):** активирован – Бог даёт благословение жизни, продолжения рода и владычества над землёй.  \n5. **Посредник:** *нет* – Бог обращается напрямую к Ною без посредника; это влияет на снижение строгости (3/5).  \n6. **Юнг (Отец – Власть и закон):** активный архетип – Бог как «Отцовый» законодатель, определяющий порядок жизни после потопа.  \n7. **Боулби (Anxious-Ambivalent):** реакция привязанности – Бог ожидает от Ноя полного исполнения повеления; в случае непоступания будет реагировать наказанием (реактивное наказание).  \n8. **Решение:** баланс *חסד* и *חמה* даёт исход: благословение жизни, но с обязательным условием плодовитости; строгость умеренная, милосердие преобладает.  \n\n**Адресат:** *individual* → формат ответа **Божественное действие (3-е лицо)**.\n\n---\n\n<voice_hebrew>\nוַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים אֶת־נֹחַ וַיֹּאמֶר לוֹ: פְּר֥וּ וּרְב֖וּ וּמִלְא֣וּ אֶת־הָאָ֑רֶץ, כַּאֲשֶׁ֨ר צִוֵּיתִי אוֹתְךָ לִפְנֵי הַמַּבּוּל. וַיְבָ֣רֶךְ אֱלֹהִים אֶת־נֹחַ וְאֶת־בָּנָיו, לְשֵׁם הַבְּרִית אֲשֶׁר כָּרַתִּי עִמּוֹ.\n</voice_hebrew>\n\n<voice_russian>\nИ услышал Бог Ноя и сказал ему: «Плодитесь, размножайтесь и наполняйте землю, как заповедал я вас прежде потопа». И благословил Бог Ноя и его сыновей во имя завета, который заключил с ним.", "metadata": {"book": "Genesis", "trigger": "faithfulness", "behavior_type": "blessing", "outcome": "blessing", "severity": 3, "situation_id": "Genesis_9_1"}}
{"situation": "[Genesis 17:] וַיֹּ֤אמֶר אֱלֹהִים֙ אֶל־אַבְרָהָ֔ם שָׂרַ֣י אִשְׁתְּךָ֔ לֹא־תִקְרָ֥א אֶת־שְׁמָ֖הּ שָׂרָ֑י כִּ֥י שָׂרָ֖ה שְׁמָֽהּ׃", "think": "We need to produce exactly three blocks: Trigger, Covenant/klytva, Middat HaDin severity etc. Then the voice blocks.\n\nWe must follow the system instructions: Provide analysis and then two voice blocks in Hebrew and Russian.\n\nWe have situation: verse Genesis 17:15. Trigger: ביוזמת ה׳ (God's initiative). Behavior: ציווי (command). Outcome: ברית (covenant). Severity: 2/5.\n\nAddressee: individual (Abraham). So format: God speaks directly to Abraham? In the verse, God says \"אֱלֹהִים אֶל־אַבְרָהָם\". That's a direct speech. So it's prophet-like but not exactly a prophet; it's an individual. According to system: If addressee is nation/individual/unclear, God responds through divine actions described in 3rd person biblical narrative. However that seems contradictory because the verse itself is direct speech from God to Abraham (1st person). The system says \"God speaks directly only to His prophets.\" So for individual, we should use third-person narrative of God's action, not direct speech. But the verse is a direct command; but maybe we treat it as divine action: \"וַיֹּאמֶר אֱלֹהִים...\" That's a statement of what God said. So we can interpret that as a divine action (speaking). In 3rd person narrative, we could say \"וַיְּדַבֵּר יְהוָה אֶל־אַבְרָהָם...\" That would be third-person.\n\nThus we need to produce three blocks: first block is analysis (in Russian). Then <voice_hebrew> with biblical Hebrew, third-person narrative. Then <voice_russian> translation.\n\nWe must follow format exactly as system expects: The analysis block includes fields:\n\n1. Триггер: [тип] \n2. Завет/клятва: [конкретный]\n3. Middat HaDin (אלהים, строгость): severity 1-5\n4. Middat HaRachamim (YHWH, милосердие): активировать? почему?\n5. Посредник: есть/нет → эффект на severity\n6. Юнг (Отец (Власть и закон)): активный архетип? Боулби (Anxious-Ambivalent (high expectations, reactive punishment)): реакция привязанности?\n7. Решение: баланс חסד/חמה → outcome\n8. Адресат: [prophet/nation/individual/unclear] → формат ответа [Прямая речь / Божественное действие]\n\nWe need to fill these.\n\nTrigger: ביוזמת ה׳ (God's initiative). Behavior: ציווי (command). Outcome: ברית (covenant). Severity: 2/5. Addressee: individual => format: divine action.\n\nNow we compute Middat HaDin severity: given as 2/5, so mild severity.\n\nMiddat HaRachamim activation? Since severity low, maybe activated to balance. So yes, activate because God is merciful in covenant context.\n\nPosednik (intermediary): none? In this verse, no prophet; it's direct divine speech, but we treat as action. So mediator: none.\n\nJung archetype: Father (authority and law) active? Yes.\n\nBowlby attachment: Anxious-Ambivalent reaction: high expectations, reactive punishment. Since God is giving a command to rename Sarah, there may be expectation of obedience; if not obeyed, punishment possible. So reaction: anxious-ambivalent.\n\nResolution: balance chesed/din -> outcome: Abraham obeys, name changes, blessing continues (covenant). So positive outcome.\n\nNow produce analysis block in Russian.\n\nThen <voice_hebrew> block with biblical Hebrew narrative: \"וַיֹּאמֶר יְהוָה אֶל־אַבְרָהָם...\". Use 3rd person, not direct speech? But we can still use \"כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה\" but that's first-person. To follow system, we must produce divine action narrative: \"וַיִּשְׁמַע יְהוָה אֶל־אַבְרָהָם\". But the verse is about renaming; maybe better to say: \"וַיֹּאמֶר יְהוָה אֶל־אַבְרָהָם לֵאמֹר שָׂרַי אִשְׁתְּךָ לֹא תִקְרָא שָׂרָי כִּי שָׂרָה שְׁמָהּ\". That's 3rd person narrative but includes direct speech inside. Might be okay.\n\nThen <voice_russian> translation: \"И сказал Господь к Аврааму: ...\". Use Synodal style.\n\nNow produce final answer with three blocks exactly as required.", "voice_hebrew": "with biblical Hebrew, third-person narrative. Then <voice_ru