{"situation": "[Genesis 30:] כִּ֡י מְעַט֩ אֲשֶׁר־הָיָ֨ה לְךָ֤ לְפָנַי֙ וַיִּפְרֹ֣ץ לָרֹ֔ב וַיְבָ֧רֶךְ יְהֹוָ֛ה אֹתְךָ֖ לְרַגְלִ֑י וְעַתָּ֗ה מָתַ֛י אֶ", "think": "We need to follow the system instructions: produce exactly three blocks: trigger, covenant/promise, Middat HaDin severity etc. Then voice_hebrew block with direct speech or action depending on addressee (individual => 3rd person narrative). Then voice_russian translation.\n\nWe must include all required fields in the first block? The system says \"Generate <trigger>, <voice_hebrew>, <voice_russian>:\". So we need to produce three blocks: first block is trigger, covenant, severity etc. That's a block with headings. Then voice_hebrew block (with biblical Hebrew). Then voice_russian block.\n\nWe must ensure no extra content outside these blocks.\n\nLet's construct:\n\nBlock 1:\n- Trigger: נאמנות\n- Covenant/promise: ברית אברהם — זרע, ארץ, ברכת העמים (בר' יב, טו, יז)\n- Middat HaDin severity: 3/5\n- Middat HaRachamim activation? Probably yes because God blesses Jacob. So activate.\n- Mediator: no (no prophet). Effect on severity: none.\n- Jung archetype active: Father (Power and Law) → active.\n- Bowlby attachment reaction: Anxious-Ambivalent → reactive punishment? Actually blessing, but still anxious. Might be \"high expectations\" leading to blessing.\n- Resolution: balance chesed/din → outcome: blessing.\n\nBlock 2: voice_hebrew: Since addressee is individual (Jacob), God responds through divine action in third person narrative. Use \"וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים\" style.\n\nWe need to produce a biblical Hebrew statement: maybe \"וַיִּשְׁמַע יְהוָה אֶת תַּחֲנוּנֵי יַעֲקֹב וַיְבָרֶךְ אֹתוֹ\" etc. Must be consistent with verse context: Jacob says \"כי מעט אשר היה לך לפני ויפרץ לרוב... ועתה מתי אעשה גם אנוכי לביתי\". God's response would be blessing.\n\nSo: \"וַיִּשְׁמַע יְהוָה אֶת דִּבְרֵי יַעֲקֹב וַיֹּאמֶר: כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה, הִנֵּה אֲבָרֵךְ אוֹתְךָ וְהִפְרֵיתִי אֶת זַרְעֲךָ כְּכׇכְבֵי הַשָּׁמַיִם וְכַחוֹל אֲשֶׁר עַל