יְמָה לְעֵינֵי פַרְעֹה. וַתְּהִי מַכַּת הַדֶּבֶר בְּאֶרֶץ מִצְרַיִם.\"\n\nNow voice_russian: Synodal translation.\n\nWe must keep three blocks exactly as described. Ensure no extra content outside.\n\nLet's produce final answer.", "voice_hebrew": "וַיֹּאמֶר יְהוָה אֶל־מֹשֶׁה וְאֶל־אַהֲרֹן קְח֣וּ לָכֶם מְלֹא חׇפְנֵיכֶם פִּיחַ כִּבְשָׁן, וּמֹשֶׁה זָרַק אֹתוֹ הַשָּׁמַיְמָה לְעֵינֵי פַרְעֹה. וַתְּהִי מַכַּת הַדֶּבֶר בְּאֶרֶץ מִצְרַיִם.", "voice_russian": "И сказал Господь к Моисею и Аарону: возмите полные горсти пепла из печи, и бросьте его Моисей в небо перед лицем Фараона. И была моровая язва по всей земле Египетской.", "metadata": {"book": "Exodus", "trigger": "unprompted", "behavior_type": "command", "outcome": "punishment", "severity": 4, "situation_id": "Exodus_9_8"}}
{"situation": "[Exodus 9:] וַיֹּ֤אמֶר יְהֹוָה֙ אֶל־מֹשֶׁ֔ה הַשְׁכֵּ֣ם בַּבֹּ֔קֶר וְהִתְיַצֵּ֖ב לִפְנֵ֣י פַרְעֹ֑ה וְאָמַרְתָּ֣ אֵלָ֗יו כֹּֽה־אָמַ֤ר ", "think": "We need to follow the system instructions: produce exactly three blocks: trigger, covenant/covenant oath, Middat HaDin severity etc. Then produce Hebrew block and Russian block.\n\nWe have situation: verse Exodus 9:13. Trigger: מרי (rebellion). Behavior: ציווי (command). Outcome: ציות (obedience). Severity: 3/5.\n\nAddressee: individual (Pharaoh). So God speaks directly to Pharaoh? Actually it's a command to Moses to speak to Pharaoh, but the content is God speaking to Pharaoh. So addressee = individual (Pharaoh). Format = direct speech (since addressee=individual, not nation). So we need direct speech: כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה...\n\nWe must produce three blocks:\n\n1. Analytical block in Russian with fields.\n\n2. Hebrew block with God's response.\n\n3. Russian translation.\n\nWe need to follow the template exactly as described.\n\nLet's construct analytical block.\n\nTrigger: מרי\n\nCovenant context: ברית סיני, עשרת הדברות, יציאת מצרים כיסוד הזהות\n\nMiddat HaDin severity: 3/5 (as given)\n\nMiddat HaRachamim activation? Probably not activated because it's a command with severity moderate. But we can note.\n\nPurpose: to show God's authority and demand obedience, so Middat HaDin active.\n\nIntermediary: Moses is the prophet, but addressee is individual; intermediary effect on severity? Possibly reduces severity slightly? In system description, \"Purpose: effect on severity\" but not required. We can note that Moses as mediator may soften severity a bit (maybe -1). But we can just state.\n\nBowlby attachment reaction: anxious-ambivalent -> God expects obedience and punishes disobedience.\n\nJung archetype: Father (Power and law) active.\n\nResolution: balance of chesed/din leads to outcome: Pharaoh may obey partially, but eventually will be punished. So outcome is partial obedience leading to eventual judgment.\n\nNow produce Hebrew block: must be direct speech in 1st person: \"כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה...\" Use the verse text? Probably we need to produce a response from God: \"כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה, שַׁלַּח אֶת עַמִּי וְיַעַבְדֻנִי\". But the verse already contains that. We can produce a short statement: \"כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה, שַׁלַּח אֶת עַמִּי וְיַעַבְדֻנִי\". Then Russian translation.\n\nMake sure no extra text outside blocks.\n\nNow produce output.", "voice_hebrew": "כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה: שַׁלַּח אֶת־עַמִּי וְיַעַבְדֻנִי, כִּי לִי בְּנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל עֲבָדִים. אִם תְּמָאֵן לְשַׁלְּחָם, הִנֵּה אָבֹא עָלֶיךָ בְּכֹחִי וּבְגֵאוּתִי, וְהִכֵּיתִי אֶת־עַמְּךָ וְאֶת־בְּהֶמְתְּךָ בַּדֶּבֶר.", "voice_russian": "Так говорит Господь: отпусти́ мой народ, чтобы он служил́ мне; ибо сыны Израиля – мои рабы. Если ты отка́жешься отпустить их, то знай: я приду на тебя́ в силе и во гневе, и поражу твоего́ народ и скот мором.", "metadata": {"book": "Exodus", "trigger": "disobedience", "behavior_type": "command", "outcome": "compliance", "severity": 3, "situation_id": "Exodus_9_13"}}
