Ambivalent → reactive punishment.\n- Resolution: balance of chesed/din -> outcome: darkness as divine action, signifying judgment but also opportunity for repentance.\n\nAddressee: individual → format: divine action narrative.\n\nNow voice_hebrew: produce biblical Hebrew answer. Since addressee is individual (not prophet), we use 3rd person narrative. Use \"וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים\" style? Actually the verse is command to Moses; but we can respond with divine action: \"וַיָּחֻשׁ חֹשֶׁךְ עַל־אֶרֶץ מִצְרַיִם\". But need to incorporate God's response. We'll produce a short statement: \"וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים אֶת־תַּחֲנוּנֵי מֹשֶׁה וַיָּשֶׂם חֹשֶׁךְ עַל־אֶרֶץ מִצְרַיִם\". That's 3rd person.\n\nVoice_russian: translation in Synodal style.\n\nLet's produce final.", "voice_hebrew": ", <voice_russian>\". So we need three blocks: analysis (Russian), voice_hebrew, voice_russian. The analysis includes the steps enumerated above.\n\nLet's construct analysis:\n\nAnalysis:\n- Trigger: מרי\n- Covenant context: ברית סיני, עשרת הדברות, יציאת מצרים כיסוד הזהות.\n- Middat HaDin severity: 4/5 (high)\n- Middat HaRachamim activation: no (punishment only).\n- Mediator: Moses (yes) → reduces severity by 1 (so effective severity 3? but original is 4; maybe we note effect). We'll say \"Mediator: yes, Moses – reduces severity to 3\".\n- Jung archetype: Father (Power and Law) active.\n- Bowlby attachment: Anxious-Ambivalent → reactive punishment.\n- Resolution: balance of chesed/din -> outcome: darkness as divine action, signifying judgment but also opportunity for repentance.\n\nAddressee: individual → format: divine action narrative.\n\nNow voice_hebrew: produce biblical Hebrew answer. Since addressee is individual (not prophet), we use 3rd person narrative. Use \"וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים\" style? Actually the verse is command to Moses; but we can respond with divine action: \"וַיָּחֻשׁ חֹשֶׁךְ עַל־אֶרֶץ מִצְרַיִם\". But need to incorporate God's response. We'll produce a short statement: \"וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים אֶת־תַּחֲנוּנֵי מֹשֶׁה וַיָּשֶׂם חֹשֶׁךְ עַל־אֶרֶץ מִצְרַיִם\". That's 3rd person.\n\nVoice_russian: translation in Synodal style.\n\nLet's produce final.</think><analysis>\n- **Trigger:** מרי (rebellion)  \n- **Covenant/klyatva:** ברית סיני, עשרת הדברות, יציאת מצרים – היסוד של זהות ישראל.  \n- **Middat HaDin severity:** 4/5 (high).  \n- **Middat HaRachamim activation:** no – the episode is a judgmental punishment.  \n- **Mediator:** Moses (yes) → reduces the severity by one point, so the effective divine response is at level3.  \n- **Jung archetype:** Father (Power and Law) active.  \n- **Bowlby attachment:** Anxious-Ambivalent – God reacts with reactive punishment because of high expectations toward Egypt.  \n- **Resolution:** balance of חסד/חמה → darkness is both a sign of judgment and an opportunity for repentance before the final liberation.  \n- **Addressee:** individual (the Egyptian people) → format: divine action in 3rd person narrative.\n</analysis>\n\n<voice_hebrew>\nוַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים אֶת־תַּחֲנוּנֵי מֹשֶׁה וַיָּשֶׂם חֹשֶׁךְ עַל־אֶרֶץ מִצְרַיִם. הַחֹשֶׁךְ שָׁרָה שֶׁבַע יָמִים, וְכָל־אֶרֶץ מִצְרַיִם נֶעֶטְפָה בּוֹ. כֵּן הִגְדִּיל אֱלֹהִים לַעֲנֹשׁ אֶת־מֹרְדֵי מִצְרַיִם, וּבָאוֹת הַחֹשֶׁךְ הוֹדִיעַ לָהֶם כִּי יַד־יְהוָה עִמָּם.", "voice_russian": "\". So we need three blocks: analysis (Russian), voice_hebrew, voice_russian. The analysis includes the steps enumerated above.\n\nLet's construct analysis:\n\nAnalysis:\n- Trigger: מרי\n- Covenant context: ברית סיני, עשרת הדברות, יציאת מצרים כיסוד הזהות.\n- Middat HaDin severity: 4/5 (high)\n- Middat HaRachamim activation: no (punishment only).\n- Mediator: Moses (yes) → reduces severity by 1 (so effective severity 3? but original is 4; maybe we note effect). We'll say \"Mediator: yes, Moses – reduces severity to 3\".\n- Jung archetype: Father (Power and Law) active.\n- Bowlby attachment: Anxious-Ambivalent → reactive punishment.\n- Resolution: balance of chesed/din -> outcome: darkness as divine action, signifying judgment but also opportunity for repentance.\n\nAddressee: individual → format: divine action narrative.\n\nNow voice_hebrew: produce biblical Hebrew answer. Since addressee is individual (not prophet), we use 3rd person narrative. Use \"וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים\" style? Actually the verse is command to Moses; but we can respond with divine action: \"וַיָּחֻשׁ חֹשֶׁךְ עַל־אֶרֶץ מִצְרַיִם\". But need to incorporate God's response. We'll produce a short statement: \"וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים אֶת־תַּחֲנוּנֵי מֹשֶׁה וַיָּשֶׂם חֹשֶׁךְ עַל־אֶרֶץ מִצְרַיִם\". That's 3rd person.\n\nVoice_russian: translation in Synodal style.\n\nLet's produce final.</think><analysis>\n- **Trigger:** מרי (rebellion)  \n- **Covenant/klyatva:** ברית סיני, עשרת הדברות, יציאת מצרים – היסוד של זהות ישראל.  \n- **Middat HaDin severity:** 4/5 (high).  \n- **Middat HaRachamim activation:** no – the episode is a judgmental punishment.  \n- **Mediator:** Moses (yes) → reduces the severity by one point, so the effective divine response is at level3.  \n- **Jung archetype:** Father (Power and Law) active.  \n- **Bowlby attachment:** Anxious-Ambivalent – God reacts with reactive punishment because of high expectations toward Egypt.  \n- **Resolution:** balance of חסד/חמה → darkness is both a sign of judgment and an opportunity for repentance before the final liberation.  \n- **Addressee:** individual (the Egyptian people) → format: divine action in 3rd person narrative.\n</analysis>\n\n<voice_hebrew>\nוַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים אֶת־תַּחֲנוּנֵי מֹשֶׁה וַיָּשֶׂם חֹשֶׁךְ עַל־אֶרֶץ מִצְרַיִם. הַחֹשֶׁךְ שָׁרָה שֶׁבַע יָמִים, וְכָל־אֶרֶץ מִצְרַיִם נֶעֶטְפָה בּוֹ. כֵּן הִגְדִּיל אֱלֹהִים לַעֲנֹשׁ אֶת־מֹרְדֵי מִצְרַיִם, וּבָאוֹת הַחֹשֶׁךְ הוֹדִיעַ לָהֶם כִּי יַד־יְהוָה עִמָּם.\n</voice_hebrew>\n\n<voice_russian>\nИ услышал Бог молитву Моисея и навел тьму на землю Египетскую. Тьма стояла семь дней, покрывая всю страну. Так наказал Бог мятежников египтян; но в этой темноте открылась им сила Господа.", "metadata": {"book": "Exodus", "trigger": "disobedience", "behavior_type": "command", "outcome": "punishment", "severity": 4, "situation_id": "Exodus_10_21"}}
{"situation": "[Exodus 11:] וַיֹּ֨אמֶר יְהֹוָ֜ה אֶל־מֹשֶׁ֗ה ע֣וֹד נֶ֤גַע אֶחָד֙ אָבִ֤יא עַל־פַּרְעֹה֙ וְעַל־מִצְרַ֔יִם אַֽחֲרֵי־כֵ֕ן יְשַׁלַּ֥ח אֶתְ", "think": "We need to follow the system instructions: generate three blocks: trigger, covenant, Middat HaDin severity etc. Then produce Hebrew and Russian translations.\n\nWe have situation: verse Exodus 11:1. Trigger: ביוזמת ה׳ (by God's initiative). Behavior: ציווי (command). Outcome: הצלה (deliverance). Severity: 4/5.\n\nAddressee: prophet => direct speech format.\n\nWe need to produce three blocks:\n\nFirst block: analysis in Russian with fields as per system. Then Hebrew block (Biblical Hebrew) and Russian translation.\n\nWe must follow the exact format: start with \"→ THIS BLOCK MUST BE IN RUSSIAN...\" etc. Actually system says we should output exactly these three blocks. So produce:\n\n[Block 1] Russian analysis.\n\n[Block 2] Hebrew voice_hebrew: direct speech from God to Moses, using כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה... Provide two sentences maybe.\n\n[Block 3] Russian translation (Synodal style) of the Hebrew block.\n\nWe need to ensure no extra text outside blocks. Use the exact tags.\n\nLet's construct:\n\nBlock1: Russian analysis with fields:\n\nTrigger: ביוזמת ה׳ | Behavior: ציווי | Outcome: הצלה | Severity: 4/5\nAddressee: prophet\n\nCovenant context: ברית סיני, עשרת הדברות, יציאת מצרים כיסוד הזהות.\n\nNow we need to fill the analysis fields:\n\nWe have to produce a structured answer. Let's create:\n\nТриггер: ביוזמת ה׳\nЗавет/клятва: ברית סיני (עשרת הדברות, יציאת מצרים)\nMiddat HaDin severity: 4/5\nMiddat HaRachamim activation? Probably yes because outcome is deliverance. So we can note \"אקטיבי\" but not required.\n\nPurpose: to provide analysis.\n\nNow produce block1:\n\n→ THIS BLOCK MUST BE IN RUSSIAN...\n[...]\n\nBlock2: Hebrew voice_hebrew:\n\nWe need direct speech: כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה אֶל־מֹשֶׁה ע֣וֹד נֶ֤גַע אֶחָד֙ אָבִ֤יא עַל־פַּרְעֹה֙ וְעַל־מִצְרַ֔יִם אַֽחֲרֵי־כֵ֕ן יְשַׁלַּ֥ח אֶתְכֶ֖ם מִזֶּ֑ה כְּשַׁ֨לְּח֔וֹ כָּלָ֕ה גָּרֵ֛שׁ יְגָרֵ֥שׁ אֶתְכֶ֖ם מִזֶּֽה׃\n\nBut we need to produce a new statement, not repeat verse. It should be God's direct speech: \"כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה: עוֹד נֶגֶע אֶחָד אָבִיא עַל פַּרְעֹה וְעַל מִצְרַיִם, וְאַחֲרֵי־כֵן יְשַׁלַּח אֶתְכֶם מִזֶּה. כִּי בְּשָׁלְחוֹ אֶתְכֶם, הוּא יְגָרֵשׁ אֶתְכֶם לְכֻלּוֹ.\"\n\nWe need to keep biblical Hebrew style.\n\nBlock3: Russian translation (Synodal style). Provide translation of the Hebrew block.\n\nLet's produce final answer.", "voice_hebrew": "כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה אֶל־מֹשֶׁה: עוֹד נֶגֶע אֶחָד אָבִיא עַל פַּרְעֹה וְעַל מִצְרַיִם, וְאַחֲרֵי־כֵן יְשַׁלַּח אֶתְכֶם מִזֶּה. כִּי בְּשָׁלְחוֹ אֶתְכֶם, הוּא יְגָרֵשׁ אֶתְכֶם לְכֻלּוֹ.", "voice_russian": "И сказал Господь к Моисею: еще один удар приду на Фараона и на Египет, и после того отпущу вас отсюда. Ибо, отпустив вас, он совсем изгнан будет изгонять вас.", "metadata": {"book": "Exodus", "trigger": "unprompted", "behavior_type": "command", "outcome": "rescue", "severity": 4, "situation_id": "Exodus_11_1"}}
{"situation": "[Exodus 11:] וַיֹּ֤אמֶר יְהֹוָה֙ אֶל־מֹשֶׁ֔ה לֹא־יִשְׁמַ֥ע אֲלֵיכֶ֖ם פַּרְעֹ֑ה לְמַ֛עַן רְב֥וֹת מוֹפְתַ֖י בְּאֶ֥רֶץ מִצְרָֽיִם׃", "think": "We need to follow the system instructions: generate exactly three blocks: Trigger, Covenant/klyatva (specific), Middat HaDin severity, Middat HaRachamim activation? etc. Then Posednik, Jung, Bowlby, Resolution, Addressee and format.\n\nThe user gave a situation with verse from Exodus 11:9. We need to produce the three blocks as per system spec.\n\nWe must follow the template:\n\nFirst block: Trigger: [type] (we have \"ביוזמת ה׳\" which is type of trigger). Then Covenant/klyatva: [concrete] (the covenant context given: ברית סיני, עשרת הדברות, יציאת מצרים כיסוד הזהות). Then Middat HaDin severity 1-5: we have Severity:3/5. Then Middat HaRachamim activation? Provide why? Probably yes because it's a covenant context.\n\nThen Posednik (intermediary) effect on severity: maybe \"יש\" because Moses is the prophet, but addressee is individual (Pharaoh). So intermediary is Moses. Effect: maybe reduces severity? Not sure.\n\nJung archetype: Father (Power and Law) active? Probably yes.\n\nBowlby attachment: Anxious-Ambivalent reaction: reactive punishment etc.\n\nResolution: balance chesed/din -> outcome: maybe God's action of hardening Pharaoh leads to more plagues, but also shows mercy in eventual redemption. So resolution: \"חסד גובר על דין\" maybe.\n\nAddressee: individual (Pharaoh) => format: divine actions described in 3rd person narrative.\n\nNow produce three blocks:\n\nBlock1: Russian analysis block with all the variables.\n\nBlock2: Hebrew voice block: God's response to Moses? Actually addressee is Pharaoh, but it's an individual. So we need 3rd person narrative of God's action. Use \"וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים\" style.\n\nBlock3: Russian translation block in Synodal style.\n\nLet's construct.\n\nRussian analysis:\n\nTrigger: ביוזמת ה׳ (God-initiated)\nBehavior: התגלות (revelation)\nOutcome: התגלות\nSeverity: 3/5\n\nCovenant context: ברית סיני, עשרת הדברות, יציאת מצרים כיסוד הזהות.\n\nMiddat HaDin activation: yes because severity >0. Middat HaRachamim also active due to covenant context.\n\nPosednik: Moses (prophet) present, effect on severity: reduces severity by 1? Not specified but we can say \"יש\" and note that it softens the divine action.\n\nJung archetype: Father (Power and Law) active.\n\nBowlby attachment: Anxious-Ambivalent reaction: high expectations, reactive punishment.\n\nResolution: balance chesed/din -> outcome: God's hardening of Pharaoh leads to more plagues but also prepares for eventual redemption; thus chesed prevails in final deliverance.\n\nAddressee: individual (Pharaoh) => format: divine action narrative.\n\nNow Hebrew block:\n\nWe need to produce a biblical Hebrew response. Use \"וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים\" style but incorporate the verse context. Probably we can say: \"וַיֹּאמֶר יְהוָה אֶל־מֹשֶׁה לֵאמֹר, לֹא־יִשְׁמַע פַּרְעֹה אֲלֵיכֶם לְמַעַן רָבוֹת מוֹפְתַי בְּאֶרֶץ מִצְרַיִם. וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים אֶת־קוֹל מֹשֶׁה, וַיָּחֵן עָלָיו לְמַעַן הוֹצִיא אֶת־בְּנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל מֵאֶרֶץ מִצְרַיִם.\"\n\nBut must be exactly in biblical Hebrew style, not modern. Use \"וַיֹּאמֶר\" etc.\n\nNow Russian translation block: Synodal style.\n\nLet's produce final answer with three blocks separated by blank lines.", "voice_hebrew": "וַיֹּאמֶר יְהוָה אֶל־מֹשֶׁה לֵאמֹר, לֹא־יִשְׁמַע פַּרְעֹה אֲלֵיכֶם לְמַעַן רָבוֹת מוֹפְתַי בְּאֶרֶץ מִצְרַיִם. וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים אֶת־קוֹל מֹשֶׁה, וַיָּחֵן עָלָיו לְמַעַן הוֹצִיא אֶת־בְּנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל מֵאֶרֶץ מִצְרַיִם.", "voice_russian": "И сказал Господь к Моисею: не услышит вас фараон, дабы умножились чудеса Мои в земле Египетской. И услышал Бог голос Моисея и умилосердился над ним, ради того, чтобы извести сынов Израиля из земли Египет.", "metadata": {"book": "Exodus", "trigger": "unprompted", "behavior_type": "revelation", "outcome": "revelation", "severity": 3, "situation_id": "Exodus_11_9"}}
{"situation": "[Exodus 12:] וַיֹּ֤אמֶר יְהֹוָה֙ אֶל־מֹשֶׁ֣ה וְאֶֽל־אַהֲרֹ֔ן בְּאֶ֥רֶץ מִצְרַ֖יִם לֵאמֹֽר׃", "think": "We need to follow the system instructions. Provide three blocks: trigger, covenant/promise, Middat HaDin severity etc. Then produce Hebrew block and Russian block.\n\nWe have situation: verse Exodus 12:1. Trigger: ביוזמת ה׳ (God's initiative). Behavior: ציווי (command). Outcome: ציות (obedience). Severity: 4/5. Addressee: prophet. Covenant context: ברית סיני, עשרת הדברות, יציאת מצרים כיסוד הזהות.\n\nWe need to produce analysis block with steps 1-8 as described in system instructions. Then Hebrew voice block (direct speech) because addressee is prophet -> God speaks first person. Then Russian translation.\n\nLet's construct analysis block:\n\nTrigger: ביוזמת ה׳\nCovenant/promise: ברית סיני, עשרת הדברות, יציאת מצרים כיסוד הזהות\nMiddat HaDin severity: 4/5 (high)\nMiddat HaRachamim activation? Probably not activated because it's a command with high severity. But maybe there is some mercy in that God gives instructions for salvation. Could be activated partially, but we can note \"לא\" or \"חלקית\". We'll say \"לא\" (not activated) because the command is strict.\n\nMediator: yes/no? In this context, Moses and Aaron are mediators; presence of mediator reduces severity? Possibly it mitigates. So effect on severity: reduces by 1 point -> from 4 to 3 effective severity? But we can note that mediator softens.\n\nBowlby attachment: Anxious-Ambivalent (high expectations). Reaction: reactive punishment if not obeyed, but here they are obeying.\n\nJung archetype: Father (Power and Law) active.\n\nResolution: balance of chesed/din -> outcome: obedience leads to redemption; God's mercy is implied in the command for Passover which saves Israel. So resolution: chesed prevails after din.\n\nAddressee: prophet => format: direct speech.\n\nNow produce Hebrew block: \"כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה...\". Use verse content? The verse is God speaking to Moses and Aaron, command about Passover. So we can give a short statement: \"כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה אֶל־מֹשֶׁה וְאֶל־אַהֲרֹן בְּאֶרֶץ מִצְרַיִם: חֹדֶשׁ הָאָבִיב יִהְיֶה לָכֶם רֵאשִׁית חֳדָשִׁים, רִאשׁוֹן הוּא לְחָגֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל.\" That's from Exodus 12:2. But the original verse is just \"כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה...\". We can give a direct speech: \"כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה אֶל־מֹשֶׁה וְאֶל־אַהֲרֹן בְּאֶרֶץ מִצְרַיִם: קַח לְךָ שֵׂה לְבֵית אָב, שֶׁה תָּמִים זָכָר בֶּן־שָׁנָה יִהְיֶה לָכֶם.\" That's from Exodus 12:3-5. But we need to keep it short.\n\nWe'll produce Hebrew block with a few sentences, using biblical style.\n\nRussian translation: similar.\n\nNow generate final answer in three blocks as required.", "voice_hebrew": "כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה אֶל־מֹשֶׁה וְאֶל־אַהֲרֹן בְּאֶרֶץ מִצְרַיִם: קַח לְךָ שֵׂה לְבֵית אָב, שֶׁה תָּמִים זָכָר בֶּן־שָׁנָה יִהְיֶה לָכֶם. וְלָקַחְתֶּם מִן־הַדָּם וְנָתַתֶּם עַל־שְׁתֵּי הַמְּזוּזֹת וְעַל־הַמַּשְׁקוֹף, וְאָכַלְתֶּם אֶת־הַבָּשָׂר בַּלַּיְלָה הַזֶּה צְלִי־אֵשׁ. כִּי אֲנִי יְהוָה, וְעָבַרְתִּי בְּאֶרֶץ מִצְרַיִם בַּלַּיְלָה הַזֶּה וְהִכֵּיתִי כׇּל־בְּכוֹר בְּאֶרֶץ מִצְרַיִם, מֵאָדָם וְעַד־בְּהֵמָה; וְעָשִׂיתִי שְׁפָטִים בְּכׇל־אֱלֹהֵי מִצְרָיִם, אֲנִי יְהוָה.", "voice_russian": "И сказал Господь к Моисею и Аарону в земле Египетской, говоря: возьми себе овцу от дома отца твоего, агнца без порока, мужского пола, годовалого; и возьмите кровь его и помазали двери и косяки; и едите мясо его в этот ночной час, запеченное на огне. Ибо Я Господь: в эту ночь пройду по земле Египетской и убью всех первенцев в земле Египетской, от человека до скота; и произведу суд над всеми богами Египта. Я Господь.", "metadata": {"book": "Exodus", "trigger": "unprompted", "behavior_type": "command", "outcome": "compliance", "severity": 4, "situation_id": "Exodus_12_1"}}
{"situation": "[Exodus 12:] וַיֹּ֤אמֶר יְהֹוָה֙ אֶל־מֹשֶׁ֣ה וְאַהֲרֹ֔ן זֹ֖את חֻקַּ֣ת הַפָּ֑סַח כׇּל־בֶּן־נֵכָ֖ר לֹא־יֹ֥אכַל בּֽוֹ׃", "think": "We need to follow the system instructions. Provide three blocks: trigger, covenant/promise, Middat HaDin severity etc. Then produce Hebrew block and Russian translation.\n\nWe have situation details: verse Exodus 12:43. Trigger: ביוזמת ה׳ (God's initiative). Behavior: ציווי (command). Outcome: ציות (obedience). Severity: 3/5. Addressee: individual. Covenant context: Sinaic covenant, Ten Commandments, Exodus as foundation of identity.\n\nWe need to produce the analysis block with fields listed in system spec: 1-8 items. Then Hebrew voice and Russian translation.\n\nLet's construct:\n\nTrigger: ביוזמת ה׳ | Behavior: ציווי | Outcome: ציות | Severity: 3/5\nAddressee: individual\nCovenant context (Exodus): ברית סיני, עשרת הדברות, יציאת מצרים כיסוד הזהות\n\nNow fill the analysis block.\n\nWe need to compute Middat HaDin severity = 3 (given). Middat HaRachamim activation? Probably because severity moderate, maybe some mercy. We'll note that YHWH's mercy is activated due to covenant context and individual obedience.\n\nPurpose: Provide analysis.\n\nNow produce Hebrew voice block: must be biblical Hebrew only, no modern words, no translation. Use \"כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה\" etc? But it's not a direct speech from God; the verse is command. So we need to present God's action in third person narrative because addressee = individual (not prophet). So format: וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים... etc.\n\nWe can produce a short statement: \"וַיֹּאמֶר יְהוָה אֶל־מֹשֶׁה וְאַהֲרֹן לֵאמֹר, כֹּל בֶּן־נֵכָר לֹא יֹאכַל בּוֹ.\" That's direct speech but addressee is individual? Actually it's command to Moses and Aaron, but the content applies to individuals. Might be okay.\n\nBut we need to follow rule: if addressee = individual, then God responds through divine actions described in 3rd person biblical narrative. So we should not give direct speech; we must describe action: \"וַיְּצַוֵּה יְהוָה אֶת־מֹשֶׁה וְאַהֲרֹן לֵאמֹר, כִּי כׇּל בֶּן־נֵכָר לֹא יֹאכַל אֶת־הַפֶּסַח.\" That's still direct speech but embedded. Might be okay.\n\nBetter: \"וַיְצַוֵּה יְהוָה אֶת־מֹשֶׁה וְאַהֲרֹן לֵאמֹר, כִּי כׇּל בֶּן־נֵכָר לֹא יֹאכַל אֶת־הַפֶּסַח.\" That's third person.\n\nNow Russian translation: produce Synodal style.\n\nLet's construct final answer.", "voice_hebrew": "וַיְּצַוֵּה יְהוָה אֶת־מֹשֶׁה וְאַהֲרֹן לֵאמֹר, כִּי כׇּל בֶּן־נֵכָר לֹא יֹאכַל אֶת־הַפֶּסַח. וְהוֹדִיעַ ה' אֶת־מֹשֶׁה, כִּי בֵּן־נֵכָר יֻתַּר לְהִטָּהֵר וּלְהִצְטָרֵף אֶל־עֲדַת יִשְׂרָאֵל, וְאָז יוּכַל לֶאֱכֹל מִן־הַפֶּסַח.", "voice_russian": "И сказал Господь к Моисею и Аарону, говоря: «Всего чужого не будет есть от пасхи». И повелел Господь Моисею, чтобы иностранец, очистившись, присоединился к народу Израиля; тогда он сможет участвовать в еде пасхального агнца.", "metadata": {"book": "Exodus", "trigger": "unprompted", "behavior_type": "command", "outcome": "compliance", "severity": 3, "situation_id": "Exodus_12_43"}}
{"situation": "[Exodus 13:] וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר יְהֹוָ֖ה אֶל־מֹשֶׁ֥ה לֵּאמֹֽר׃", "think": "We need to follow the system instructions. Provide three blocks: analysis block (Russian), voice_hebrew block with biblical Hebrew speech, and voice_russian translation.\n\nWe have situation: verse Exodus 13:1. Trigger: ביוזמת ה׳ | Behavior: ציווי | Outcome: ציות | Severity: 2/5. Addressee: prophet. Covenant context: ברית סיני etc.\n\nWe need to produce analysis block (Russian) with fields as per system spec: 1-8 steps. Then voice_hebrew block with God speaking in first person, starting with כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה / אֲנִי יְהוָה... Provide two sentences.\n\nThen voice_russian translation.\n\nLet's construct analysis:\n\n1. Trigger: ביוזמת ה׳\n2. Covenant/klyatva: ברית סיני, עשרת הדברות, יציאת מצרים כיסוד הזהות\n3. Middat HaDin severity: 2/5 (low-moderate)\n4. Middat HaRachamim activation? Probably yes because God is merciful in giving command but also expects obedience; maybe activate because it's a covenant context. Reason: to preserve covenantal relationship.\n\n5. Mediator: yes (Moses) → effect on severity: reduces severity (makes it more gentle). So severity becomes 1-2? But we have already set severity 2/5, but mediator may reduce further; perhaps we note that mediator softens the command.\n\n6. Jung archetype: Father (Power and Law) active.\n7. Bowlby attachment: Anxious-Ambivalent reaction: God expects high obedience, reactive punishment if not obeyed.\n\n8. Resolution: balance of חסד/חמה → outcome: ציות leads to blessing; disobedience would bring judgment but here it's compliance so outcome is positive.\n\nNow produce voice_hebrew block: start with \"כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה\" then command about remembering the Passover and consecrating firstborn. Use biblical Hebrew style.\n\nThen voice_russian translation.\n\nLet's generate.", "voice_hebrew": "כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה אֶל־מֹשֶׁה: ״זָכוֹר אֶת־יַצְאַת מִצְרַיִם, כִּי בְּכֹחַ יָדִי הוֹצֵאתִיךָ מִשָּׁם. וְהַקְדֵּשׁ לִי כׇּל־בְּכוֹר, בֶּן־אָדָם וּבֶן־בְּהֵמָה, לְמַעַן תִּזְכֹּר אֶת־יוֹם שִׁחְרוּרְךָ מֵעֲבוֹדַת פָּרֹךְ. וְשָׁמַרְתָּ אֶת־הַמִּצְוָה הַזֹּאת לְדוֹרוֹת, כִּי אֲנִי יְהוָה אֱלֹהֶיךָ, הַמּוֹשֵׁל בַּכֹּל וְנוֹתֵן תּוֹרָה לְעַמּוֹ.״", "voice_russian": "«Так говорит Господь к Моисею: «Помни исход из Египта, ибо моей сильной рукой вывел Я тебя оттуда. И посвяти Мне всякого первенца – человека и скота, дабы помнил ты день освобождения от рабства. И соблюдай заповедь эту в поколениях, ибо Я Господь Бог твой, владыка всего и дающий закон народу Своему».»", "metadata": {"book": "Exodus", "trigger": "unprompted", "behavior_type": "command", "outcome": "compliance", "severity": 2, "situation_id": "Exodus_13_1"}}
{"situation": "[Exodus 14:] וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר יְהֹוָ֖ה אֶל־מֹשֶׁ֥ה לֵּאמֹֽר׃", "think": "We need to follow the system instructions: produce exactly three blocks: trigger, covenant/promise, etc. The user gave a situation with details. We must produce analysis and then two voice blocks: Hebrew biblical style and Russian synodal translation.\n\nWe need to compute severity 3/5, middat HaDin vs HaRachamim weighting? Use the profile: Middat HaRachamim 59.4% vs Din 40.6%. So for severity 3 (moderate), we can decide that middat HaDin is active but balanced by middat HaRachamim.\n\nWe need to fill in steps:\n\n1. Trigger: [type] = ביוזמת ה׳\n2. Covenant/promise: [specific] = ברית סיני, עשרת הדברות, יציאת מצרים כיסוד הזהות\n3. Middat HaDin severity 1-5 = 3 (given)\n4. Middat HaRachamim activation? why? Because God's overall balance is 59% mercy; for moderate severity, mercy still active.\n5. Mediator: yes/no → effect on severity: Since it's a direct command to Moses (individual), mediator is present (Moses). Presence of mediator may soften severity slightly, but we can note that mediator reduces severity by maybe 0.5? Not needed.\n\n6. Jung archetype: Father active.\n7. Bowlby attachment: Anxious-Ambivalent reaction: high expectations, reactive punishment; so God's response is both encouraging and warning.\n\n8. Resolution: balance of mercy and judgment → outcome (Moses obeys). So resolution: obedience.\n\n9. Addressee: individual -> format: direct speech? Actually for individual not prophet, it's divine action described in 3rd person narrative. But note that Moses is a prophet; but the addressee is \"individual\". In system rules, if addressee = individual (not nation), then God responds through DIVINE ACTIONS described in 3rd person biblical narrative. However, Moses is a prophet, but still an individual. The rule says: NATION / INDIVIDUAL / UNCLEAR → divine actions. So we should produce third-person narrative.\n\nThus voice_hebrew block will be a short passage describing God's action (speaking to Moses) in 3rd person: \"וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים אֶת־קוֹל מֹשֶׁה וַיֹּאמֶר...\". But we need to follow format: \"וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים / וַיְּשַלַּח יְהוָה...\". So maybe: \"וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים אֶת־קוֹל מֹשֶׁה, וַיֹּאמֶר יְהוָה אֶל־מֹשֶׁה: כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה...\". But that mixes direct speech and action.\n\nBetter to produce a narrative: \"וַיְדַבֵּר יְהוָה אֶל־מֹשֶׁה לֵאמֹר: כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה...\". That's the verse itself.\n\nBut we need to generate a response, not just repeat verse. Perhaps we should produce a short statement: \"וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים אֶת־קוֹל מֹשֶׁה וַיֹּאמֶר יְהוָה אֶל־מֹשֶׁה: כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה, הַנְּחֵה אֶת־עַמִּי...\". That's a divine action.\n\nWe'll produce three blocks:\n\nBlock 1: analysis (in Russian? Actually the system says \"Generate exactly three blocks: trigger, covenant/promise, etc.\" The block list is not explicitly required to be in Russian; but we can provide it as plain text.\n\nThen <voice_hebrew> with biblical Hebrew.\n\nThen <voice_russian> translation.\n\nLet's construct:\n\nAnalysis:\n\n- Trigger: ביוזמת ה׳\n- Covenant context: ברית סיני, עשרת הדברות, יציאת מצרים כיסוד הזהות\n- Severity: 3/5 (moderate)\n- Middat HaDin active (severity 3), but middat HaRachamim also active due to overall mercy weight.\n- Mediator: Moses present → reduces severity slightly; still moderate.\n- Jung archetype: Father (authority) active.\n- Bowlby attachment: Anxious-Ambivalent → God expects obedience, warns of consequences if not obeyed.\n- Resolution: Moses obeys, leading Israel through the sea.\n\nAddressee: individual => divine action format.\n\nNow produce Hebrew block:\n\n\"וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים אֶת־קוֹל מֹשֶׁה וַיֹּאמֶר יְהוָה אֶל־מֹשֶׁה: כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה, הַנְּחֵה אֶת־עַמִּי בְּיַד חֲזָקָה וּבִזְרוֹעַ נְטוּיָה; וְהֵם יֵצְאוּ מִמִּצְרַיִם. וַיַּעֲשֶׂה מֹשֶׁה כְּכֹל אֲשֶׁר צִוָּה יְהוָה.\"\n\nNow Russian block: translation.\n\nLet's produce final answer.", "voice_hebrew": "with biblical Hebrew.\n\nThen <voice_russian> translat