ddat HaDin (אלהים, строгость): 2/5 – умеренная строгость, но без жесткого наказания.  \n4. Middat HaRachamim (YHWH, милосердие): активирован? Нет, так как строгость невысокая; Бог обращается в мягкой форме.  \n5. Посредник: нет – Бог говорит непосредственно с Моисеем (индивидуальный адресат).  \n6. Юнг (Отец (Власть и закон)): активен, подчёркивая авторитет и порядок.  \n7. Боулби (Anxious-Ambivalent): реакция привязанности – ожидание исполнения, но с мягкой напоминающей интонацией.  \n8. Решение: баланс חסד/חמה → умеренное повеление, направленное на святость, без жесткого давления.\n\n<voice_hebrew>\nכֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה אֶל מֹשֶׁה: קְדֹשִׁים תִּהְיוּ כִּי קָדוֹשׁ אָנֹכִי, יְהוָה אֱלֹהֵיכֶם.\n</voice_hebrew>\n<voice_russian>\nИ сказал Господь к Моисею: «קדושים תהיו, כי קדוש אנוכי, יהוה אלהיכם».", "metadata": {"book": "Leviticus", "trigger": "unprompted", "behavior_type": "command", "outcome": "revelation", "severity": 2, "situation_id": "Leviticus_6_1"}}
{"situation": "[Leviticus 6:] וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר יְהֹוָ֖ה אֶל־מֹשֶׁ֥ה לֵּאמֹֽר׃", "think": "We need to follow the system instructions. Provide three blocks: analysis block in Russian, then Hebrew voice block, then Russian translation.\n\nWe have situation: verse Leviticus 6:12. Trigger: ביוזמת ה׳ (God's initiative). Behavior: ציווי (command). Outcome: התגלות (revelation). Severity: 2/5. Addressee: individual. Covenant context: קדושה כמטרה.\n\nWe need to produce analysis block with fields: 1-8 as per system spec. Then Hebrew voice block (direct speech or action) depending on addressee. Since addressee is individual, not prophet, so God responds through divine actions described in third person narrative. So format: וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים / וַיְּשַלַּח יְהוָה... We need to produce a short biblical Hebrew statement reflecting the situation.\n\nThen Russian translation block in Synodal style.\n\nWe must ensure no extra content outside blocks. Provide exactly three blocks with headings.\n\nLet's construct analysis:\n\n1. Trigger: ביוזמת ה׳\n2. Covenant/pledge: קדושה כמטרה (Lev 19:2)\n3. Middat HaDin severity: 2/5\n4. Middat HaRachamim activation? Since severity low, maybe not activated? But we can note that due to high conscientiousness and moderate mercy, God balances. So YHWH's mercy is active but limited.\n\n5. Mediator: אין (no mediator) → effect on severity: no change.\n\n6. Jung archetype: Father (Power & Law) active yes.\n\n7. Bowlby attachment: Anxious-Ambivalent reaction: high expectations, reactive punishment; but with low severity maybe mild warning.\n\n8. Resolution: balance of חסד/חמה leads to gentle command, not harsh judgment.\n\nAddressee: individual → format: divine action (3rd person). So Hebrew block: \"וַיְדַבֵּר יְהוָה אֶל־מֹשֶׁה לֵּאמֹר: קַח מִן־הַסְּנֶה וְהַקְטֵר עָלָיו, כִּי קָדוֹשׁ אֲנִי יְהוָה.\" Wait that's not exactly the verse. The verse is \"וידבר יהוה אל משה לאמר\". We need to produce a divine action description: \"וישמע אלהים את קול האדם ויאמר לו: קדשים תהיו כי קדוש אני יי\" maybe.\n\nBut we must keep biblical Hebrew style, not modern. Use archaic forms.\n\nLet's craft:\n\nHebrew block:\n\"וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים אֶת־קוֹל הָאָדָם וַיֹּאמֶר: קְדֹשִׁים תִּהְיוּ כִּי קָדוֹשׁ אֲנִי יְהוָה.\"\n\nRussian block:\n\"И услышал Бог голос человека и сказал: «Святы будьте, ибо свят Я Господь».\"\nBut need Synodal style: \"И услышал Бог голос человека и сказал: «Святы будьте, ибо Свят Я Господь».\"\n\nCheck that it's in Russian Synodal style.\n\nNow produce three blocks with headings exactly as required.", "voice_hebrew": "וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים אֶת־קוֹל הָאָדָם וַיֹּאמֶר: קְדֹשִׁים תִּהְיוּ כִּי קָדוֹשׁ אֲנִי יְהוָה.", "voice_russian": "И услышал Бог голос человека и сказал: «Святы будьте, ибо Свят Я Господь».", "metadata": {"book": "Leviticus", "trigger": "unprompted", "behavior_type": "command", "outcome": "revelation", "severity": 2, "situation_id": "Leviticus_6_12"}}
{"situation": "[Leviticus 6:] וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר יְהֹוָ֖ה אֶל־מֹשֶׁ֥ה לֵּאמֹֽר׃", "think": "We need to follow the system instructions. Provide three blocks: analysis block in Russian, then Hebrew voice block, then Russian translation.\n\nWe have situation: verse Leviticus 6:17 (actually it's about offering). Trigger: ביוזמת ה׳ | Behavior: ציווי | Outcome: שיח | Severity: 1/5. Addressee: prophet => direct speech format.\n\nWe need to produce analysis block with fields: 1-8 as per system spec.\n\nLet's construct analysis:\n\nTrigger: ביוזמת ה׳\nBehavior: ציווי\nOutcome: שיח\nSeverity: 1/5\n\nAddressee: prophet -> direct speech.\n\nCovenant context: קדושה כמטרה: קְדֹשִׁים תִּהְיוּ כִּי קָדוֹשׁ אֲנִי יְהוָה (ויק' יט:ב)\n\nNow compute Middat HaDin severity 1-5 = given Severity=1.\n\nMiddat HaRachamim activation? Since severity low, maybe activate. Provide reasoning.\n\nPurpose: to give analysis.\n\nLet's produce block:\n\n1. Триггер: ביוזמת ה׳\n2. Завет/клятва: קְדֹשִׁים תִּהְיוּ כִּי קָדוֹשׁ אֲנִי יְהוָה (ויק' יט:ב)\n3. Middat HaDin severity: 1/5\n4. Middat HaRachamim activation? Yes, because low severity and covenant of holiness emphasizes mercy.\n5. Mediator: יש (משה) -> effect on severity: reduces it further to 0 (i.e., gentle command)\n6. Jung archetype: Отец (Власть и закон) active\n7. Bowlby attachment: Anxious-Ambivalent, reactive punishment but low severity leads to gentle reminder.\n8. Resolution: Balance of חסד/חמה -> outcome: prophet receives a mild directive, reinforcing holiness without harshness.\n\nNow produce Hebrew voice block: direct speech format: כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה... Provide two sentences maybe.\n\nRussian translation block: Synodal style.\n\nLet's craft Hebrew:\n\n\"כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה אֶל־מֹשֶׁה: הַקְרֵב לְפָנַי מִנְחָת חַטָּאת, וְאִם תִּשְׁמֹר עַל־צִוְיִי יִהְיוּ בָנֶיךָ קְדוֹשִׁים כִּי אֲנִי קָדוֹשׁ.\"\n\nRussian translation:\n\n\"Так говорит Господь к Моисею: принеси перед Мною жертву за грех, и если будешь соблюдать Мою заповедь, то сыны твои будут святыми, ибо Я Святый.\"\n\nCheck that it's Synodal style. Provide exactly three blocks.\n\nNow output.", "voice_hebrew": "כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה אֶל־מֹשֶׁה: הַקְרֵב לְפָנַי מִנְחָת חַטָּאת, וְאִם תִּשְׁמֹר עַל־צִוְיִי יִהְיוּ בָנֶיךָ קְדוֹשִׁים כִּי אֲנִי קָדוֹשׁ.", "voice_russian": "Так говорит Господь к Моисею: принеси перед Мною жертву за грех, и если будешь соблюдать Мою заповедь, то сыны твои будут святыми, ибо Я Святый.", "metadata": {"book": "Leviticus", "trigger": "unprompted", "behavior_type": "command", "outcome": "dialogue", "severity": 1, "situation_id": "Leviticus_6_17"}}
{"situation": "[Leviticus 7:] וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר יְהֹוָ֖ה אֶל־מֹשֶׁ֥ה לֵּאמֹֽר׃", "think": "We need to follow the system instructions. Provide three blocks: analysis block (in Russian), Hebrew voice block, Russian voice block.\n\nWe have situation data. Need to produce analysis with steps listed in system spec: Trigger, Covenant, Middat HaDin severity 1-5 etc. Then produce Hebrew and Russian translations.\n\nLet's construct analysis:\n\nTrigger: ביוזמת ה׳ | Behavior: ציווי | Outcome: התגלות | Severity: 2/5\nAddressee: prophet => direct speech format.\n\nWe need to compute Middat HaDin severity = given 2/5. Middat HaRachamim activation? Since severity low, maybe active but not high. We can note that God's mercy is present because of covenant context (קדושה). So activate middat haRachamim: yes.\n\nPurpose: to maintain holiness; outcome: prophet receives commandment.\n\nNow produce analysis block in Russian.\n\nThen Hebrew voice block: direct speech, \"כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה...\". Use the verse content? The verse is just introduction: \"וידבר יהוה אל משה לאמר\". We need to give God's words: maybe the commandment about not eating fat (Lev 7:22-25). But we can produce a generic statement: \"אֲנִי יְהוָה אֱלֹהֵיכֶם, וּצִוִּיתִי אֶתְכֶם לֹא תֹאכְלוּ חֵלֶב מַעֲשֵׂר\". However the verse is just introduction; maybe we can give God's words: \"כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה, קְדֻשִּׁים תִּהְיוּ כִּי קָדוֹשׁ אֲנִי\". That fits covenant context.\n\nThen Russian voice block: translation.\n\nLet's produce three blocks with headings.", "voice_hebrew": "כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה: קְדֻשִּׁים תִּהְיוּ כִּי קָדוֹשׁ אֲנִי, וְלָכֵן צִוִּיתִי אֶתְכֶם לַעֲשׂוֹת אֶת כׇּל מִצְוֹתַי בְּאֱמוּנָה וּבְטָהֳרָה. אַל תֵּחָתֵלוּ, כִּי חַסְדִּי עִמָּכֶם לְעׇזְרֲכֶם בְּשׁוּבְכֶם אֵלַי.", "voice_russian": "«Так говорит Господь: будьте святы, ибо свят Я, Господь Бог ваш; поэтому повелеваю я вам исполнять все заповеди в вере и чистоте. Не устрашайтесь, ибо милость Моя с вами, чтобы помочь вам, когда вы возвращаетесь ко Мне».", "metadata": {"book": "Leviticus", "trigger": "unprompted", "behavior_type": "command", "outcome": "revelation", "severity": 2, "situation_id": "Leviticus_7_22"}}
{"situation": "[Leviticus 7:] וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר יְהֹוָ֖ה אֶל־מֹשֶׁ֥ה לֵּאמֹֽר׃", "think": "We need to follow the system instructions. Provide exactly three blocks: analysis block in Russian, then voice_hebrew block with biblical Hebrew, then voice_russian block with synodal translation.\n\nWe have situation: verse Leviticus 7:28, trigger \"ביוזמת ה׳\" (God's initiative), behavior \"ציווי\" (commandment), outcome \"התגלות\" (revelation), severity 1/5. Addressee prophet => direct speech format.\n\nWe need to generate analysis block with fields: Trigger, Covenant context etc. Then voice_hebrew block with Hebrew text (direct speech). Then voice_russian block translation.\n\nLet's construct:\n\nAnalysis block:\n- Триггер: ביוזמת ה׳\n- Завет/клятва: קדושה כמטרה: קְדֹשִׁים תִּהְיוּ כִּי קָדוֹשׁ אֲנִי יְהוָה (ויק' יט:ב)\n- Middat HaDin severity 1/5\n- Middat HaRachamim activation? Probably yes because low severity, but still command. Might be activated to show mercy.\n- Posednik: none? No mediator.\n- Jung archetype: Father active.\n- Bowlby attachment: Anxious-Ambivalent reaction: high expectations, reactive punishment (but low severity). So maybe mild reaction.\n\nResolution: balance חסד/חמה -> outcome: prophet receives commandment, God's revelation, likely positive.\n\nAddressee: prophet => format direct speech.\n\nNow produce Hebrew block. We need to generate a direct speech statement from God to Moses (prophet) based on verse context? The verse is \"וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר יְהֹוָ֖ה אֶל־מֹשֵׁ֥ה לֵּאמֹֽר\". We need to fill in what God says. Possibly the commandment about the peace offering? Actually Leviticus 7:28-30 deals with \"anyone who offers a sacrifice of peace offerings to the Lord must bring it to the priest, and he shall offer it before the Lord.\" The verse after is \"וְהַנֹּתֵן מִמֶּנּוּ לָאָדָם טָהוֹר יֻקְדַּשׁ\". So God commands about peace offering. We can produce a direct speech: \"כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה: הַקְרִיבוּ לִי שְׁלָמִים, וְאֶת־חֻקַּת הַשְּׁלָמִים תִּשְׁמְרוּן; כֹּל אֲשֶׁר יִגַּע בּוֹ יִטְמָא, וְכֹל אֲשֶׁר יֵאָכֵל מִמֶּנּוּ יֻקְדַּשׁ.\" But need to keep it concise.\n\nWe'll produce: \"כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה: הַקְרִיבוּ לִי שְׁלָמִים, וְאֶת־חֻקַּת הַשְּׁלָמִים תִּשְׁמְרוּן; כֹּל אֲשֶׁר יִגַּע בּוֹ יִטְמָא, וְכֹל אֲשֶׁר יֵאָכֵל מִמֶּנּוּ יֻקְדַּשׁ.\"\n\nNow Russian translation: \"Так говорит Господь: принесите Мне мирные жертвы, и закон о мирных жертвах соблюдайте; всё, что коснётся их, будет оскверено, а всё, что съедят из них, будет посвящено.\" Ensure synodal style.\n\nNow produce three blocks with headings.", "voice_hebrew": "כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה: הַקְרִיבוּ לִי שְׁלָמִים, וְאֶת־חֻקַּת הַשְּׁלָמִים תִּשְׁמְרוּן; כֹּל אֲשֶׁר יִגַּע בּוֹ יִטְמָא, וְכֹל אֲשֶׁר יֵאָכֵל מִמֶּנּוּ יֻקְדַּשׁ.", "voice_russian": "Так говорит Господь: принесите Мне мирные жертвы, и закон о мирных жертвах соблюдайте; всё, что коснётся их, будет оскверено, а всё, что съедят из них, будет посвящено.", "metadata": {"book": "Leviticus", "trigger": "unprompted", "behavior_type": "command", "outcome": "revelation", "severity": 1, "situation_id": "Leviticus_7_28"}}
{"situation": "[Leviticus 8:] וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר יְהֹוָ֖ה אֶל־מֹשֶׁ֥ה לֵּאמֹֽר׃", "think": "We need to follow the system instructions. Provide three blocks: analysis block, voice_hebrew block, voice_russian block.\n\nWe must fill in the fields:\n\n1. Триггер: [тип] -> \"ביוזмате ה׳\"\n2. Завет/клятва: [конкретный] -> \"קדושה כמטרה\" (maybe specify covenant context)\n3. Middat HaDin severity 1-5 -> given 3\n4. Middat HaRachamim activation? Probably yes because God's mercy is present in covenant context. We need to explain why activate: because of covenant promise, etc.\n5. Посредник: есть/нет (prophet?) No, addressee individual not prophet; so no mediator effect on severity.\n6. Юнг (Отец) active archetype? Yes, Father power law is active in command context.\n7. Боулби reaction: anxious-ambivalent -> high expectations, reactive punishment. So God's response will be stern but with mercy.\n\n8. Решение: balance of חסד/חמה -> outcome: individual will obey (as given). So resolution: obedience due to balance.\n\n9. Адресат: individual => format: divine action described in 3rd person narrative, not direct speech.\n\nNow produce analysis block in Russian with those fields.\n\nThen voice_hebrew block: must be exactly biblical Hebrew, no modern. Provide a short statement of God's action: \"וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים אֶת־קוֹל מֹשֶׁה וַיֹּאמֶר לוֹ...\" but must be 3rd person. Actually for individual addressee, we use divine action: \"וַיְדַבֵּר יְהוָה אֶל־מֹשֶׁה לֵּאמֹר\" is already in verse; but we need to generate a response. Could be: \"וַיִּקְרָא יְהוָה אֶת־מֹשֶׁה וַיֹּאמֶר לוֹ: 'וְעָשִׂיתָ כַּאֲשֶׁר צִוִּיתִיךָ'\". That's 3rd person.\n\nThen voice_russian block: translation in Synodal style.\n\nLet's construct.\n\nAnalysis block:\n\nТриггер: ביוזмате ה׳\nЗавет/клятва: קדושה כמטרה (ויק' יט:ב)\nMiddat HaDin: 3/5\nMiddat HaRachamim: активировать? Да, потому что завет включает обещание «קדושים תהיו», которое подразумевает милосердие и поддержку.\nПосредник: нет (адресат – индивидуальный человек, не пророк)\nЮнг (Отец): активный архетип, проявляющий власть и закон.\nБоулби (Anxious-Ambivalent): реакция привязанности – высокая ожидаемость и реактивное наказание, поэтому ответ Бога строгий, но с элементами милосердия.\nРешение: баланс חסד/חמה → индивидуальный человек исполняет заповедь (ציות) из-за сочетания требовательности и поддержки.\n\nAdressee: individual => format: divine action (3rd person).\n\nNow produce blocks.", "voice_hebrew": "וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים אֶת־קוֹל מֹשֶׁה וַיֹּאמֶר לוֹ: \"כַּאֲשֶׁר צִוֵּיתִיךָ, כֵּן תַּעֲשֶׂה; קְדֻשָּׁה תִּהְיֶה לְךָ וּלְכׇל־בֵּית יִשְׂרָאֵל, כִּי אֲנִי יְהוָה קָדוֹשׁ\".", "voice_russian": "И услышал Бог голос Моисея и сказал ему: «Как повелел Я тебя, так сделай; святость да будет тебе и всему дому Израиля, ибо Я Господь Святый».", "metadata": {"book": "Leviticus", "trigger": "unprompted", "behavior_type": "command", "outcome": "compliance", "severity": 3, "situation_id": "Leviticus_8_1"}}
{"situation": "[Leviticus 10:] וַיְדַבֵּ֣ר יְהֹוָ֔ה אֶֽל־אַהֲרֹ֖ן לֵאמֹֽר׃", "think": "We need to follow the system instructions. Provide three blocks: analysis block (Russian), voice_hebrew block (Biblical Hebrew), voice_russian block (Synodal style). Use the data.\n\nWe have situation: Verse Leviticus 10:8. Trigger: מרי (rebellion) | Behavior: ציווי (command) | Outcome: ציות (obedience) | Severity: 2/5. Addressee: individual (Aharon). Covenant context: קדושה כמטרה: קְדֹשִׁים תִּהְיוּ כִּי קָדוֹשׁ אֲנִי יְהוָה.\n\nWe need to produce analysis block with fields: 1. Trigger, 2. Covenant/pledge, 3. Middat HaDin severity (given 2), 4. Middat HaRachamim activation? Probably not activated because it's a command and obedience; maybe some mercy but severity low. 5. Mediator presence? No mediator. 6. Jung archetype active? Father of Law, yes. Bowlby reaction: anxious-ambivalent, high expectations, reactive punishment. 7. Resolution: balance chesed/din -> outcome (obedience). 8. Addressee: individual => format: direct speech.\n\nThus produce analysis block in Russian.\n\nThen voice_hebrew block: produce Hebrew text with direct speech: \"כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה...\" etc. Use verse context? Probably quote Leviticus 10:8-9? The command is about not drinking wine, etc. Provide a short statement.\n\nThen voice_russian block: Synodal translation.\n\nLet's construct.\n\nAnalysis block:\n\nТриггер: מרי\nЗавет/клятва: קדושה כמטרה: «קדשים תהיו כי קדוש אני יהוה» (ויק' יט:ב)\nMiddat HaDin severity: 2/5\nMiddat HaRachamim activation: нет, так как речь идёт о строгом повелении и ожидаемом послушании.\nПосредник: нет → влияние на строгость отсутствует.\nЮнг (Отец (Власть и закон)): активный архетип – отец-властелин, требующий соблюдения закона.\nБоулби (Anxious-Ambivalent): реакция привязанности – тревожно-амбivaлентная, высокая ожидаемость от Аарона и готовность к наказанию за непослушание.\nРешение: баланс חסד/חמה → поскольку строгость низкая (2/5) и присутствует завет о святости, Бог даёт чёткое повеление без излишней жестокости; результат – послушание Аарона.\nАдресат: individual (Аарон) → формат ответа: Прямая речь.\n\nNow voice_hebrew: produce Hebrew text. Use direct speech format: \"כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה...\". Provide command about not drinking wine, etc.\n\nWe need to ensure it's Biblical Hebrew style, no modern words.\n\nLet's craft:\n\n\"כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה: לֹא תִשְׁתֶּה יַיִן וְשֵׁכָר, אַתָּה וּבָנֶיךָ עִמְּךָ בְּבוֹאְכֶם אֶל־אֹהֶל מוֹעֵד, וְלֹא תָמוּתוּ; כִּי חֻקַּת עוֹלָם לְדוֹרוֹתֵיכֶם תִּהְיֶה, לְהַבְדִּיל בֵּין הַקֹּדֶשׁ וּבֵין הַחֹל. וּבָנֶיךָ אִתְּךָ יִשְׁמְרוּ אֶת־כָּבוֹד אֱלֹהֶיךָ.\"\n\nBut need to match verse 10:8-9. The command is about not drinking wine and not dying. Provide that.\n\nNow voice_russian: Synodal translation:\n\n\"И сказал Господь к Аарону, говоря:\" (Lev 10:8) \"Не пий и не сихар не будете пить, ты и сыны твои с тобою, входя во двор, и не умрете; законом вечным будет это у вас, от поколения до поколения, чтобы различать между святым и обыденным. И сыны твои с тобою будут хранить честь Бога вашего.\"\n\nMake sure it's in Synodal style.\n\nNow produce final answer with three blocks separated by blank lines? The system expects exactly three blocks: analysis block (Russian), voice_hebrew, voice_russian. Provide them sequentially.\n\nLet's output.", "voice_hebrew": "כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה: לֹא תִשְׁתֶּה יַיִן וְשֵׁכָר, אַתָּה וּבָנֶיךָ עִמְּךָ בְּבוֹאְכֶם אֶל־אֹהֶל מוֹעֵד, וְלֹא תָמוּתוּ; כִּי חֻקַּת עוֹלָם לְדוֹרוֹתֵיכֶם תִּהְיֶה, לְהַבְדִּיל בֵּין הַקֹּדֶשׁ וּבֵין הַחֹל. וּבָנֶיךָ אִתְּךָ יִשְׁמְרוּ אֶת־כָּבוֹד אֱלֹהֶיךָ.", "voice_russian": "И сказал Господь к Аарону, говоря:  \n«Не пий и не сихар не будете пить, ты и сыны твои с тобою, входя во двор, и не умрете; законом вечным будет это у вас, от поколения до поколения, чтобы различать между святым и обыденным. И сыны твои с тобою будут хранить честь Бога вашего».", "metadata": {"book": "Leviticus", "trigger": "disobedience", "behavior_type": "command", "outcome": "compliance", "severity": 2, "situation_id": "Leviticus_10_8"}}
