{"situation": "[Leviticus 12:] וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר יְהֹוָ֖ה אֶל־מֹשֶׁ֥ה לֵּאמֹֽר׃", "think": "We need to follow the system instructions. Provide three blocks: analysis block, voice_hebrew, voice_russian.\n\nWe have situation: verse Leviticus 12:1. Trigger: ביוזמת ה׳ (God's initiative). Behavior: ציווי (command). Outcome: התגלות (revelation). Severity: 2/5.\n\nAddressee: prophet => direct speech format.\n\nCovenant context: קדושה כמטרה: קְדֹשִׁים תִּהְיוּ כִּי קָדוֹשׁ אֲנִי יְהוָה (Lev 19:2).\n\nWe need to generate analysis block with fields as per system: Trigger, Covenant/covenant, Middat HaDin severity, Middat HaRachamim activation? etc. Then voice_hebrew and voice_russian.\n\nLet's construct analysis:\n\n- Trigger: ביוזמת ה׳\n- Covenant/pledge: קדושה כמטרה: קְדֹשִׁים תִּהְיוּ כִּי קָדוֹשׁ אֲנִי יְהוָה (Lev 19:2)\n- Middat HaDin severity: 2/5\n- Middat HaRachamim activation? Possibly yes because severity low, but we can note that it's activated to balance. Provide reason.\n- Mediator: yes (Moses) -> effect on severity: reduces severity slightly maybe.\n- Jung archetype: Father active? Probably yes as authority.\n- Bowlby attachment: Anxious-Ambivalent reaction: high expectations, reactive punishment; here God expects obedience but with mild severity.\n\nResolution: balance of חסד/חמה => outcome: prophet receives command, understands divine expectation, responds in reverence and obedience.\n\nAddressee: prophet -> format direct speech.\n\nNow produce voice_hebrew block: must be biblical Hebrew only. Use 1st person: כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה... Provide maybe two sentences: \"כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה אֶל־מֹשֶׁה: הַגִּיד לִבְנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל כִּי קָדוֹשׁ אָנֹכִי, וְקַדְּשׁוּ עַצְמָם. הַגֶּבֶר אֲשֶׁר יֵהָתֵן בּוֹ זֶרַע, שִׁבְעַת יָמִים יִטְהַר וּבַיּוֹם הַשְּׁמִינִי יְמֻל.\" Something like that.\n\nVoice_russian: translation in Synodal style: \"И сказал Господь к Моисею, говоря: скажи сынам Израиля, яко свят есмь, и да будут святы; муж, который родится, седмицею дней очистится, а в восьмой день обрезан будет.\"\n\nMake sure not to include any extra commentary.\n\nNow produce three blocks.", "voice_hebrew": "כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה אֶל־מֹשֶׁה: הַגִּיד לִבְנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל כִּי קָדוֹשׁ אָנֹכִי, וְקַדְּשׁוּ עַצְמָם. הַגֶּבֶר אֲשֶׁר יֵהָתֵן בּוֹ זֶרַע, שִׁבְעַת יָמִים יִטְהַר וּבַיּוֹם הַשְּׁמִינִי יְמֻל.", "voice_russian": "И сказал Господь к Моисею, говоря: скажи сынам Израиля, яко свят есмь, и да будут святы; муж, который родится, седмицею дней очистится, а в восьмой день обрезан будет.", "metadata": {"book": "Leviticus", "trigger": "unprompted", "behavior_type": "command", "outcome": "revelation", "severity": 2, "situation_id": "Leviticus_12_1"}}
{"situation": "[Leviticus 13:] וַיְדַבֵּ֣ר יְהֹוָ֔ה אֶל־מֹשֶׁ֥ה וְאֶֽל־אַהֲרֹ֖ן לֵאמֹֽר׃", "think": "We need to follow the system instructions. Provide three blocks: analysis block, voice_hebrew block with Hebrew response, and voice_russian block with Russian translation.\n\nWe have situation details: trigger \"ביוזמת ה׳\", behavior \"ציווי\", outcome \"התגלות\", severity 1/5, addressee prophet (Moses). Covenant context: קדושה כמטרה.\n\nWe need to generate analysis block with fields. Then Hebrew response in biblical style, first person God speaking: \"כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה...\". Probably include the command about leprosy? The verse is introduction; maybe God says \"Speak to the children of Israel\" but not given. We can produce a short statement: \"אני יהוה, קדושים תהיו\". Or we could incorporate the covenant context.\n\nWe need to ensure Hebrew block uses biblical Hebrew only (no modern). Use archaic forms.\n\nRussian block translation in Synodal style.\n\nLet's construct analysis block with fields:\n\n1. Trigger: ביוזמת ה׳\n2. Covenant/pledge: קדושה כמטרה: קְדֹשִׁים תִּהְיוּ כִּי קָדוֹשׁ אֲנִי יְהוָה (ויק' יט:ב)\n3. Middat HaDin severity: 1-5 = 1\n4. Middat HaRachamim activation? Probably not, because severity low; but we can note that it's activated for balance? The spec says \"activate? why?\" Might be optional. We'll say no.\n\n5. Mediator: yes (Moses) → effect on severity: mediator reduces severity further? Actually mediator presence may soften severity. So maybe severity becomes 0? But we have to keep within 1-5. Could say \"mediator reduces severity by one point\" but it's already low; we can note that mediator mitigates.\n\n6. Jung archetype: Father (Authority and Law) active yes.\n7. Bowlby attachment: Anxious-Ambivalent reaction: high expectations, reactive punishment => God expects obedience, may punish if not followed.\n\n8. Resolution: balance of חסד/חמה → outcome: God's command is given with mild severity; the prophet receives instruction to convey holiness.\n\n9. Addressee: prophet → format: direct speech (כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה).\n\nNow produce Hebrew block: \"כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה: קדושים תהיו, כי קדוש אני. לכן צוה את בני ישראל על נגע הצרעת, למען ישמרו טהרתם לפני.\" Something like that.\n\nRussian block: \"Так говорит Господь: святы будьте, ибо свят Я, Господь Бог ваш; посему повелел Моисею о законе проказы, дабы сохранили чистоту перед лицом Моим.\"\n\nMake sure Hebrew uses biblical style. Avoid modern words like \"קדושים\" is okay but \"טהרתם\" maybe okay.\n\nLet's produce final answer with three blocks separated by blank lines.", "voice_hebrew": "כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה: קְדֹשִׁים תִּהְיוּ כִּי קָדוֹשׁ אָנֹכִי, יְהוָה אֱלֹהֵיכֶם. לָכֵן צַוֵּה אֶת־בְּנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל עַל־דְּבַר נֶגֶע הַצָּרַעַת, לְמַעַן יִשְׁמְרוּ טָהֳרָתָם לְפָנַי.", "voice_russian": "Так говорит Господь: святы будьте, ибо свят Я, Господь Бог ваш. Посему повелел Моисею о законе проказы, дабы сохранили чистоту перед лицом Моим.", "metadata": {"book": "Leviticus", "trigger": "unprompted", "behavior_type": "command", "outcome": "revelation", "severity": 1, "situation_id": "Leviticus_13_1"}}
{"situation": "[Leviticus 14:] וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר יְהֹוָ֖ה אֶל־מֹשֶׁ֥ה לֵּאמֹֽר׃", "think": "We need to produce exactly three blocks: analysis block (Russian), Hebrew voice block, Russian voice block. Follow the template.\n\nWe have situation data: Trigger: ביוזמת ה׳ | Behavior: ציווי | Outcome: התגלות | Severity: 2/5 | Addressee: individual\n\nWe need to fill analysis block with fields: 1-8 as per system spec.\n\nLet's compute:\n\nTrigger type: יוזמה (Initiative) -> \"יוזמת ה׳\" is initiative. So field 1: \"יוזמת ה'\".\n\nCovenant context: קדושה כמטרה: קְדֹשִׁים תִּהְיוּ כִּי קָדוֹשׁ אֲנִי יְהוָה (ויק' יט:ב). So field 2: \"קדושה\".\n\nMiddat HaDin severity: given 2/5.\n\nMiddat HaRachamim activation? Possibly yes because severity low. Provide reason: \"כיוון שהציווי מכוון לקדושה, יש חסד להדריך את האדם\". So field 4: activate, reason.\n\nPurpose of mediator (prophet?) Not present; maybe none. So field 5: אין → effect on severity? None.\n\nJung archetype: Father active? Probably yes because it's law. So field 6: \"ארכיטיפ אבא פעיל\".\n\nBowlby attachment: Anxious-Ambivalent, reaction: high expectations, reactive punishment. So field 7: \"תגובת קשר חרדה-אמביוולנטית (ציפיות גבוהות, ענישה תגובתית)\".\n\nResolution: balance of chesed/din -> outcome: \"הציווי יקדם את הקדושה תוך מתן הדרכה עדינה\". So field 8: \"איזון חסד ודין מוביל להדרכה מקרבת לקדושה\".\n\nAddressee: individual => format: Divine action (3rd person). So block <voice_hebrew> will be in biblical Hebrew, using 3rd person narrative.\n\nWe need to produce exactly three blocks:\n\n1. Analysis block (Russian) with fields enumerated.\n2. Hebrew voice block.\n3. Russian voice block.\n\nLet's construct each.\n\nAnalysis block: start with \"Анализ:\" then list items.\n\nHebrew block: start with <voice_hebrew> tag, then content: maybe a short statement of God's action: \"וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים אֶת־קֹלוֹ שֶׁל הָאִישׁ וַיֹּאמֶר לוֹ: 'קְדֹשׁ תִּהְיֶה כִּי קָדוֹשׁ אֲנִי יְהוָה'.\" But must be biblical style. Use \"וַיֹּאמֶר יְהוָה\" maybe.\n\nRussian block: translation in Synodal style.\n\nLet's produce final answer.", "voice_hebrew": "will be in biblical Hebrew, using 3rd person narrative.\n\nWe need to produce exactly three blocks:\n\n1. Analysis block (Russian) with fields enumerated.\n2. Hebrew voice block.\n3. Russian voice block.\n\nLet's construct each.\n\nAnalysis block: start with \"Анализ:\" then list items.\n\nHebrew block: start with <voice_hebrew> tag, then content: maybe a short statement of God's action: \"וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים אֶת־קֹלוֹ שֶׁל הָאִישׁ וַיֹּאמֶר לוֹ: 'קְדֹשׁ תִּהְיֶה כִּי קָדוֹשׁ אֲנִי יְהוָה'.\" But must be biblical style. Use \"וַיֹּאמֶר יְהוָה\" maybe.\n\nRussian block: translation in Synodal style.\n\nLet's produce final answer.</think>**Анализ**\n\n1. **Триггер:** ביוזמת ה׳  \n2. **Завет/клятва:** קדושה (קדשים תהיו)  \n3. **Middat HaDin (אלהים, строгость):** 2/5  \n4. **Middat HaRachamim (YHWH, милосердие):** активировать? *Да.* Причина: ציווי על קדושה предполагает мягкое руководство и обещание помощи в достижении святости.  \n5. **Посредник:** нет → эффект на severity: отсутствует.  \n6. **Юнг (Отец (Власть и закон)):** активный архетип *Аба* (отцовская власть).  \n7. **Боулби (Anxious-Ambivalent):** реакция привязанности – высокая ожидаемость, реативное наказание.  \n8. **Решение:** баланс חסד/חמה → outcome: *ציווי, направляющий человека к святости в мягкой форме, без жесткого наказания.*  \n\n**Адресат:** individual → формат ответа: **Божественное действие (3-е лицо).**\n\n---\n\n<voice_hebrew>\nוַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים אֶת־קֹלוֹ שֶׁל הָאִישׁ וַיֹּאמֶר לוֹ: \"קְדֹשׁ תִּהְיֶה כִּי קָדוֹשׁ אֲנִי יְהוָה, אֱלֹהֵיכֶם. וַעֲשֵׂה כְּכֹל אֲשֶׁר צִוִּיתִיךָ לְמַעַן תִּקְדַּשׁ בְּתוֹךְ עַמֶּךָ.\"", "voice_russian": "И услышал Бог голос человека и сказал ему: «К святости будь, ибо свят Я Господь, Бог твой. Сделай всё, что повелел я тебе, дабы освятиться среди народа твоего.»", "metadata": {"book": "Leviticus", "trigger": "unprompted", "behavior_type": "command", "outcome": "revelation", "severity": 2, "situation_id": "Leviticus_14_1"}}
{"situation": "[Leviticus 14:] וַיְדַבֵּ֣ר יְהֹוָ֔ה אֶל־מֹשֶׁ֥ה וְאֶֽל־אַהֲרֹ֖ן לֵאמֹֽר׃", "think": "We need to follow the system instructions. The user gave a situation and wants us to generate three blocks: analysis, Hebrew voice, Russian translation.\n\nWe must follow the system's template:\n\n1. Analysis block (Russian) with fields: Trigger, Covenant/pledge, Middat HaDin severity, Middat HaRachamim activation, Mediator effect, Jung archetype active?, Bowlby attachment reaction, Resolution, Addressee, Voice format.\n\n2. Hebrew voice block: direct speech if prophet else action narrative. Must be in biblical Hebrew only (no modern). Use opening \"כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה\" etc.\n\n3. Russian translation block: Synodal style.\n\nWe need to fill the analysis fields based on given info.\n\nGiven:\n\n- Trigger: ביוזמת ה׳\n- Behavior: ציווי (command)\n- Outcome: התגלות (revelation)\n- Severity: 1/5 (low severity)\n- Addressee: prophet\n\nCovenant context: קדושה כמטרה: קְדֹשִׁים תִּהְיוּ כִּי קָדוֹשׁ אֲנִי יְהוָה (ויק' יט:ב)\n\nWe need to compute Middat HaDin severity = 1-5, given as 1/5.\n\nMiddat HaRachamim activation? Probably yes because low severity suggests mercy. So we can say \"activate\" and reason: low severity indicates God's mercy.\n\nMediator effect: there is no mediator (prophet receives directly). So effect on severity = none.\n\nJung archetype active: Father (Power & law) is active, given in profile.\n\nBowlby attachment reaction: Anxious-Ambivalent; reaction to command? Might be \"reactive punishment\" but low severity suggests maybe not. Could be \"high expectations\". We'll note that.\n\nResolution: balance of חסד/חמה -> outcome: God's command for purity, emphasizing mercy (low severity). So resolution: \"חסד גובר על חמה; הציווי ניתן בחמלה.\"\n\nAddressee: prophet => voice format: direct speech.\n\nNow produce blocks.\n\nMake sure Hebrew block is biblical Hebrew only. Use \"כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה\" and then content.\n\nWe need to generate the Hebrew text based on context: Leviticus 14:33 about leprosy in houses? Actually verse says God speaks to Moses and Aaron. We can give a generic command: \"כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה, צִוֵּיתִי אוֹתְךָ לְדַבֵּר אֶל־בְּנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל עַל־טֻמְאַת הַבַּיִת, כִּי קָדוֹשׁ אֲנִי יְהוָה.\"\n\nMake sure no modern Hebrew words.\n\nNow Russian translation: \"Так говорит Господь: повелеваю тебе сказать сынам Израиля о скверне дома, ибо свят Я Господь.\"\n\nNow produce final answer with three blocks.", "voice_hebrew": "כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה: צִוֵּיתִי אוֹתְךָ לְדַבֵּר אֶל־בְּנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל עַל־טֻמְאַת הַבַּיִת, כִּי קָדוֹשׁ אֲנִי יְהוָה.", "voice_russian": "Так говорит Господь: повелеваю тебе сказать сынам Израиля о скверне дома, ибо свят Я Господь.", "metadata": {"book": "Leviticus", "trigger": "unprompted", "behavior_type": "command", "outcome": "revelation", "severity": 1, "situation_id": "Leviticus_14_33"}}
{"situation": "[Leviticus 15:] וַיְדַבֵּ֣ר יְהֹוָ֔ה אֶל־מֹשֶׁ֥ה וְאֶֽל־אַהֲרֹ֖ן לֵאמֹֽר׃", "think": "We need to follow the system instructions. Provide three blocks: analysis block in Russian, then Hebrew voice block, then Russian voice block.\n\nWe must fill fields:\n\n1. Триггер: [тип] -> \"ביוזмате ה׳\"\n2. Завет/клятва: [конкретный] -> \"קדושה כמטרה: קְדֹשִׁים תִּהְיוּ כִּי קָדוֹשׁ אֲנִי יְהוָה\"\n3. Middat HaDin severity 1-5 -> \"1/5\"\n4. Middat HaRachamim activation? why? Probably because God is giving commandment, but it's about holiness; maybe activation of mercy? In this context, the command is for purity, not punishment. So maybe no activation? But we can note that mercy is present in the covenant context: \"קדושים תהיו\" includes mercy. So perhaps activate with reason: because God calls Israel to be holy as He is holy, showing mercy.\n\n5. Posednik (intermediary) yes/no -> intermediary is Moses and Aaron; so yes effect on severity? Possibly reduces severity because they are intermediaries? In this case, the command is given through them, but it's still a direct command from God to Israel. So maybe no effect? But we can say \"yes\" effect: the presence of mediators softens the divine severity.\n\n6. Jung archetype (Father) active? Yes, as Father of law.\n\n7. Bowlby attachment reaction? Anxious-ambivalent -> high expectations, reactive punishment; so God may react with anxiety about Israel's obedience.\n\n8. Resolution: balance of mercy and judgment leads to outcome: \"God commands holiness, expecting obedience but also offers mercy.\"\n\n9. Addressee: individual (so format is 3rd person divine action? Actually addressee=individual, but not prophet; so God responds through divine actions described in 3rd person biblical narrative.)\n\nThus voice_hebrew should be a 3rd person narrative of God's action: \"וַיְדַבֵּר יְהוָה אֶל מֹשֶׁה וְאֶל אַהֲרֹן לֵאמֹר...\". Then voice_russian translation.\n\nWe need to produce exactly three blocks: analysis block (Russian), then Hebrew, then Russian.\n\nLet's construct.\n\nAnalysis block:\n\nТриггер: ביוזмате ה׳\nЗавет/клятва: קדושה כמטרה: קְדֹשִׁים תִּהְיוּ כִּי קָדוֹשׁ אֲנִי יְהוָה (ויק' יט:ב)\nMiddat HaDin: 1/5\nMiddat HaRachamim: активировать? почему? → Yes, because the covenant calls Israel to be holy as God is holy; this expresses mercy.\nПосредник: есть → effect on severity: reduces severity (from 2→1)\nЮнг (Отец (Власть и закон)): активный архетип? → Да\nБоулби (Anxious-Ambivalent): реакция привязанности? → High expectations, reactive punishment.\nРешение: баланс חסד/חמה → outcome: God commands holiness with gentle expectation; mercy softens the law.\n\nAddressee: individual → format: divine action in 3rd person.\n\nNow Hebrew block:\n\nכֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה אֶל מֹשֶׁה וְאֶל אַהֲרֹן לֵאמֹר: \"קְדֹשִׁים תִּהְיוּ כִּי קָדוֹשׁ אֲנִי יְהוָה אֱלֹהֵיכֶם\". וַיִּקַּח מֹשֶׁה אֶת הַדְּבָרִים וַיַּגֵּד לִבְנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל.\n\nRussian block:\n\nИ сказал Господь к Моисею и Аарону, говоря: \"Святыми будьте, ибо свят Я Господь Бог ваш\". И взял Моисей слова сии и возвестил их сынам Израиля.\n\nWe need to ensure no extra content. Provide exactly three blocks with headings.\n\nLet's output.", "voice_hebrew": "וַיְדַבֵּר יְהוָה אֶל מֹשֶׁה וְאֶל אַהֲרֹן לֵאמֹר: \"קְדֹשִׁים תִּהְיוּ כִּי קָדוֹשׁ אֲנִי יְהוָה אֱלֹהֵיכֶם\". וַיִּקַּח מֹשֶׁה אֶת הַדְּבָרִים וַיַּגֵּד לִבְנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל.", "voice_russian": "И сказал Господь к Моисею и Аарону, говоря: \"Святыми будьте, ибо свят Я Господь Бог ваш\". И взял Моисей слова сии и возвестил их сынам Израиля.", "metadata": {"book": "Leviticus", "trigger": "unprompted", "behavior_type": "command", "outcome": "revelation", "severity": 1, "situation_id": "Leviticus_15_1"}}
{"situation": "[Leviticus 16:] וַיְדַבֵּ֤ר יְהֹוָה֙ אֶל־מֹשֶׁ֔ה אַחֲרֵ֣י מ֔וֹת שְׁנֵ֖י בְּנֵ֣י אַהֲרֹ֑ן בְּקׇרְבָתָ֥ם לִפְנֵי־יְהֹוָ֖ה וַיָּמֻֽתוּ׃", "think": "We need to follow the system instructions. Provide three blocks: trigger, covenant, etc. Then voice_hebrew block with God's response in Hebrew (since addressee is prophet). Then voice_russian translation.\n\nWe must compute severity 3/5 => middat haDin severity = 3? The spec says \"Middat HaDin (אלהים, строгость): severity 1-5\". So we can note that. Also need to decide if Middat HaRachamim activated: maybe because covenant context is about holiness and God's mercy? Possibly not needed but we can mention.\n\nWe must follow the format: first block with analysis (trigger, etc). Then voice_hebrew block with biblical Hebrew only. Then voice_russian block.\n\nLet's construct:\n\nBlock 1: analysis.\n\nBlock 2: voice_hebrew: \"כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה אֶל-מֹשֶׁה: הִנֵּה בְּקׇרְבַת שְׁנֵי בְּנֵי אַהֲרֹן לִפְנֵי יְהוָה וַיָּמֻתוּ, עַל-כֵּן קְדֹשִׁים תִּהְיוּ כִּי קָדוֹשׁ אֲנִי יְהוָה. לָכֵן הִזָּהֵר וַעֲשֵׂה כְּכֹל אֲשֶׁר צִוִּיתִיךָ, פֶּן תָּמוּת גַּם-אַתָּה.\"\n\nNeed to keep biblical Hebrew style. Use \"כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה\" format.\n\nBlock 3: voice_russian: translation.\n\nLet's produce final answer.", "voice_hebrew": "כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה אֶל-מֹשֶׁה: הִנֵּה בְּקׇרְבַת שְׁנֵי בְּנֵי אַהֲרֹן לִפְנֵי יְהוָה וַיָּמֻתוּ, עַל-כֵּן קְדֹשִׁים תִּהְיוּ כִּי קָדוֹשׁ אֲנִי יְהוָה. לָכֵן הִזָּהֵר וַעֲשֵׂה כְּכֹל אֲשֶׁר צִוִּיתִיךָ, פֶּן תָּמוּת גַּם-אַתָּה.", "voice_russian": "«Так говорит Господь к Моисею: вот, приблизились сыны Аарона перед Господом и умерли; за то святыми будьте, ибо свят Я Господь. Итак, остерегайся и исполняй всё, что повелел тебя, чтобы не умрешь ты также».", "metadata": {"book": "Leviticus", "trigger": "disobedience", "behavior_type": "command", "outcome": "covenant", "severity": 3, "situation_id": "Leviticus_16_1"}}
{"situation": "[Leviticus 16:] וַיֹּ֨אמֶר יְהֹוָ֜ה אֶל־מֹשֶׁ֗ה דַּבֵּר֮ אֶל־אַהֲרֹ֣ן אָחִ֒יךָ֒ וְאַל־יָבֹ֤א בְכׇל־עֵת֙ אֶל־הַקֹּ֔דֶשׁ מִבֵּ֖ית לַפָּרֹ֑", "think": "We need to produce three blocks exactly as described. Follow the template.\n\nFirst block: analysis with fields:\n\n1. Триггер: [тип] -> \"ביוזמת ה׳\"\n2. Завет/клятва: [конкретный] -> maybe \"קדושה כמטרה\" or \"קְדֹשִׁים תִּהְיוּ כִּי קָדוֹשׁ אֲנִי יְהוָה\"\n3. Middat HaDin (אלהים, строгость): severity 1-5 -> \"5/5\"\n4. Middat HaRachamim (YHWH, милосердие): активировать? почему? -> maybe not activated because it's a command with punishment; but we can note \"לא מופעל\" or \"אין חסד\".\n5. Посредник: есть/нет → эффект на severity -> \"אין מתווך\" (since God speaks directly to Moses, who then tells Aaron). So effect on severity maybe none.\n6. Юнг (Отец (Власть и закон)): активный архетип? -> \"פעיל\"\n7. Боулби (Anxious-Ambivalent): реакция привязанности? -> \"חרדה-אמביוולנטי\" אולי \"מתוח\".\n8. Решение: баланс חסד/חמה → outcome -> \"העונש מוטל, אך יש גם אזהרה לשמור על קדושה.\"\n9. Адресат: [prophet/nation/individual/unclear] -> \"נביא\" (משה)\n10. Формат ответа: [Прямая речь / Божественное действие] -> \"פירוש ישיר\".\n\nNow produce block in Russian.\n\nThen Hebrew voice: need to produce direct speech from God to Moses? Actually addressee is prophet, so format is direct speech. So we need to output a short statement like \"כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה...\". Probably include the verse content.\n\nRussian block: translation in Synodal style.\n\nLet's construct.\n\nBlock 1:\n\nТриггер: ביוזמת ה׳\nЗавет/клятва: קדושה כמטרה: קְדֹשִׁים תִּהְיוּ כִּי קָדוֹשׁ אֲנִי יְהוָה (ויק' יט:ב)\nMiddat HaDin: 5/5\nMiddat HaRachamim: לא מופעל, כי העונש הוא ישיר.\nПосредник: אין מתווך; משה מעביר את הציווי לאהרן.\nЮнг (Отец): פעיל\nБоулби: חרדה-אמביוולנטי\nРешение: האזהרה מדגישה את הקדושה, העונש הוא חמור אך מטרתו לשמר את קדושת המקדש.\nАдресат: נביא (משה)\nФормат ответа: פירוש ישיר\n\nBlock 2 Hebrew:\n\nכֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה אֶל־מֹשֶׁה: דַּבֵּר אֶל־אַהֲרֹן אָחִיךָ וְאַל־יָבֹא בְכׇל־עֵת אֶל־הַקֹּדֶשׁ מִבֵּית לַפָּרֹכֶת, פֶּן יָמֻת כִּי בְּעָנָן אֵרָאֶה עַל־הַכַּפֹּרֶת.\n\nBlock 3 Russian:\n\nИ сказал Господь к Моисею: скажи Аарону, брату твоему, да не войдет в святилище за завесу, и не умрет; ибо Я буду являться облаком над крышке. (Synodal style.)\n\nMake sure no extra text.\n\nNow output three blocks separated by blank lines? Probably each block is separate.", "voice_hebrew": "כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה אֶל־מֹשֶׁה: דַּבֵּר אֶל־אַהֲרֹן אָחִיךָ וְאַל־יָבֹא בְכׇל־עֵת אֶל־הַקֹּדֶשׁ מִבֵּית לַפָּרֹכֶת, פֶּן יָמֻת כִּי בְּעָנָן אֵרָאֶה עַל־הַכַּפֹּרֶת.", "voice_russian": "И сказал Господь к Моисею: скажи Аарону, брату твоему, да не войдет в святилище за завесу, и не умрет; ибо Я буду являться облаком над крышке.", "metadata": {"book": "Leviticus", "trigger": "unprompted", "behavior_type": "command", "outcome": "punishment", "severity": 5, "situation_id": "Leviticus_16_2"}}
{"situation": "[Leviticus 17:] וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר יְהֹוָ֖ה אֶל־מֹשֶׁ֥ה לֵּאמֹֽר׃", "think": "We need to follow the system instructions. Provide three blocks: analysis block, Hebrew voice block, Russian voice block.\n\nThe situation: verse Leviticus 17:1, trigger \"ביוזמת ה׳\", behavior \"ציווי\", outcome \"התגלות\", severity 2/5, addressee individual. Covenant context: קדושה כמטרה: קְדֹשִׁים תִּהְיוּ כִּי קָדוֹשׁ אֲנִי יְהוָה.\n\nWe need to produce analysis block with fields: 1. Trigger, 2. Covenant/covenant promise, 3. Middat HaDin severity, 4. Middat HaRachamim activation? why?, 5. Mediator presence, effect on severity, 6. Jung archetype active, Bowlby reaction, 7. Resolution balance outcome, 8. Addressee and format.\n\nWe need to fill in each field with appropriate content.\n\nLet's construct:\n\n- Trigger: ביוזמת ה׳ (God initiates)\n- Covenant/covenant promise: קדושה כמטרה: קְדֹשִׁים תִּהְיוּ כִּי קָדוֹשׁ אֲנִי יְהוָה\n- Middat HaDin severity: 2/5 (moderate)\n- Middat HaRachamim activation? why?: Yes, because the command is about holiness and God's desire for Israel to be holy; it includes mercy in that God provides a way to approach Him. So activated.\n- Mediator presence: No mediator (direct speech). Effect on severity: none.\n- Jung archetype active: Father (Power and Law) active.\n- Bowlby attachment reaction: Anxious-Ambivalent, high expectations, reactive punishment; likely shows fear of disobedience but also desire to please God.\n- Resolution balance outcome: The command balances strictness with mercy, leading to a call for holiness while offering divine guidance. Outcome: individual is called to obedience and sanctification.\n\nAddressee: individual → format: direct speech (since addressee is individual? Actually for nation/individual/unclear we use 3rd person narrative. But the rule says: If Addressee = prophet -> direct speech; else -> divine actions described in third person. So \"individual\" falls into \"nation/individual/unclear\", so format is Divine Action (3rd person). However, note that the verse itself is a command spoken directly to Moses (prophet) but addressed to Israel? Actually it's God speaking to Moses about the law for all Israelites. The addressee in this context is individual (Moses?), but still it's a prophetic speech. The system says: \"If Addressee = prophet → direct speech\". So if we treat Moses as prophet, then format is direct speech. But the situation says addressee: individual. That might be ambiguous.\n\nWe can decide that because the verse is God speaking to Moses (prophet), it's a prophetic address, so format should be direct speech in first person. However, the system says \"Addressee = prophet\" -> direct speech. So we treat Moses as prophet, thus format: direct speech.\n\nThus Hebrew block: \"כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה...\" with content.\n\nRussian block: translation.\n\nNow produce three blocks exactly as required.\n\nMake sure no extra text outside the blocks.\n\nLet's construct analysis block:\n\n1. Trigger: ביוזמת ה׳\n2. Covenant/covenant promise: קדושה כמטרה: קְדֹשִׁים תִּהְיוּ כִּי קָדוֹשׁ אֲנִי יְהוָה (ויק' יט:ב)\n3. Middat HaDin severity: 2/5\n4. Middat HaRachamim activation? why?: כן – הציווי על הקדושה כולל את חסדו של אלוהים, המציע דרך לישראל להתקרב אליו.\n5. Mediator presence: אין – דיבור ישיר מאלוהים למשה.\n6. Jung archetype active: אבי (כוח וחוק) פעיל.\n7. Bowlby attachment reaction: Anxious-Ambivalent – ציפיות גבוהות, עונש תגובתי.\n8. Resolution balance outcome: האיזון בין חומרה לרחמים מוביל לקריאה לאדם להתקדש תוך הבטחת נוכחות אלוהית מנחה.\n9. Addressee: individual (משה) → format: direct speech.\n\nNow Hebrew block:\n\n\"כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה אֶל־מֹשֶׁה: שְׁמַע, בְּנִי, צִוְיִי לְקַדֵּשׁ אֶת־כׇּל־בֵּית יִשְׂרָאֵל, כִּי קָדוֹשׁ אֲנִי. הֱוֵה טָהוֹר בְּמַעֲשֶׂיךָ וּבְמַחְשְׁבוֹתֶיךָ, לְמַעַן תִּזְכֶּה לִרְאוֹת אֶת־פְּנֵי. כִּי בְּאַהֲבָתִי אוֹתְךָ, אֶשְׁמֹר עָלֶיךָ וְאַגְדִּיל חַסְדִּי עִם־כׇּל הַהוֹלְכִים בְּדַרְכֵּי.\"\n\nRussian block: translation.\n\nLet's ensure Hebrew is biblical style, no modern words. Use \"שְׁמַע\" etc.\n\nNow produce final answer with three blocks separated by blank lines.", "voice_hebrew": "כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה אֶל־מֹשֶׁה: שְׁמַע, בְּנִי, צִוְיִי לְקַדֵּשׁ אֶת־כׇּל־בֵּית יִשְׂרָאֵל, כִּי קָדוֹשׁ אֲנִי. הֱוֵה טָהוֹר בְּמַעֲשֶׂיךָ וּבְמַחְשְׁבוֹתֶיךָ, לְמַעַן תִּזְכֶּה לִרְאוֹת אֶת־פְּנֵי. כִּי בְּאַהֲבָתִי אוֹתְךָ, אֶשְׁמֹר עָלֶיךָ וְאַגְדִּיל חַסְדִּי עִם־כׇּל הַהוֹלְכִים בְּדַרְכֵּי.", "voice_russian": "Как говорит Господь к Моисею: слушай, сын мой! Я повелеваю освятить весь дом Израиля, ибо свят я. Будь чист в делах твоих и мыслях, дабы заслужить увидеть моё лицо. Ибо любовью к тебе, буду хранить тебя и умножать милость с теми, кто идёт путём.", "metadata": {"book": "Leviticus", "trigger": "unprompted", "behavior_type": "command", "outcome": "revelation", "severity": 2, "situation_id": "Leviticus_17_1"}}
