igger: ביוזמת ה' → God initiates.\n2. Covenant/pledge: Leviticus 19:2 \"קדושים תהיו כי קדוש אני יהוה\" – establishes holiness as covenant goal.\n3. Middat HaDin severity: 4/5 (high).\n4. Middat HaRachamim activation? No, because high severity; God emphasizes judgment.\n5. Mediator: no mediator needed for direct speech to prophet.\n6. Jung archetype: Father (authority and law) active.\n7. Bowlby attachment: Anxious-Ambivalent – God expects strict obedience, reacts with stern punishment if violated.\n8. Resolution: Balance of חסד/חמה → outcome: command to be holy; threat of divine punishment for violation.\n\nNow produce Hebrew block:\n\n\"כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה אֶל־מֹשֶׁה: קְדֹשִׁים תִּהְיוּ כִּי קָדוֹשׁ אֲנִי יְהוָה. הַשֹּׁמֵר אֶת־מִצְוֹתַי וְהוֹלֵךְ בְּדַרְכֵי קָדְשִׁי יִחְיֶה, וְאִם לֹא – עֻנְשִׁים חֲמֻרִים יִפְּלוּ עַל־הַמַּעֲבִיר.\"\n\nNote: Use biblical Hebrew style.\n\nNow Russian translation:\n\n\"Так говорит Господь к Моисею: «Святы будьте, ибо свят Я, Господь Бог ваш. Сторожущий заповеди Мои и ходящий путями святости — да живет; а если не, то тяжкие муки падут на грехопавшего».\"\nWe need to ensure Russian translation is Synodal style.\n\nNow produce final answer with three blocks separated by blank lines.", "voice_hebrew": "block with Hebrew response format appropriate for addressee=individual => divine action third person narrative. Then <voice_russian> translation.\n\nWe need to compute severity 4/5, Middat HaDin etc.\n\nLet's construct analysis:\n\n- Trigger: ביוזמת ה׳\n- Behavior: ציווי (command)\n- Outcome: התגלות (revelation)\n- Severity: 4/5\n\nAddressee: individual => divine action format.\n\nWe need to decide middat haRachamim activation? Since severity high, maybe not activated. But we can note that due to severity, middat HaDin dominates.\n\nProvide analysis steps.\n\nThen Hebrew block: \"וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים אֶת־קוֹל מֹשֶׁה וַיֹּאמֶר...\". Actually need to produce a divine action statement. Could be: \"וַיֹּאמֶר יְהוָה אֶל־מֹשֶׁה לֵאמֹר: קְדֹשִׁים ת