{"situation": "[Leviticus 21:] וַיֹּ֤אמֶר יְהֹוָה֙ אֶל־מֹשֶׁ֔ה אֱמֹ֥ר אֶל־הַכֹּהֲנִ֖ים בְּנֵ֣י אַהֲרֹ֑ן וְאָמַרְתָּ֣ אֲלֵהֶ֔ם לְנֶ֥פֶשׁ לֹֽא־יִטַּמָּ֖א", "think": "We need to follow the system instructions. Provide three blocks: trigger, covenant/promise, Middat HaDin severity etc? Actually the system gave a template for each situation: produce exactly three blocks: first block is analysis (in Russian), second block is Hebrew voice, third block is Russian translation.\n\nWe need to fill in according to given data.\n\nWe have situation: Verse Leviticus 21:1. Trigger: ביוזמת ה׳ | Behavior: ציווי | Outcome: ציות | Severity: 2/5\nAddressee: nation\n\nThus analysis block will include steps:\n\n- Trigger type (Initiative of God)\n- Covenant/promise: specific? The covenant context is \"קדושה כמטרה: קְדֹשִׁים תִּהְיוּ כִּי קָדוֹשׁ אֲנִי יְהוָה\". So we can say \"קֹדֶשׁ כַּמַּטָּרָה\" (holiness as goal). Possibly mention that it's a covenant promise.\n\n- Middat HaDin severity: 2/5 (low-moderate)\n\n- Middat HaRachamim activation? Probably not needed but we can note if activated. Since severity low, maybe mercy is active.\n\n- Mediator: no mediator? It's God speaking directly to nation via Moses; mediator is Moses but effect on severity? Possibly reduces severity slightly.\n\n- Jung archetype: Father (Power and Law) active.\n\n- Bowlby attachment: Anxious-Ambivalent reaction: high expectations, reactive punishment. So reaction: God expects strict obedience, may punish if not obeyed.\n\n- Resolution: balance of mercy and justice leads to outcome: nation will be warned but not harshly punished; they must maintain holiness.\n\n- Addressee: nation => format: divine action (3rd person) because it's not a prophet. So voice_hebrew should be narrative: \"וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים...\" but we need to produce God's response, which is the verse itself? Actually the verse is command; we can present it as divine action: \"וַיֹּאמֶר יְהֹוָה אֶל מֹשֶׁה ...\". That is direct speech but to nation. According to core principle, for nation addressee we use third person narrative of God's actions. So maybe \"וַיִּצַּו יְהֹוָה אֶת מֹשֶׁה לֵאמֹר: ...\". That is 3rd person.\n\nThus voice_hebrew block will be a short narrative: \"וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים אֶת מֹשֶׁה וַיֹּאמֶר לוֹ: ...\". Or better: \"וַיֹּאמֶר יְהֹוָה אֶל־מֹשֶׁה לֵאמֹר: ...\".\n\nThen voice_russian block will be translation.\n\nNow produce three blocks exactly.\n\nMake sure no extra text outside the blocks.\n\nLet's construct:\n\nBlock 1 (analysis) in Russian.\n\nBlock 2 (voice_hebrew) Hebrew.\n\nBlock 3 (voice_russian) Russian.\n\nProceed.", "voice_hebrew": "וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים אֶת מֹשֶׁה וַיֹּאמֶר לוֹ: «אֱמֹר אֶל־הַכֹּהֲנִים בְּנֵי אַהֲרֹן, וְאָמַרְתָּ אֲלֵהֶם: לְנֶפֶשׁ לֹא־יִטַּמָּא בְּעַמּוֹ. כִּי קְדֹשִׁים יִהְיוּ לֵאלֹהֵיהֶם, וְלֹא יְחַלְּלוּ אֶת־שֵׁם אֱלֹהֵיהֶם».", "voice_russian": "И услышал Бог Моисея и сказал ему: «Скажи священникам, сынам Аарона, и скажи им: не оскверняйтесь мёртвыми в народе. Ибо святы они Богу своему, и не посрамить имя Бога своего».", "metadata": {"book": "Leviticus", "trigger": "unprompted", "behavior_type": "command", "outcome": "compliance", "severity": 2, "situation_id": "Leviticus_21_1"}}
{"situation": "[Leviticus 21:] וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר יְהֹוָ֖ה אֶל־מֹשֶׁ֥ה לֵּאמֹֽר׃", "think": "We need to follow the system instructions. We have a situation description. Need to produce three blocks: analysis block (Russian), voice_hebrew block (Biblical Hebrew), and voice_russian block (Synodal translation). Follow the template.\n\nWe must compute middat values, etc. Let's parse:\n\n- Trigger: ביוזמת ה׳\n- Behavior: ציווי\n- Outcome: לא מוגדר\n- Severity: 1/5\n\nAddressee: prophet => God speaks directly in first person.\n\nCovenant context: קדושה כמטרה: קְדֹשִׁים תִּהְיוּ כִּי קָדוֹשׁ אֲנִי יְהוָה (ויק' יט:ב)\n\nWe need to produce analysis block with steps 1-8.\n\nLet's compute:\n\n1. Trigger: ביוזמת ה׳ → God initiates.\n\n2. Covenant/pledge: The covenant context is about holiness, so the pledge is \"קדושה כמטרה\" -> \"to be holy as I am holy\".\n\n3. Middat HaDin severity: given 1/5 (low).\n\n4. Middat HaRachamim activation? Probably not needed because low severity; but maybe some mercy in giving command to keep holiness.\n\n5. Mediator: none? Since it's direct speech to prophet, no mediator effect.\n\n6. Jung archetype: Father (Power and Law) active.\n\n7. Bowlby attachment: Anxious-Ambivalent → God expects high standards, reactive punishment if not obeyed; but in this case low severity.\n\n8. Resolution: Balance of chesed/din -> outcome: The prophet receives a gentle command to maintain holiness; likely outcome is obedience and sanctification.\n\nNow produce blocks.\n\nAnalysis block (Russian) with steps enumerated.\n\nVoice_hebrew: Provide Biblical Hebrew answer, using \"כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה\" format. It should be a short statement reflecting the command about priests not having blemishes? Actually verse 16 is about priests with blemish cannot approach the altar; but we can give a direct speech: \"כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה: קדושים תהיו, כי אני יהוה\". Or incorporate the command.\n\nVoice_russian: Synodal translation.\n\nLet's produce.", "voice_hebrew": "כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה: קְדֹשִׁים תִּהְיוּ, כִּי אֲנִי יְהוָה אֱלֹהֵיכֶם.", "voice_russian": "«Так говорит Господь: Святы будьте, ибо Я Господь Бог ваш».", "metadata": {"book": "Leviticus", "trigger": "unprompted", "behavior_type": "command", "outcome": "unclear", "severity": 1, "situation_id": "Leviticus_21_16"}}
{"situation": "[Leviticus 22:] וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר יְהֹוָ֖ה אֶל־מֹשֶׁ֥ה לֵּאמֹֽר׃", "think": "We need to follow the system instructions. Provide three blocks: analysis block, voice_hebrew block, voice_russian block.\n\nWe must fill in the analysis fields as per template. Let's parse situation:\n\n- Trigger: ביוזמת ה׳ (God initiates)\n- Behavior: ציווי (command)\n- Outcome: התגלות (revelation)\n- Severity: 1/5\n- Addressee: prophet\n\nWe need to fill analysis fields:\n\n1. Триггер: [тип] -> \"ביוזמת ה׳\"\n2. Завет/клятва: [конкретный] -> maybe \"ברית קדושה\" or \"קדושה כמטרה\". Use \"ברית הקדושה\".\n3. Middat HaDin (אלהים, строгость): severity 1-5 -> 1\n4. Middat HaRachamim (YHWH, милосердие): активировать? почему? Since severity low and covenant context is about holiness, maybe mercy activated: \"כן\" because God's command is gentle, not punitive.\n5. Посредник: есть/нет -> no mediator for direct speech to prophet (none). So effect on severity: none.\n6. Юнг (Отец (Власть и закон)): активный архетип? Probably active as Father archetype because it's about law/command.\n7. Боулби (Anxious-Ambivalent): reaction? Since God initiates command, likely anxious-ambivalent: high expectations -> \"reactive punishment\" but severity low so maybe mild anxiety.\n\n8. Решение: баланс חסד/חמה -> outcome: since mercy activated and severity low, outcome is \"God grants holiness to Israel through gentle command\".\n\n9. Адресат: prophet -> format: direct speech (כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה / אֲנִי יְהוָה...).\n\nNow generate blocks.\n\nAnalysis block in Russian.\n\nVoice_hebrew: must be biblical Hebrew, no modern. Provide a short statement: \"כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה אֶל־מֹשֶׁה לֵאמֹר: קְדֹשִׁים תִּהְיוּ כִּי קָדוֹשׁ אֲנִי יְהוָה.\" Might be too long. Use the verse context: \"כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה אֶל־מֹשֶׁה לֵאמֹר: קְדֹשִׁים תִּהְיוּ כִּי קָדוֹשׁ אֲנִי יְהוָה.\" That's fine.\n\nVoice_russian: translation in Synodal style. Provide \"Сказал Господь к Моисею, говоря: Святы будьте, ибо свят Я Господь.\"\n\nMake sure no extra text outside blocks.", "voice_hebrew": "כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה אֶל־מֹשֶׁה לֵאמֹר: קְדֹשִׁים תִּהְיוּ כִּי קָדוֹשׁ אֲנִי יְהוָה.", "voice_russian": "Сказал Господь к Моисею, говоря: Святы будьте, ибо свят Я Господь.", "metadata": {"book": "Leviticus", "trigger": "unprompted", "behavior_type": "command", "outcome": "revelation", "severity": 1, "situation_id": "Leviticus_22_1"}}
{"situation": "[Leviticus 22:] וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר יְהֹוָ֖ה אֶל־מֹשֶׁ֥ה לֵּאמֹֽר׃", "think": "We need to generate three blocks as per system instructions. The situation gives details.\n\nWe must follow the format:\n\n1. Trigger: [type] (we have \"ביוזמת ה׳\")\n2. Covenant/promise: [specific]\n3. Middat HaDin severity 1-5 -> given 2/5\n4. Middat HaRachamim activation? why?\n5. Mediator: yes/no effect on severity\n6. Jung (Father) active archetype? Bowlby reaction attachment? Provide answer.\n7. Resolution: balance chesed/din -> outcome\n8. Addressee: prophet => format direct speech.\n\nWe need to produce three blocks:\n\n- First block: analysis in Russian (the system says \"Триггер: [тип]\" etc). So we give a structured analysis.\n\n- Second block: voice_hebrew: God's direct speech in 1st person, using biblical Hebrew. Must be exactly as per format: start with \"כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה / אֲנִי יְהוָה...\". Provide the verse content? The situation is about Leviticus 22:17, but we need to produce a response from God for this situation.\n\n- Third block: voice_russian: translation in Synodal style.\n\nWe must ensure no extra text outside blocks.\n\nLet's construct analysis:\n\nTrigger: ביוזמת ה׳ (God initiates)\n\nCovenant/promise: קדושה כמטרה: קְדֹשִׁים תִּהְיוּ כִּי קָדוֹשׁ אֲנִי יְהוָה.\n\nMiddat HaDin severity 2/5 (moderate)\n\nMiddat HaRachamim activation? Yes, because God's command is linked to covenant of holiness; He shows mercy by giving instruction rather than immediate punishment. So activated.\n\nMediator: yes (Moses) -> effect on severity: reduces severity from maybe 3 to 2.\n\nJung archetype Father active: yes.\n\nBowlby attachment: Anxious-Ambivalent, so God expects high obedience; reaction is reactive punishment if not obeyed.\n\nResolution: balance chesed/din => outcome: the command ensures holiness while allowing mercy for those who repent.\n\nAddressee: prophet -> direct speech format.\n\nNow produce Hebrew block:\n\nWe need to produce a short statement from God: \"כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה אֶל־מֹשֶׁה: קְדֹשִׁים תִּהְיוּ כִּי קָדוֹשׁ אָנֹכִי, וַאֲנִי יְהוָה הַמְּצַוֶּה עֲלֵיכֶם לִשְׁמֹר מִצְוֹתַי. אִם תִּשְׁמְרוּ, חַסְדִּי יִגְבַּע עֲלֵיכֶם; וְאִם תָּפֵרוּ, דִּינִי יִקַּח אֶת־נַפְשׁוֹתֵיכֶם.\"\n\nMake sure it's biblical Hebrew style.\n\nNow Russian block: translation.\n\nLet's produce final answer.", "voice_hebrew": "כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה אֶל־מֹשֶׁה: קְדֹשִׁים תִּהְיוּ כִּי קָדוֹשׁ אָנֹכִי, וַאֲנִי יְהוָה הַמְּצַוֶּה עֲלֵיכֶם לִשְׁמֹר מִצְוֹתַי. אִם תִּשְׁמְרוּ, חַסְדִּי יִגְבַּע עֲלֵיכֶם; וְאִם תָּפֵרוּ, דִּינִי יִקַּח אֶת־נַפְשׁוֹתֵיכֶם.", "voice_russian": "И сказал Господь к Моисею: «קדשים תהיו, כי קדוש אני, и Я Господь, повелевающий вас соблюдать заповеди Мои. Если будете хранить их, милость Моя будет покрывать вас; если же нарушите, суд Моей строгости возьмет ваши души».", "metadata": {"book": "Leviticus", "trigger": "unprompted", "behavior_type": "command", "outcome": "revelation", "severity": 2, "situation_id": "Leviticus_22_17"}}
{"situation": "[Leviticus 22:] וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר יְהֹוָ֖ה אֶל־מֹשֶׁ֥ה לֵּאמֹֽר׃", "think": "We need to follow the system instructions. Provide three blocks: analysis block in Russian, Hebrew voice block, Russian voice block.\n\nWe have situation details: verse Leviticus 22:26 \"וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר יְהֹוָ֖ה אֶל־מֹשֶׁ֥ה לֵּאמֹֽר׃\" Trigger: ביוזמת ה׳ (God's initiative). Behavior: ציווי (command). Outcome: התגלות (revelation). Severity: 3/5.\n\nAddressee: prophet. So God speaks directly in first person.\n\nWe need to produce analysis block with fields: 1-8 as per system spec.\n\nThen Hebrew voice block: God's direct speech, opening \"כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה\" etc.\n\nThen Russian voice block: translation.\n\nLet's construct analysis:\n\nTrigger: ביוזמת ה׳ | Behavior: ציווי | Outcome: התגלות | Severity: 3/5\nAddressee: prophet\n\nWe need to fill fields:\n\n1. Trigger type: God-initiated (ביוזמת ה').\n2. Covenant specifics: The Leviticus covenant about holiness: \"קדשים תהיו כי קדוש אני יהוה\".\n3. Middat HaDin severity: 3/5.\n4. Middat HaRachamim activation? Possibly because of covenant, but severity moderate; maybe not activated strongly. We can say not fully activated.\n\n5. Mediator: yes (Moses). Effect on severity: reduces it slightly, so maybe severity becomes 2-3? But we have fixed severity 3/5. Might note that mediator softens.\n\n6. Jung archetype: Father (Power and law) active.\n7. Bowlby attachment: Anxious-Ambivalent reaction: high expectations, reactive punishment.\n\n8. Resolution: balance of chesed/din leads to moderate command; outcome is revelation of divine will for holiness.\n\nNow produce Hebrew voice block: God speaking in first person, maybe \"כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה\" and then the command from Leviticus 22:26? Actually verse says \"וידבר יהוה אל משה לאמר\". The content of command is not given; maybe we need to infer. Could be about offering animals without blemish (Lev 22:20-25). But we can give a generic statement: \"קדשים תהיו כי קדוש אני יהוה\". Or \"כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה: צִוֵּיתִי אוֹתְךָ לְשָׁמֹר אֶת־קָדְשִׁי, כִּי קָדוֹשׁ אֲנִי יְהוָה\".\n\nRussian block: translation.\n\nLet's produce final answer.", "voice_hebrew": "כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה: צִוֵּיתִי אוֹתְךָ לִשְׁמֹר אֶת־קָדְשִׁי, כִּי קָדוֹשׁ אֲנִי יְהוָה. הַקְדֵּשׁ אֶת־עַצְמְךָ וְאֶת־כׇּל־אֲשֶׁר לְךָ, כִּי בִּקְדֻשָּׁה תִּהְיוּ. אִם תַּעֲבֹר עַל־מִצְוָתִי, הִנֵּה חֲמָתִי תִּפְגַּע בְּךָ; וְאִם תִּשְׁמֹר אוֹתָהּ, אָז חַסְדִּי יִלְוֶה עִמְּךָ.", "voice_russian": "Так говорит Господь: я повелеваю тебе сохранять святость Моего; ибо свят Я, Господь. Освяти себя и всё, что принадлежит тебе, потому что в святости вы должны быть. Если ты нарушишь Мою заповедь, гнев Моей строгости упадёт на тебя; если же ты соблюдёшь её, милосердие Моего благословения будет с тобой.", "metadata": {"book": "Leviticus", "trigger": "unprompted", "behavior_type": "command", "outcome": "revelation", "severity": 3, "situation_id": "Leviticus_22_26"}}
{"situation": "[Leviticus 23:] וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר יְהֹוָ֖ה אֶל־מֹשֶׁ֥ה לֵּאמֹֽר׃", "think": "We need to follow the system instructions. Provide three blocks: trigger analysis block, Hebrew voice block, Russian voice block.\n\nWe have situation data: Verse Leviticus 23:1. Trigger: ביוזמת ה׳ (God's initiative). Behavior: ציווי (command). Outcome: התגלות (revelation). Severity: 1/5 (low severity). Addressee: individual (so format is divine action, third person). Covenant context: קדושה כמטרה: קְדֹשִׁים תִּהְיוּ כִּי קָדוֹשׁ אֲנִי יְהוָה.\n\nWe need to produce the three blocks as per system spec. The first block is analysis (in Russian). Then Hebrew voice block: must be biblical Hebrew only, no modern Hebrew, and follow format for individual addressee => third person narrative. Then Russian voice block: Synodal style translation.\n\nWe have to incorporate the Middat HaDin severity 1-5? In the system spec they gave steps but not required in output? Probably we need to include analysis of middot etc. The analysis block should contain all steps listed (trigger, covenant, severity, middot, mediator, Jung archetype, Bowlby attachment, resolution). Then Hebrew and Russian blocks.\n\nLet's construct:\n\nAnalysis block: start with \"Триггер: ...\". Provide each step.\n\nHebrew block: Use 3rd person narrative. Possibly: \"וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים אֶת־קוֹלוֹ שֶׁל־מֹשֶׁה וַיְּדַבֵּר אֵלָיו לֵאמֹר: ...\". But need to follow format: \"וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים / וַיְּשַלַּח יְהוָה...\". So we can use \"וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים אֶת־קוֹלוֹ שֶׁל־מֹשֶׁה וַיְּדַבֵּר אֵלָיו לֵאמֹר: כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה ...\". Actually for individual addressee, God speaks directly? The rule says only prophets get direct speech. Individual is not prophet; so we must use divine action description in third person. So maybe: \"וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים אֶת־קוֹלוֹ שֶׁל־מֹשֶׁה וַיְּדַבֵּר אֵלָיו לֵאמֹר: כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה ...\" is still direct speech but to Moses (prophet). The addressee is individual, not necessarily prophet. So we must treat as nation/individual/unclear => third person narrative.\n\nThus Hebrew block: \"וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים אֶת־קוֹלוֹ שֶׁל־מֹשֶׁה וַיְּדַבֵּר אֵלָיו לֵאמֹר: קָדוֹשׁ תִּהְיֶה כִּי קָדוֹשׁ אֲנִי יְהוָה.\" But that is still direct speech. Might be okay if we treat Moses as prophet, but the addressee is individual (Moses). That's a prophet though. The rule says \"Addressee=prophet\" then God speaks directly in 1st person. So if we treat Moses as prophet, we should use direct speech format: \"כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה...\". But the addressee is individual; maybe they intend that it's not a prophet but an individual (like any Israelite). Then we must use third person narrative.\n\nThus Hebrew block: \"וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים אֶת־קוֹלוֹ שֶׁל־מֹשֶׁה וַיְּדַבֵּר אֵלָיו לֵאמֹר: קָדוֹשׁ תִּהְיֶה כִּי קָדוֹשׁ אֲנִי יְהוָה.\"\n\nBut that still includes direct speech. Might be okay if we treat it as prophet but they said addressee=individual, not prophet.\n\nMaybe we can interpret \"individual\" as a generic person (not Moses). Then the verse is about God speaking to Moses, but the situation says addressee: individual. That's contradictory. Possibly they want us to treat it as individual, so we must produce third-person narrative: \"וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים וַיְּדַבֵּר אֶת־מֹשֶׁה לֵאמֹר: קָדוֹשׁ תִּהְיֶה כִּי קָדוֹשׁ אֲנִי יְהוָה.\" That's still direct speech but to Moses (prophet). Hmm.\n\nMaybe we can treat it as \"individual\" meaning the individual Israelite, and God speaks through prophetic word that applies to them. In Tanakh, when God commands individuals, it's often in second person singular: \"אתה תעשה\". That is direct speech to an individual but not a prophet. The rule says only prophets get 1st person; others get third-person narrative. So we must use third-person.\n\nThus Hebrew block: \"וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים וַיְּדַבֵּר אֶת־מֹשֶׁה לֵאמֹר: קָדוֹשׁ תִּהְיֶה כִּי קָדוֹשׁ אֲנִי יְהוָה.\"\n\nNow Russian block: Synodal translation.\n\nLet's produce analysis:\n\nTrigger: ביוזמת ה׳ (God's initiative)\nBehavior: ציווי (command)\nOutcome: התגלות (revelation)\nSeverity: 1/5\nAddressee: individual\n\nCovenant context: קדושה כמטרה: קְדֹשִׁים תִּהְיוּ כִּי קָדוֹשׁ אֲנִי יְהוָה (ויק' יט:ב)\n\nNow analysis steps:\n\n- Middat HaDin severity 1/5 => low severity, mild punishment.\n- Middat HaRachamim activation? Probably yes because covenant of holiness emphasizes mercy. So activate.\n\n- Mediator: none? Possibly Moses as mediator but not required.\n\n- Jung archetype: Father (Power and law) active.\n\n- Bowlby attachment: Anxious-Ambivalent, high expectations => God reacts with mild command.\n\n- Resolution: balance leads to outcome of holiness.\n\nNow produce blocks.\n\nMake sure Hebrew block is exactly biblical Hebrew style. Use no punctuation after verses? Probably okay.\n\nLet's output:\n\n[Block 1] Russian analysis.\n[Block 2] Hebrew voice.\n[Block 3] Russian translation.\n\nProceed.", "voice_hebrew": "וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים אֶת־קוֹלוֹ שֶׁל־מֹשֶׁה וַיְּדַבֵּר אֵלָיו לֵאמֹר: קָדוֹשׁ תִּהְיֶה כִּי קָדוֹשׁ אֲנִי יְהוָה.", "voice_russian": "И слышав Бог голос Моисея, сказал ему: «קדוש תהיה, כי קדוש אני Господь».", "metadata": {"book": "Leviticus", "trigger": "unprompted", "behavior_type": "command", "outcome": "revelation", "severity": 1, "situation_id": "Leviticus_23_1"}}
