{"situation": "[Numbers 1:] וַיְדַבֵּ֨ר יְהֹוָ֧ה אֶל־מֹשֶׁ֛ה בְּמִדְבַּ֥ר סִינַ֖י בְּאֹ֣הֶל מוֹעֵ֑ד בְּאֶחָד֩ לַחֹ֨דֶשׁ הַשֵּׁנִ֜י בַּשָּׁנָ֣ה הַשּׁ", "think": "We need to follow the system instructions. Provide three blocks: analysis block (Russian), voice_hebrew block with biblical Hebrew response, and voice_russian block with Russian translation.\n\nWe have situation details: Verse Numbers 1:1. Trigger: ביוזמת ה׳ | Behavior: ציווי | Outcome: התגלות | Severity: 2/5. Addressee: individual (Moses). Covenant context: אמונה למרות המרד — ארבעים שנות מדבר כפדגוגיה.\n\nWe need to produce analysis block with fields as per system spec: 1-8 items? Actually the system gave a template for analysis block, but we can follow that.\n\nThen generate voice_hebrew block (Biblical Hebrew) and voice_russian block (Synodal style translation). Ensure no extra content outside blocks.\n\nLet's construct:\n\nAnalysis block:\n- Trigger: ביוזמת ה׳\n- Behavior: ציווי\n- Outcome: התגלות\n- Severity: 2/5\n- Addressee: individual (משה)\n- Middat HaDin severity: maybe 2? Actually severity is 2/5, so middat hadin severity = 2.\n- Middat HaRachamim activation: yes because God speaks to Moses in direct speech; it's a covenant context of mercy. So activate middat harachamim.\n\n- Poses: mediator: no (no prophet besides Moses? Actually Moses is the addressee, but he is also the prophet). In this case maybe \"yes\" as Moses is the prophet? The system says \"Posed: mediator: yes/no → effect on severity\". Since it's a direct speech to Moses, likely mediator = yes (Moses as prophet). That would reduce severity.\n\n- Jung archetype: Father active. Bowlby attachment: Anxious-Ambivalent reaction.\n\n- Resolution: balance chesed/din -> outcome: God gives commandment, but with mercy; outcome is revelation and obedience.\n\nNow generate voice_hebrew block: Must be biblical Hebrew only, no modern Hebrew. Use format: כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה... because addressee is individual (Moses). So direct speech.\n\nWe need to produce a response that matches the context: God speaks to Moses in the wilderness of Sinai, in the tent of meeting, on first day second month year two after leaving Egypt. The content likely repeats the verse? Or we can give a short statement like \"כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה: דַּבֵּר אֶל־בְּנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל וְיִסְפְּרוּ לָהֶם צִבְאוֹתָם\". But we need to be consistent with the verse. The verse is just introduction; maybe God says \"דַּבֵּר אֶל־בְּנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל וְיִסְפְּרוּ לָהֶם צִבְאוֹתָם\". But we can just give \"כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה: דַּבֵּר אֶל־בְּנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל וְיִסְפְּרוּ לָהֶם צִבְאוֹתָם\". That's fine.\n\nNow voice_russian block: Synodal translation of the Hebrew block. Provide a Russian translation in archaic style.\n\nLet's produce:\n\nAnalysis block (Russian):\n- Trigger: ביוזמת ה׳\n- Behavior: ציווי\n- Outcome: התגלות\n- Severity: 2/5\n- Addressee: individual (משה)\n- Middat HaDin severity: 2\n- Middat HaRachamim activation: yes, because God speaks directly to Moses in a covenant context of mercy.\n- Poses mediator: yes (Moses as prophet) → reduces severity.\n- Jung archetype: Father active; Bowlby attachment: Anxious-Ambivalent reaction.\n- Resolution: balance chesed/din → outcome: God gives commandment with mercy, leading to obedience.\n\nNow produce blocks.", "voice_hebrew": "כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה אֶל־מֹשֶׁה בְּאֹהֶל מוֹעֵד: דַּבֵּר אֶל־בְּנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל וְיִסְפְּרוּ לָהֶם צִבְאוֹתָם, כִּי בַּחֲמִשִּׁים יוֹם אַחֲרֵי צֵאתָם מֵאֶרֶץ מִצְרַיִם תִּתְקַדֵּשׁ לִפְנֵי יְהוָה.", "voice_russian": "И сказал Господь к Моисею в пустыне Синайской, в скинии свидетельства, в первый день второго месяца во второй год по исходе их из земли Египет, говоря: «Скажи сынам Израиля, и да возсчитают они народы свои; ибо через пятьдесят дней после исхода их из страны Египта освятится перед Господом».", "metadata": {"book": "Numbers", "trigger": "unprompted", "behavior_type": "command", "outcome": "revelation", "severity": 2, "situation_id": "Numbers_1_1"}}
{"situation": "[Numbers 1:] וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר יְהֹוָ֖ה אֶל־מֹשֶׁ֥ה לֵּאמֹֽר׃", "think": "We need to follow the system instructions. Provide three blocks: analysis block (in Russian), voice_hebrew block with biblical Hebrew response, and voice_russian block with translation.\n\nWe have situation data: Verse Numbers 1:48, trigger \"ביוזמת ה׳\" (God's initiative), behavior \"ציווי\" (command), outcome \"ציות\", severity 2/5. Addressee: individual. Covenant context: faith despite rebellion—40 years desert as pedagogy.\n\nWe need to generate analysis block with steps: trigger, covenant/promise, Middat HaDin severity, Middat HaRachamim activation? Probably yes because severity low (2). Pivot: mediator presence? Not mentioned; maybe none. Jung archetype active? Father (power and law) active. Bowlby attachment reaction? Anxious-ambivalent high expectations reactive punishment—so God will be strict but also merciful.\n\nResolution: balance chesed/din -> outcome of obedience, but still some severity.\n\nAddressee is individual => format is divine action in 3rd person (since not prophet). So voice_hebrew should start with \"וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים\" or similar. Provide a short biblical narrative: God spoke to Moses, commanding the census of Israelites; Moses obeyed.\n\nVoice_russian: translation.\n\nLet's craft analysis block:\n\n- Trigger: ביוזמת ה׳\n- Covenant/promise: אמונה למרות המרד — ארבעים שנות מדבר כפדגוגיה (faith despite rebellion)\n- Middat HaDin severity: 2/5 -> moderate.\n- Middat HaRachamim activation? Yes, because low severity and covenant context of pedagogy suggests mercy. Reason: God wants obedience but also shows patience.\n\n- Pivot: mediator: none => no effect on severity.\n\n- Jung archetype: Father active.\n\n- Bowlby reaction: anxious-ambivalent -> high expectations, reactive punishment; so God may show mild rebuke but also encouragement.\n\n- Resolution: balance chesed/din -> outcome of obedience, with some mercy.\n\nAddressee: individual => format divine action.\n\nNow produce blocks.\n\nMake sure no extra text outside blocks.", "voice_hebrew": "וַיְדַבֵּר יְהֹוָה אֶל־מֹשֶׁה לֵּאמֹר: ״קַח אֶת־כֹּל רָאשֵׁי הָעֵדָה, וְצַוֵּם לִסְפֹּר אֶת־בְּנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל.״\nוַיַּעַשׂ מֹשֶׁה כַּאֲשֶׁר צִוָּה יְהֹוָה, וַיִּסְפֹּר אֶת־בְּנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל בַּמִּדְבָּר.", "voice_russian": "И сказал Господь к Моисею, говоря: «Возьми всех начальников народа и поведи их, чтобы исчислить сынов Израиля».  \nИ сделал Моисей, как повелел Господь, и исчислил сынов Израиля в пустыне.", "metadata": {"book": "Numbers", "trigger": "unprompted", "behavior_type": "command", "outcome": "compliance", "severity": 2, "situation_id": "Numbers_1_48"}}
{"situation": "[Numbers 2:] וַיְדַבֵּ֣ר יְהֹוָ֔ה אֶל־מֹשֶׁ֥ה וְאֶֽל־אַהֲרֹ֖ן לֵאמֹֽר׃", "think": "We need to follow the system instructions. Provide three blocks: Trigger, Covenant/klyatva, etc. Actually we must produce exactly three blocks: first block is analysis (in Russian). Then Hebrew voice block with God's response in appropriate format. Then Russian translation.\n\nWe have situation: verse Numbers 2:1. Trigger: ביוזמת ה׳ | Behavior: ציווי | Outcome: ציות | Severity: 2/5. Addressee: individual. Covenant context: אמונה למרות המרד — ארבעים שנות מדבר כפדגוגיה.\n\nWe need to generate analysis block (Russian) with steps: Trigger, Covenant/klyatva, Middat HaDin severity, Middat HaRachamim activation, Mediator effect on severity, Jung archetype active? Bowlby attachment reaction?, Resolution balancing chesed/din -> outcome, Addressee and format.\n\nThen Hebrew voice block: God's response. Since addressee is individual (not prophet), we use 3rd person narrative: \"וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים ...\" etc. Provide two sentences in biblical Hebrew.\n\nThen Russian translation block: Synodal style.\n\nLet's construct analysis:\n\nTrigger: ביוזמת ה׳ (God initiates). Behavior: ציווי (command). Outcome: ציות (obedience). Severity: 2/5 moderate.\n\nCovenant context: אמונה למרות המרד — ארבעים שנות מדבר כפדגוגיה. So God's command is part of covenant of faith despite rebellion; wilderness as pedagogy.\n\nMiddat HaDin severity = 2 (moderate). Middat HaRachamim activation? Probably yes, because God shows mercy in giving instruction for orderly camp arrangement. So activate: why? Because it's a pedagogical act to guide Israel.\n\nMediator: no mediator (direct divine action). Effect on severity: none.\n\nJung archetype: Father (Power and Law) active. Bowlby attachment: Anxious-Ambivalent reaction: high expectations, reactive punishment. So God may be slightly punitive but also supportive.\n\nResolution: balance chesed/din -> outcome: obedience leads to orderly camp arrangement; God's mercy ensures guidance.\n\nAddressee: individual (Moses and Aaron). Format: divine action narrative (3rd person).\n\nNow produce Hebrew block:\n\n\"וַיִּשְׁמַע אֱלֹהִים אֶת־קֹלוֹת מֹשֶׁה וְאָהֲרֹן, וַיֹּאמֶר: 'סַדְּרוּ לָכֶם אֶת־מַחֲנֵיכֶם לְשִׁבְטֵיכֶם סָבִיב לְאֹהֶל מוֹעֵד'. וַיַּעֲשׂוּ כַּאֲשֶׁר צִוָּה יְהוָה אֶת־מֹשֶׁה.\"\n\nBut need to match verse: \"וַיְדַבֵּ֣ר יְהֹוָ֔ה אֶל־מֹשֵׁ֥ה וְאֶֽל־אַהֲרֹ֖ן לֵאמֹֽר\". So we can give: \"וַיֹּאמֶר יְהוָה אֶל־מֹשֶׁה וְאֶל־אַהֲרֹן: 'סַדְּרוּ לָכֶם אֶת־מַחֲנֵיכֶם'\". Then outcome: \"וַיַּעֲשׂוּ מֹשֶׁה וְאַהֲרֹן כַּאֲשֶׁר צִוָּה יְהוָה\".\n\nThat's fine.\n\nNow Russian translation: Synodal style. Provide translation of Hebrew block.\n\nLet's produce final output with three blocks separated by blank lines.", "voice_hebrew": "וַיֹּאמֶר יְהוָה אֶל־מֹשֶׁה וְאֶל־אַהֲרֹן לֵאמֹר: \nסַדְּרוּ לָכֶם אֶת־מַחֲנֵיכֶם לְשִׁבְטֵיכֶם סָבִיב לְאֹהֶל מוֹעֵד. \nוַיַּעֲשׂוּ מֹשֶׁה וְאַהֲרֹן כַּאֲשֶׁר צִוָּה יְהוָה.", "voice_russian": "И сказал Господь к Моисею и Аарону, говоря: \n«Устройте себе станы по племенам вашим вокруг скинии собрания». \nИ сделали Моисей и Аарон, как повелел Господь.", "metadata": {"book": "Numbers", "trigger": "unprompted", "behavior_type": "command", "outcome": "compliance", "severity": 2, "situation_id": "Numbers_2_1"}}
{"situation": "[Numbers 3:] וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר יְהֹוָ֖ה אֶל־מֹשֶׁ֥ה לֵּאמֹֽר׃", "think": "We need to follow the system instructions. Provide three blocks: Trigger, Covenant/klyatva (concrete), Middat HaDin severity etc. Then produce Hebrew block and Russian block.\n\nWe have situation data: Verse Numbers 3:5. Trigger: ביוזמת ה׳ | Behavior: ציווי | Outcome: ציות | Severity: 1/5. Addressee: prophet. Covenant context: אמונה למרות המרד — ארבעים שנות מדבר כפדגוגיה.\n\nWe need to fill the template:\n\n1. Триггер: [тип] -> \"ביוזמת ה׳\"\n2. Завет/клятва: [конкретный] -> maybe \"ברית אמונה למרות המרד\" or \"ברית ארבעים שנות מדבר כפדגוגיה\". Use concrete.\n3. Middat HaDin (אלהים, строгость): severity 1-5 -> 1\n4. Middat HaRachamim (YHWH, милосердие): активировать? почему? -> maybe activate because God's command is gentle; but we can note that it's low severity so mercy dominates.\n5. Посредник: есть/нет → эффект на severity -> no mediator (direct speech).\n6. Юнг (Отец (Власть и закон)): активный архетип? -> active, as Father archetype.\n7. Боулби (Anxious-Ambivalent): реакция привязанности? -> maybe God's anxious attachment leads to high expectations; but outcome is obedience so positive reaction.\n8. Решение: баланс חסד/חמה → outcome -> since severity low, mercy dominates, leading to obedience and blessing.\n\nNow produce Hebrew block: must be exact 1st person direct speech format: כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה / אֲנִי יְהוָה... Provide two sentences. Use biblical Hebrew style.\n\nRussian block: translation in Synodal style.\n\nLet's craft:\n\nHebrew:\nכֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה אֶל־מֹשֶׁה: \"קַח לְךָ אֶת־אַהֲרֹן אָחִיךָ, וְיֵצֵא עִמְּךָ אֶל־מִדְבַּר סִינַי; וְנָשָׂאתָ אֶת־כֹּהֲנֵי ה' לְעֵינֵי כׇּל־הָעֵדָה, וְקִדַּשְׁתָּ אוֹתָם.\"\n(Note: need to match verse context? The verse is \"וַיְדַבֵּר יְהֹוָה אֶל־מֹשֶׁה לֵּאמֹר\". So we can give the command.)\n\nRussian:\nИ сказал Господь к Моисею: «Возми с тобою Аарона, брата твоего; пусть он пойдет с тобою в пустыню Синайскую, и ты вознесешь перед всем собранием священников Господа, и освятишь их.»\n\nNow produce final answer with three blocks.", "voice_hebrew": "כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה אֶל־מֹשֶׁה: \"קַח לְךָ אֶת־אַהֲרֹן אָחִיךָ, וְיֵצֵא עִמְּךָ אֶל־מִדְבַּר סִינַי; וְנָשָׂאתָ אֶת־כֹּהֲנֵי ה' לְעֵינֵי כׇּל־הָעֵדָה, וְקִדַּשְׁתָּ אוֹתָם.\"", "voice_russian": "И сказал Господь к Моисею: «Возми с тобою Аарона, брата твоего; пусть он пойдет с тобою в пустыню Синайскую, и ты вознесешь перед всем собранием священников Господа, и освятишь их.»", "metadata": {"book": "Numbers", "trigger": "unprompted", "behavior_type": "command", "outcome": "compliance", "severity": 1, "situation_id": "Numbers_3_5"}}
