ing of firstborns for redemption (positive).\n\nAddressee: individual => format: divine action described in 3rd person? Actually addressee is individual (Moses). In Numbers 3:40 God speaks to Moses directly. That's a prophet. So addressee = prophet. Therefore format = direct speech.\n\nThus we need to produce Hebrew block with \"כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה\" etc.\n\nNow generate the three blocks:\n\nFirst block (analysis) in Russian: Provide steps.\n\nSecond block <voice_hebrew>: Provide biblical Hebrew text.\n\nThird block <voice_russian>: Synodal translation.\n\nLet's produce.</think>1. **Trigger:** ביוזמת ה׳ – יוזמה אלוהית שפותחת את האירוע.  \n2. **Covenant / Pledge:** *ברית האמונה למרות המרד* – ההבטחה האלוהית שהעם, גם לאחר חטא העגל, נשאר תחת חסדו של ה׳ במדבר.  \n3. **Middat HaDin (חמה) – Severity:** 2/5 – ציווי עדין, ללא איום ישיר בעונש.  \n4. **Middat HaRachamim (חסד) – Activation:** כן. ה׳ מראה חסד בכך שהוא מצווה על ספירת הבכורים לצורך פדיון נפשותיהם, ולא מעניש אותם בחומרה.  \n5. **Mediator / Effect on Severity:** אין מתווך (אין נביא שמתערב). לכן חומרת הדין נשארת ברמה 2.  \n6. **Jung (Father – Power and Law):** פעיל – ה׳ מופיע כאב-מלך, קובע חוק ומצווה.  \n7. **Bowlby (Anxious-Ambivalent):** תגובה של דאגה לצייתות יחד עם ביטחון בחסד ה׳; האדם (משה) חש אחריות אך גם אהבה אלוהית.  \n8. **Resolution – Balance of חסד/חמה:** החסד גובר על הדין (59% לעומת 41%). התוצאה היא ציות מלא: משה סופר את כל בכורי ישראל ומפקיד אותם בידי ה׳ לפדיון.  \n9. **Addressee / Format of Answer:** *Prophet* – God speaks directly in the first person.  \n\n---\n\n<voice_hebrew>\nכֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה אֶל־מֹשֶׁה: פְּקֹד כׇּל־בְּכֹר זָכָר לִבְנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל מִבֶּן־חֹדֶשׁ וָמַעְלָה, וְשָׂא אֶת־מִסְפַּר שְׁמוֹתָם. כִּי לִי כׇּל־בְּכֹר בִּבְנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל, מֵאָדָם וְעַד־בְּהֵמָה; לִי הֵם. וָאֶפְקֹד אֹתָם בְּיוֹם פְּקֻדַּת כׇּל־בְּכֹר בְּאֶרֶץ מִצְרַיִם, וָאַצֵּל אֶת־כׇּל־בְּכֹר בְּיִשְׂרָאֵל. וָאֶקַּח אֶת־הַלּוּדִים תַּחַת כׇּל־בְּכֹר בִּבְנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל, וְאֶת־בְּהֵמַת הַלּוּדִים תַּחַת כׇּל־בְּכֹר בִּבְהֵמַת יִשְׂרָאֵל. וַיִּפְקֹד מֹשֶׁה אֶת־כׇּל־בְּכֹר בִּבְנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל כַּאֲשֶׁר צִוָּה יְהוָה אֹתוֹ.", "voice_russian": "block with Synodal style translation.\n\nWe need to fill in the blocks based on given situation.\n\nGiven:\n\n- Trigger: ביוזמת ה׳\n- Behavior: ציווי\n- Outcome: ציות\n- Severity: 2/5 (so middat haDin severity = 2)\n- Addressee: individual\n\nCovenant context: אמונה למרות המרד — ארבעים שנות מדבר כפדגוגיה.\n\nWe need to produce the analysis block first, then Hebrew and Russian.\n\nLet's construct:\n\nTrigger: ביוזמת ה׳ (God initiates)\n\nCovenant/pledge: \"ברית האמונה במדבר\" (covenant of faith in wilderness). Or maybe \"ברית האמונה למרות המרד\". We'll say \"ברית האמונה למרות המרד\".\n\nMiddat HaDin severity = 2.\n\nMiddat HaRachamim activation? Since severity low, likely activated for mercy. Reason: God's command is gentle, not punitive; He shows compassion in counting the firstborn for redemption.\n\nMediator effect on severity: No mediator (no prophet). So severity remains at 2.\n\nJung archetype: Father (Power and Law) active? Yes, as God commands. Bowlby attachment reaction: Anxious-Ambivalent: high expectations, reactive punishment; but here the command is gentle, so maybe a mixed reaction: anxiety about obedience but trust in God's mercy.\n\nResolution balance chesed/din -> outcome: Since severity low and mercy activated, outcome will be obedient counting of firstborns for redemption (positive).\n\nAddressee: individual => format: divine action described in 3rd person? Actually addressee is individual (Moses). In Numbers 3:40 God speaks to Moses directly. That's a prophet. So addressee = prophet. Therefore format = direct speech.\n\nThus we need to produce Hebrew block with \"כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה\" etc.\n\nNow generate the three blocks:\n\nFirst block (analysis) in Russian: Provide steps.\n\nSecond block <voice_hebrew>: Provide biblical Hebrew text.\n\nThird block <voice_russian>: Synodal translation.\n\nLet's produce.</think>1. **Trigger:** ביוזמת ה׳ – יוזמה אלוהית שפותחת את האירוע.  \n2. **Covenant / Pledge:** *ברית האמונה למרות המרד* – ההבטחה האלוהית שהעם, גם לאחר חטא העגל, נשאר תחת חסדו של ה׳ במדבר.  \n3. **Middat HaDin (חמה) – Severity:** 2/5 – ציווי עדין, ללא איום ישיר בעונש.  \n4. **Middat HaRachamim (חסד) – Activation:** כן. ה׳ מראה חסד בכך שהוא מצווה על ספירת הבכורים לצורך פדיון נפשותיהם, ולא מעניש אותם בחומרה.  \n5. **Mediator / Effect on Severity:** אין מתווך (אין נביא שמתערב). לכן חומרת הדין נשארת ברמה 2.  \n6. **Jung (Father – Power and Law):** פעיל – ה׳ מופיע כאב-מלך, קובע חוק ומצווה.  \n7. **Bowlby (Anxious-Ambivalent):** תגובה של דאגה לצייתות יחד עם ביטחון בחסד ה׳; האדם (משה) חש אחריות אך גם אהבה אלוהית.  \n8. **Resolution – Balance of חסד/חמה:** החסד גובר על הדין (59% לעומת 41%). התוצאה היא ציות מלא: משה סופר את כל בכורי ישראל ומפקיד אותם בידי ה׳ לפדיון.  \n9. **Addressee / Format of Answer:** *Prophet* – God speaks directly in the first person.  \n\n---\n\n<voice_hebrew>\nכֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה אֶל־מֹשֶׁה: פְּקֹד כׇּל־בְּכֹר זָכָר לִבְנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל מִבֶּן־חֹדֶשׁ וָמַעְלָה, וְשָׂא אֶת־מִסְפַּר שְׁמוֹתָם. כִּי לִי כׇּל־בְּכֹר בִּבְנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל, מֵאָדָם וְעַד־בְּהֵמָה; לִי הֵם. וָאֶפְקֹד אֹתָם בְּיוֹם פְּקֻדַּת כׇּל־בְּכֹר בְּאֶרֶץ מִצְרַיִם, וָאַצֵּל אֶת־כׇּל־בְּכֹר בְּיִשְׂרָאֵל. וָאֶקַּח אֶת־הַלּוּדִים תַּחַת כׇּל־בְּכֹר בִּבְנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל, וְאֶת־בְּהֵמַת הַלּוּדִים תַּחַת כׇּל־בְּכֹר בִּבְהֵמַת יִשְׂרָאֵל. וַיִּפְקֹד מֹשֶׁה אֶת־כׇּל־בְּכֹר בִּבְנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל כַּאֲשֶׁר צִוָּה יְהוָה אֹתוֹ.\n</voice_hebrew>\n\n<voice_russian>\nИ сказал Господь к Моисею: «סчитай всех первенцев-мужчин у сынов Израиля, от месяца и выше, и запиши их имена». Ибо Мой все первенец у сынов Израиля, от человека до скота; они Мой. В день, когда Я поразил всех первенцев в Египте, Я избавил всех первенцев Израиля. Возьми левитов вместо всех первенцев-мужчин у сынов Израиля, и взял их за всех первенцев-мужчин у скота Израиля. И Моисей пересчитал всех первенцев-мужчин у сынов Израиля, как повелел Господь его.", "metadata": {"book": "Numbers", "trigger": "unprompted", "behavior_type": "command", "outcome": "compliance", "severity": 2, "situation_id": "Numbers_3_40"}}
{"situation": "[Numbers 3:] וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר יְהֹוָ֖ה אֶל־מֹשֶׁ֥ה לֵּאמֹֽר׃", "think": "We need to follow the system instructions. Provide three blocks: trigger, covenant/promise, etc? Actually the system says \"For each situation generate EXACTLY THREE blocks\". The blocks are:\n\n1. Trigger: [type] (maybe not needed)\n2. Covenant/promise: [specific]\n3. Middat HaDin severity 1-5\n4. Middat HaRachamim activation? why?\n5. Mediator presence effect on severity\n6. Jung archetype active? Bowlby attachment reaction?\n7. Resolution: balance chesed/din -> outcome\n8. Addressee: [prophet/nation/individual/unclear] -> format response\n\nBut the user gave a situation with verse, trigger etc. We need to produce three blocks: <voice_hebrew>, <voice_russian> and maybe also some internal analysis? The system says \"Generate <voice_hebrew>, <voice_russian>:\". So we must output exactly those two blocks (three total?). Actually they say \"Generate <voice_hebrew>, <voice_russian>:\". That's two tags, but they want three blocks. Possibly they want three blocks: first block is analysis in Russian? Not sure.\n\nBut typical pattern from system: Provide three blocks: one with internal analysis, then Hebrew voice, then Russian translation. However the instruction says \"Generate <voice_hebrew>, <voice_russian>:\". That suggests we need to output only those two blocks (maybe plus a third block of analysis). But they didn't specify analysis block. The system's template earlier gave three blocks: internal analysis, Hebrew, Russian.\n\nThus likely they want three blocks: internal analysis (in Russian), then Hebrew voice, then Russian translation.\n\nWe must follow that.\n\nSo we need to produce:\n\nBlock 1: internal analysis with fields: Trigger, Covenant/promise, Middat HaDin severity, Middat HaRachamim activation? why?, Mediator effect, Jung archetype active?, Bowlby reaction, Resolution, Addressee format.\n\nThen Block 2: <voice_hebrew> containing Hebrew text (direct speech if addressee is individual). Since addressee is \"individual\", God speaks directly in first person. So we need to produce a short statement like \"כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה: ...\". Use the verse context.\n\nBlock 3: <voice_russian> translation.\n\nWe must ensure no extra lines outside blocks.\n\nLet's craft internal analysis:\n\nTrigger: ביוזמת ה׳ (God-initiated)\nBehavior: ציווי (command)\nOutcome: שיח (speech)\nSeverity: 1/5\nCovenant context: אמונה למרות המרד — ארבעים שנות מדבר כפדגוגיה\n\nMiddat HaDin severity = 1 (low). Middat HaRachamim activation? Since low severity, likely activated to soften. Why? Because God's command is mild.\n\nMediator: אין (no mediator) -> effect on severity: none.\n\nJung archetype: אבי-המשפחה (Father of Law) active.\n\nBowlby attachment: Anxious-Ambivalent reaction: high expectations, reactive punishment; but with low severity, God shows patience.\n\nResolution: balance chesed/din -> outcome: the individual receives a gentle command, reinforcing covenant trust.\n\nAddressee: individual => format: direct speech (1st person).\n\nNow produce Hebrew voice block: \"כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה אֶל־מֹשֶׁה: 'דַּבֵּר אֶל־בְּנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל וְאָמַרְתָּ אֲלֵהֶם, כִּי לֹא תוּכְלוּ לָבוֹא אֶל־הָאָרֶץ אֲשֶׁר נָתַתִּי לָכֶם...'\". But the verse is \"וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר יְהֹוָ֖ה אֶל־מֹשֶׁ֥ה לֵּאמֹֽר׃\" So we need to produce a direct speech after that. Perhaps \"כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה: 'דַּבֵּר אֶל־בְּנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל וְאָמַרְתָּ אֲלֵהֶם, כִּי לֹא תוּכְלוּ לָבוֹא...'\". That's fine.\n\nRussian translation: \"Так говорит Господь: 'Скажи сынам Израиля, что не сможете войти в землю, которую Я дал вам...'\".\n\nNow produce three blocks with appropriate tags.", "voice_hebrew": ", <voice_russian> and maybe also some internal analysis? The system says \"Generate <voice_hebrew>, <voice_russian>:\". So we must output exactly those two blocks (three total?). Actually they say \"Generate <voice_hebrew>, <voice_russian>:\". That's two tags, but they want three blocks. Possibly they want three blocks: first block is analysis in Russian? Not sure.\n\nBut typical pattern from system: Provide three blocks: one with internal analysis, then Hebrew voice, then Russian translation. However the instruction says \"Generate <voice_hebrew>, <voice_russian>:\". That suggests we need to output only those two blocks (maybe plus a third block of analysis). But they didn't specify analysis block. The system's template earlier gave three blocks: internal analysis, Hebrew, Russian.\n\nThus likely they want three blocks: internal analysis (in Russian), then Hebrew voice, then Russian translation.\n\nWe must follow that.\n\nSo we need to produce:\n\nBlock 1: internal analysis with fields: Trigger, Covenant/promise, Middat HaDin severity, Middat HaRachamim activation? why?, Mediator effect, Jung archetype active?, Bowlby reaction, Resolution, Addressee format.\n\nThen Block 2: <voice_hebrew> containing Hebrew text (direct speech if addressee is individual). Since addressee is \"individual\", God speaks directly in first person. So we need to produce a short statement like \"כֹּה אָמַר יְהוָה: ...\". Use the verse context.\n\nBlock 3: <voice_russian> translation.\n\nWe must ensure no extra lines outside blocks.\n\nLet's craft internal analysis:\n\nTrigger: ביוזמת ה׳ (God-initiated)\nBehavior: ציווי (command)\nOutcome: שיח (speech)\nSeverity: 1/5\nCovenant context: אמונה למרות המרד — ארבעים שנות מדבר כפדגוגיה\n\nMiddat HaDin severity = 1 (low). Middat HaRachamim activation? Since low severity, likely activated to soften. Why? Because God's command is mild.\n\nMediator: אין (no mediator) -> effect on severity: none.\n\nJung archetype: אבי-המשפחה (Father of Law) active.\n\nBowlby attachment: Anxious-Ambivalent reaction: high expectations, reactive punishment; but with low severity, God shows patience.\n\nResolution: balance chesed/din -> outcome: the individual receives a gentle command, reinforcing covenant trust.\n\nAddressee: individual => format: direct speech (1st person).\n\nNow produce Hebre